issing from Rust `.so`** | **{len(miss)}** |\n| extra symbols in Rust `.so` not in C  | {len(extra)} |\n| undefined (imported) non-libc symbols in Rust `.so` | 0 (only libc/`__gmon_start__`/`_Unwind_*`) |\n\n`nm -D -u target/release/libpcre2.so` lists only glibc (`malloc`, `memcpy`,\n`is*`/`to*`, `strlen`, …) plus unwinder/loader symbols — no unresolved PCRE2\nsymbol.\n\n## Defects found and fixed in this phase\n\n1. `src/pcre2_substitute.rs` contained **two** `#[no_mangle] pcre2_substitute_8`\n   definitions; the second was a truncated (unbalanced-brace) partial\n   re-translation that stopped at C `pcre2_substitute.c:1048`. The crate did not\n   compile at all. The truncated duplicate was removed (the first translation is\n   complete through C line 1795).\n2. `_pcre2_ucp_gentype_8` had **29** elements instead of 30 — the final `ucp_Z`\n   (for `ucp_Zs`, index 29) was missing. `ucp_gentype[chartype]` is indexed with\n   `chartype` up to `ucp_Zs`, so `\\\\p{{Zs}}`-class code paths read one past the\n   end (Rust: bounds-check abort; C: valid read). Fixed to 30 elements.\n3. `_pcre2_ucd_nocase_ranges_8` had **82** u32 instead of 84 — the\n   `0xffffffff, 0xffffffff` terminator pair was missing, although\n   `_pcre2_ucd_nocase_ranges_size_8 == 82` and\n   `pcre2_compile_class.c:133` returns `ranges + size`, i.e. the terminator is\n   dereferenced. Fixed to 84 elements.\n\nData-object sizes are now identical for every exported data symbol; the byte\n*contents* of every exported data object are additionally compared at runtime by\n`tests/tables_diff.rs` (both `.so`s loaded with `libloading`).\n\n## Symbol table\n\n`T` = text/function, `R` = read-only data, `D`/`B` = data. Sizes in bytes from\n`nm -S`.\n\n| # | symbol | C type | C size | Rust type | Rust size | in Rust `.so` | note |\n|---|--------|--------|--------|-----------|-----------|---------------|------|\n\"\"\"\nopen('SYMBOLS.md','w').write(hdr+\"\\n\".join(lines)+\"\\n\")\nprint(\"missing\",len(miss),\"extra\