{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01NTVmRyW6UNYY7fbYKJzoTD","type":"tool_result","content":"# SYMBOLS.md — exported-symbol parity (C `.so` vs Rust `.so`)\n\nGenerated mechanically by `nm -D -S --defined-only` on\n\n* **C**    `c_src/build/libpcre2.so` — built per `c_src/CMakeLists.txt`\n  (`HAVE_CONFIG_H`, `PCRE2_CODE_UNIT_WIDTH=8`, `SUPPORT_UNICODE`, no JIT support).\n* **Rust** `target/release/libpcre2.so` — `cargo build --release`\n  (crate-type `cdylib`; `Cargo.toml` declares **no `[features]`**, so the default\n  build is the *only* configuration — see `CONFIGS.md` §0).\n\n## Result\n\n| | count |\n|---|---|\n| dynamic symbols exported by C `.so`   | 143 |\n| dynamic symbols exported by Rust `.so`| 143 |\n| **C symbols missing from Rust `.so`** | **0** |\n| extra symbols in Rust `.so` not in C  | 0 |\n| undefined (imported) non-libc symbols in Rust `.so` | 0 (only libc/`__gmon_start__`/`_Unwind_*`) |\n\n`nm -D -u target/release/libpcre2.so` lists only glibc (`malloc`, `memcpy`,\n`is*`/`to*`, `strlen`, …) plus unwinder/loader symbols — no unresolved PCRE2\nsymbol.\n\n## Defects found and fixed in this phase\n\n1. `src/pcre2_substitute.rs` contained **two** `#[no_mangle] pcre2_substitute_8`\n   definitions; the second was a truncated (unbalanced-brace) partial\n   re-translation that stopped at C `pcre2_substitute.c:1048`. The crate did not\n   compile at all. The truncated duplicate was removed (the first translation is\n   complete through C line 1795).\n2. `_pcre2_ucp_gentype_8` had **29** elements instead of 30 — the final `ucp_Z`\n   (for `ucp_Zs`, index 29) was missing. `ucp_gentype[chartype]` is indexed with\n   `chartype` up to `ucp_Zs`, so `\\p{Zs}`-class code paths read one past the\n   end (Rust: bounds-check abort; C: valid read). Fixed to 30 elements.\n3. `_pcre2_ucd_nocase_ranges_8` had **82** u32 instead of 84 — the\n   `0xffffffff, 0xffffffff` terminator pair was missing, although\n   `_pcre2_ucd_nocase_ranges_size_8 == 82` and\n   `pcre2_compile_class.c:133` returns `ranges + size`, i.e. the terminator is\n   dereferenced. Fixed to 84 elements.\n\nData-object sizes are now identical for every exported data symbol; the byte\n*contents* of every exported data object are additionally compared at runtime by\n`tests/tables_diff.rs` (both `.so`s loaded with `libloading`).\n\n## Symbol table\n\n`T` = text/function, `R` = read-only data, `D`/`B` = data. Sizes in bytes from\n`nm -S`.\n\n| # | symbol | C type | C size | Rust type | Rust size | in Rust `.so` | note |\n|---|--------|--------|--------|-----------|-----------|---------------|------|\n| 1 | `_pcre2_OP_lengths_8` | R | 173 | R | 173 | YES | data size MATCHES |\n| 2 | `_pcre2_auto_possessify_8` | T | 1332 | T | 831 | YES | (function: byte size differs by codegen, not compared) |\n| 3 | `_pcre2_callout_end_delims_8` | R | 36 | R | 36 | YES | data size MATCHES |\n| 4 | `_pcre2_callout_start_delims_8` | R | 36 | R | 36 | YES | data size MATCHES |\n| 5 | `_pcre2_check_escape_8` | T | 4855 | T | 4120 | YES | (function: byte size differs by codegen, not compared) |\n| 6 | `_pcre2_ckd_smul_8` | T | 51 | T | 16 | YES | (function: byte size differs by codegen, not compared) |\n| 7 | `_pcre2_compile_add_name_to_table8` | T | 534 | T | 663 | YES | (function: byte size differs by codegen, not compared) |\n| 8 | `_pcre2_compile_class_nested_8` | T | 1614 | T | 707 | YES | (function: byte size differs by codegen, not compared) |\n| 9 | `_pcre2_compile_class_not_nested_8` | T | 4762 | T | 7241 | YES | (function: byte size differs by codegen, not compared) |\n| 10 | `_pcre2_compile_find_dupname_details8` | T | 461 | T | 357 | YES | (function: byte size differs by codegen, not compared) |\n| 11 | `_pcre2_compile_find_named_group8` | T | 190 | T | 135 | YES | (function: byte size differs by codegen, not compared) |\n| 12 | `_pcre2_compile_get_hash_from_name8` | T | 62 | T | 18 | YES | (function: byte size differs by codegen, not co