{"type":"system","subtype":"task_started","task_id":"ad518572570bd0599","tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01SHw5jQsqSSkKA2bdWsG5e3","description":"Analyze match.c branching","subagent_type":"Explore","task_type":"local_agent","prompt":"Read-only analysis. Do NOT modify any file. Do not write any files.\n\nBase dir: /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-GdDnk6/translated_rust/c_src\n\nAnalyze `src/pcre2_match.c`, `src/pcre2_match_next.c`, `src/pcre2_match_data.c`, `src/pcre2_study.c` (PCRE2 10.48, 8-bit, SUPPORT_UNICODE, no JIT).\n\nI need a mechanical inventory for building a differential test suite. Report:\n\n(A) In `pcre2_match()`: every branch on match options (PCRE2_NOTBOL, NOTEOL, NOTEMPTY, NOTEMPTY_ATSTART, PARTIAL_SOFT, PARTIAL_HARD, ANCHORED, ENDANCHORED, NO_UTF_CHECK, NO_JIT, COPY_MATCHED_SUBJECT, DISABLE_RECURSELOOP_CHECK) with line numbers and what each changes. Also branches on compile-time options seen at match time (PCRE2_FIRSTLINE, PCRE2_USE_OFFSET_LIMIT, PCRE2_MATCH_INVALID_UTF, PCRE2_DOLLAR_ENDONLY, PCRE2_ALT_CIRCUMFLEX, PCRE2_NO_START_OPTIMIZE, PCRE2_MATCH_UNSET_BACKREF, PCRE2_UTF, PCRE2_UCP).\n\n(B) The start-of-match optimisation logic: first-code-unit (FIRSTCODEUNIT / firstcu / firstcuflags), required last code unit (reqcu), start bitmap (start_bitmap / FIRSTBITMAP), anchored, FIRSTLINE, minlength check, \"start_match past end\" checks, offset_limit handling, and the `PCRE2_OPTIMIZATION_*` / `optimization_flags` gating (which optimisation each of PCRE2_AUTO_POSSESS, PCRE2_DOTSTAR_ANCHOR, PCRE2_START_OPTIMIZE controls, and where the flags are consulted). Give minimal pattern + subject shapes that hit each distinct branch, including the case where the optimisation is disabled.\n\n(C) Limit handling: match_limit, depth_limit, heap_limit — exact variables, where they are decremented/checked, the error codes returned, the heapframe growth path (`match_data->heapframes`, frame_size, `PCRE2_ERROR_HEAPLIMIT`, `PCRE2_ERROR_NOMEMORY`), and how a test reaches each (pattern + limit value). Also the recursion-loop check (`PCRE2_ERROR_RECURSELOOP`) and how PCRE2_DISABLE_RECURSELOOP_CHECK changes it.\n\n(D) ovector handling: oveccount 0 / 1 / small / large, how many pairs get filled, `match_data->rc` / `ovector[]` truncation semantics, `PCRE2_ERROR_PARTIAL` ovector contents, `pcre2_get_startchar`, `pcre2_get_mark`, `match_data->mark`, and `pcre2_match_data_create` vs `_from_pattern` differences (line numbers in pcre2_match_data.c). Also `pcre2_get_match_data_size` / `pcre2_get_match_data_heapframes_size`.\n\n(E) `pcre2_next_match()` in pcre2_match_next.c: exact semantics, what inputs it distinguishes (empty match, CRLF newline, UTF), and the option/state combos to cover.\n\n(F) `_pcre2_study()` in pcre2_study.c: exact signature, what it computes (minlength, firstcu, start bitmap), the distinct opcode families it branches on, and what pattern families produce each distinct result (e.g. bitmap built vs not, minlength known vs 0). Also `set_start_bits` / `set_table_bit` behaviours and any recursion/depth limit inside study.\n\n(G) Callout handling in match: `pcre2_callout` struct fields set, callout_block, callout return values (0 / >0 / <0), `PCRE2_ERROR_CALLOUT`, callout with string vs number, `callout_flags` (PCRE2_CALLOUT_STARTMATCH / PCRE2_CALLOUT_BACKTRACK).\n\nBe precise with line numbers. Output as compact structured text, no files.","uuid":"6cf6a06a-b0fc-4e8a-b4e7-a351536bb024","session_id":"aeab5d90-512d-4436-80fd-a67670a151c9"}
