{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01Qy8NQnmNxaEemp4JoUGgTp","type":"tool_result","content":"40\tARISING IN ANY WAY OUT OF THE USE OF THIS SOFTWARE, EVEN IF ADVISED OF THE\n41\tPOSSIBILITY OF SUCH DAMAGE.\n42\t-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n43\t*/\n44\t\n45\t\n46\t/* This file contains tables of Unicode properties that are extracted from\n47\tUnicode data files. See the comments at the start of maint/GenerateUcd.py for\n48\tdetails.\n49\t\n50\tAs well as being part of the PCRE2 library, this file is #included by the\n51\tpcre2test program, which redefines the PRIV macro to change table names from\n52\t_pcre2_xxx to xxxx, thereby avoiding name clashes with the library. At present,\n53\tjust one of these tables is actually needed. When compiling the library, some\n54\theaders are needed. */\n55\t\n56\t\n57\t#ifndef PCRE2_PCRE2TEST\n58\t#include \"pcre2_internal.h\"\n59\t#endif /* PCRE2_PCRE2TEST */\n60\t\n61\t\n62\t\n63\t/* The tables herein are needed only when UCP support is built, and in PCRE2\n64\tthat happens automatically with UTF support. This module should not be\n65\treferenced otherwise, so it should not matter whether it is compiled or not.\n66\tHowever a comment was received about space saving - maybe the guy linked all\n67\tthe modules rather than using a library - so we include a condition to cut out\n68\tthe tables when not needed. But don't leave a totally empty module because some\n69\tcompilers barf at that. Instead, just supply some small dummy tables. */\n70\t\n71\t#ifndef SUPPORT_UNICODE\n72\tconst ucd_record PRIV(ucd_records)[] = {{0,0,0,0,0,0,0}};\n73\tconst uint16_t PRIV(ucd_stage1)[] = {0};\n74\tconst uint16_t PRIV(ucd_stage2)[] = {0};\n75\tconst uint32_t PRIV(ucd_caseless_sets)[] = {0};\n76\tconst uint32_t PRIV(ucd_nocase_ranges)[] = {0};\n77\tconst uint32_t PRIV(ucd_nocase_ranges_size) = 0;\n78\t#else\n79\t\n80\t/* Total size: 116548 bytes, block size: 128. */\n81\t\n82\tconst char *PRIV(unicode_version) = \"17.0.0\";\n83\t\n84\t/* When recompiling tables with a new Unicode version, please check the types\n85\tin this structure definition with those in pcre2_internal.h (the actual field\n86\tnames will be different).\n87\t\n88\ttypedef struct {\n89\tuint8_t property_0;\n90\tuint8_t property_1;\n91\tuint8_t property_2;\n92\tuint8_t property_3;\n93\tint32_t property_4;\n94\tuint16_t property_5;\n95\tuint16_t property_6;\n96\t} ucd_record;\n97\t*/\n98\t\n99\t/* If the 32-bit library is run in non-32-bit mode, character values greater\n100\tthan 0x10ffff may be encountered. For these we set up a special record. */\n101\t\n102\t#if PCRE2_CODE_UNIT_WIDTH == 32\n103\tconst ucd_record PRIV(dummy_ucd_record)[] = {{\n104\t  ucp_Unknown,    /* script */\n105\t  ucp_Cn,         /* type unassigned */\n106\t  ucp_gbOther,    /* grapheme break property */\n107\t  0,              /* case set */\n108\t  0,              /* other case */\n109\t  0 | (ucp_bidiL << UCD_BIDICLASS_SHIFT), /* script extension and bidi class */\n110\t  0,              /* bool properties offset */\n111\t  }};\n112\t#endif\n113\t\n114\t/* This table contains lists of characters that are caseless sets of\n115\tmore than one character. Each list is terminated by NOTACHAR. */\n116\t\n117\tconst uint32_t PRIV(ucd_caseless_sets)[] = {\n118\t  NOTACHAR,\n119\t  0x0053,  0x0073,  0x017f,  NOTACHAR,\n120\t  0x01c4,  0x01c5,  0x01c6,  NOTACHAR,\n121\t  0x01c7,  0x01c8,  0x01c9,  NOTACHAR,\n122\t  0x01ca,  0x01cb,  0x01cc,  NOTACHAR,\n123\t  0x01f1,  0x01f2,  0x01f3,  NOTACHAR,\n124\t  0x0345,  0x0399,  0x03b9,  0x1fbe,  NOTACHAR,\n125\t  0x00b5,  0x039c,  0x03bc,  NOTACHAR,\n126\t  0x03a3,  0x03c2,  0x03c3,  NOTACHAR,\n127\t  0x0392,  0x03b2,  0x03d0,  NOTACHAR,\n128\t  0x0398,  0x03b8,  0x03d1,  0x03f4,  NOTACHAR,\n129\t  0x03a6,  0x03c6,  0x03d5,  NOTACHAR,\n130\t  0x03a0,  0x03c0,  0x03d6,  NOTACHAR,\n131\t  0x039a,  0x03ba,  0x03f0,  NOTACHAR,\n132\t  0x03a1,  