LINE` | **7398**, 7637-7654, **8050** | `firstline = !anchored && FIRSTLINE`; temporarily truncates `end_subject` at first newline; breaks bumpalong at 8050 |\n| `PCRE2_DOLLAR_ENDONLY` | **6586** | `OP_DOLL`: if set, falls through to `OP_EOD` semantics (`Feptr < true_end_subject` → NOMATCH); else `goto ASSERT_NL_OR_EOS` |\n| `PCRE2_ALT_CIRCUMFLEX` | **6642** | `OP_CIRCM`: allows `^` to match after a final newline |\n| `PCRE2_MATCH_UNSET_BACKREF` | **375**, **5333** | unset group backref matches empty (`*lengthptr=0; return 0`); at 5333 `Lmin==0 ||` MATCH_UNSET_BACKREF allows the repeat |\n| `PCRE2_NO_START_OPTIMIZE` | (none directly) | compiled into `re->optimization_flags` — see (B) |\n| `PCRE2_ANCHORED`/`ENDANCHORED` (compile) | 7397, 1000 | OR'ed with match options |\n| newline convention | 7443-7479 | `mb->nltype`/`nllen`/`nl[]` |\n| `PCRE2_HASCRORLF`, `PCRE2_HASTHEN`, `PCRE2_HASBSK`, `PCRE2_MATCH_EMPTY`, `PCRE2_STARTLINE`, `PCRE2_DUPCAPUSED` | 8069, 7421, 7422, 7423, 7399, — | CRLF bumpalong skip; verb handling; `allowemptypartial`; startline opt |\n| `PCRE2_EXTRA_ALLOW_LOOKAROUND_BSK` | 7424, **1044** | else `PCRE2_ERROR_BAD_BACKSLASH_K` (-75) when `\\K` moved start out of range (1022-1032) |\n| magic/mode checks | 7060-7066 | `PCRE2_ERROR_BADMAGIC`, `PCRE2_ERROR_BADMODE` |\n| `start_offset > length` | 7056 | `PCRE2_ERROR_BADOFFSET` |\n| NULL subject, length 0 | 7036 | treated as `null_str[1]={0xcd}` — empty string, *not* NULL error |\n\n# (B) Start-of-match optimisation\n\n## Gating: `PCRE2_OPTIM_*`\n`pcre2_internal.h:602-606`: `AUTO_POSSESS=0x1`, `DOTSTAR_ANCHOR=0x2`, `START_OPTIMIZE=0x4`, `PCRE2_OPTIMIZATION_ALL=0x7`. Public levels `pcre2.h:499-500` (`NONE=0`, `FULL=1`); context default `PCRE2_OPTIMIZATION_ALL` (`pcre2_context.c:141`), set at `pcre2_context.c:419-435`.\n\nMapping (`pcre2_compile.c`): `PCRE2_NO_AUTO_POSSESS`→clear AUTO_POSSESS (10410-10411); `PCRE2_NO_DOTSTAR_ANCHOR`→clear DOTSTAR_ANCHOR (10412-10413); `PCRE2_NO_START_OPTIMIZE`→clear START_OPTIMIZE (10414-10415). In-pattern verbs `(*NO_AUTO_POSSESS)` / `(*NO_DOTSTAR_ANCHOR)` / `(*NO_START_OPT)` at 746-749. Stored: `re->optimization_flags = optim_flags` (10921).\n\nWhat each controls:\n- **AUTO_POSSESS** → `PRIV(auto_possessify)` only (11084-11097). Purely opcode rewriting; visible only via callout counts / backtracking limits / `pcre2_pattern_info` sizes.\n- **DOTSTAR_ANCHOR** → `is_anchored(..., dotstar_anchor)` (11110-11113) and `is_startline(..., dotstar_anchor)` (11188-11190). Controls whether leading non-atomic `.*` implies ANCHORED (DOTALL) or STARTLINE (non-DOTALL).\n- **START_OPTIMIZE** → gates the whole compile-time block 11122-11270 (firstcu, asserted-firstcu, STARTLINE, reqcu, **`PRIV(study)` call at 11249**, minlength override 11266) **and** the entire runtime block `pcre2_match.c:7625-7944`. With it off, `re->flags` has no FIRSTSET/FIRSTMAPSET/STARTLINE/LASTSET and `re->minlength == 0`, and the runtime block is skipped entirely.\n\n## Runtime structure (`pcre2_match.c`)\nSetup: `has_first_cu`/`first_cu`/`first_cu2` from `PCRE2_FIRSTSET`/`PCRE2_FIRSTCASELESS` (**7557-7572**); `start_bits = re->start_bitmap` only if `!startline && PCRE2_FIRSTMAPSET` (**7573-7575**); `has_req_cu`/`req_cu`/`req_cu2` from `PCRE2_LASTSET`/`PCRE2_LASTCASELESS` (**7579-7594**). `req_cu_ptr = start_match - 1` (7049). `bumpalong_limit` (7400-7401). 8-bit memchr caches reset per fragment (7609-7612).\n\nBumpalong loop `for(;;)` at **7614**; opt block guarded by `if ((re->optimization_flags & PCRE2_OPTIM_START_OPTIMIZE) != 0)` at **7625**.\n\n| Branch | Lines | Minimal pattern / subject |\n|---|---|---|\n| firstline truncation of `end_subject` (UTF vs non-UTF scan) | 7637-7654 | `PCRE2_FIRSTLINE` + `/b/`, subj `\"a\\nb\"` → NOMATCH |\n| anchored + (firstcu or bitmap) pre-check | 7660-7684 | `/^abc/` subj `\"xbc\"` → break NOMATCH without running match() |\n| anchored, `start_match >= end_subject` → `ok=FALSE` | 7664 | `/^a/` subj `\"\"` |\n| unanchored caseless firstcu, 8-bit double `memchr` + cache | 7702-7748 | `/(?i)abc/` subj `\"...AbC\"`; cache path needs 2 bumpalongs, e.g. `/(?i)ab/` subj `\"aXaB\"` |\n| unanchored caseful firstcu (`memchr`) | 7752-7761 | `/abc/` subj `\"xxabc\"` |\n| firstcu not found → break | 7773-7777 | `if (mb->partial == 0 && start_match >= mb->end_subject)`; `/abc/` subj `\"zzz\"`. Partial-mode variant: `/(?<=abc)def/` + `PARTIAL_SOFT` subj `\"abc\"` → must NOT break |\n| `startline` (advance past newline) | 7782-7812 | `/(?m)^abc/` subj `\"x\\nabc\"`; note bitmap suppressed when startline (7574) |\n| CR/LF extra advance under ANY/ANYCRLF | 7805-7811 | `(?m)^b` + `PCRE2_NEWLINE_ANY`, subj `\"a\\r\\nb\"` |\n| start bitmap scan | 7819-7830 | `/[bcd]x/` or `/(cat\\|dog)/` subj `\"...dog\"` |\n| bitmap not found → break | 7834-7838 | `/[bcd]x/` subj `\"aaa\"` |\n| restore fudged `end_subject` | 7842 | — |\n| `if (mb->partial == 0)` guard for minlength + reqcu | 7846 | both disabled for any PARTIAL_* |\n| **minlength** check | **7855-7859** | `end_subject - start_match < re->minlength` → NOMATCH. `/abcdef/` (minlength 6) subj `\"abcde\"` |\n| **reqcu** search, `p = start_match + (has_first_cu?1:0)`, `p > req_cu_ptr` | 7879-7880 | `/a\\d+z/` subj `\"a1234\"` → NOMATCH without backtracking |\n| `REQ_CU_MAX` length gate (5000 8-bit; `pcre2_internal.h:550`), `!anchored → *1000` | 7883-7884 | subject > 5,000,000 CU with anchored `/^\\d+C/` skips the search |\n| reqcu caseless (single memchr, no earliest-find) | 7886-7909 | `/(?i)a\\d+z/` subj `\"a1Z\"` |\n| reqcu caseful | 7912-7925 | `/a\\d+z/` |\n| reqcu not found → break | 7929-7933 | `/ab/` subj `\"aaaa\"` |\n| `req_cu_ptr` memo update | 7941 | needs ≥2 bumpalongs: `/a\\d+z/` subj `\"aaz...\"` |\n| **offset_limit** | **7400-7401**, **7950-7954** | `bumpalong_limit = subject + mcontext->offset_limit`; `start_match > bumpalong_limit` → NOMATCH. Requires `PCRE2_USE_OFFSET_LIMIT` at compile (else 7118 error). `/b/` + limit 1, subj `\"aab\"` → NOMATCH; limit 2 → match |\n| **START_OPTIMIZE disabled** | 7625 false | Compile with `PCRE2_NO_START_OPTIMIZE` (or `(*NO_START_OPT)`): `/abc/` subj `\"zzz\"` now runs `match()` at every position (all callouts fire, `match_call_count` resets per position), and `/(?<=x)y/` etc. still work. Also `re->minlength==0`, no bitmap, no reqcu — differential: `pcre2_pattern_info(PCRE2_INFO_MINLENGTH/FIRSTCODEUNIT/FIRSTBITMAP/LASTCODEUNIT)` |\n| post-`match()` bumpalong advance (NOMATCH/PRUNE/THEN/SKIP) | 7994-8046 | `MATCH_SKIP_ARG` retry at same point (8000-8002); `MATCH_SKIP` uses `mb->verb_skip_ptr` (8008-8013); `MATCH_COMMIT` → `goto ENDLOOP` (8033-8035) |\n| CRLF double-advance | 8069-8077 | requires `(re->flags & PCRE2_HASCRORLF)==0`; `/x/` newline=CRLF subj `\"a\\r\\nx\"` |\n| anchored / past-end break | 8058 | `if (anchored \\|\\| start_match > end_subject) break` |\n\n# (C) Limits\n\nVariables in `match_block` (`pcre2_intmodedep.h:1038-1041`, 1095-1098): `mb->match_limit`, `mb->match_limit_depth`, `mb->heap_limit`, `mb->match_call_count`.\n\nResolution — **pattern limit wins only if smaller** (7502-7509):\n```\nmb->heap_limit       = min(mcontext->heap_limit,  re->limit_heap)     7502-7503\nmb->match_limit      = min(mcontext->match_limit, re->limit_match)    7505-7506\nmb->match_limit_depth= min(mcontext->depth_limit, re->limit_depth)    7508-7509\n```\n`re->limit_*` default `UINT32_MAX` (`pcre2_compile.c:10308-10310`), set by `(*LIMIT_HEAP=n)`/`(*LIMIT_MATCH=n)`/`(*LIMIT_DEPTH=n)` (10554-10556). Context defaults `HEAP_LIMIT=20000000` KiB, `MATCH_LIMIT=10000000`, `MATCH_LIMIT_DEPTH=MATCH_LIMIT` (`pcre2_context.c:176-178`, `config.h:169/195/208`).\n\n- **`PCRE2_ERROR_MATCHLIMIT` (-47)**: `pcre2_match.c:873` `if (mb->match_call_count++ >= mb->match_limit)`. Counted **once per frame creation / NEW_FRAME entry**. **Reset to 0 at 7969 for every bumpalong start position** → the limit is per-start-position, not per `pcre2_match()` call. Reach: `match_limit=0` → immediate on any pattern/subject. `match_limit=1` → any pattern (top-level `OP_BRA` needs ≥2 frames). Classic: `/(a+)*b/` on `\"aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\"` with default limits (needs `PCRE2_NO_AUTO_POSSESS` to defeat possessification).\n- **`PCRE2_ERROR_DEPTHLIMIT` (-53)**: `874` `if (Frdepth >= mb->match_limit_depth)`. `Frdepth` = `F->rdepth`, set at 828 (`N->rdepth = Frdepth + 1`), init 0 (741). Reach: `depth_limit=0` → immediate; `depth_limit=1`; or `/a*/` deep-nesting `/((((((((((a))))))))))/`.\n- **heapframe geometry** (7495-7497): `frame_size = (offsetof(heapframe,ovector) + re->top_bracket*2*sizeof(PCRE2_SIZE) + HEAPFRAME_ALIGNMENT-1) & ~(HEAPFRAME_ALIGNMENT-1)`; `HEAPFRAME_ALIGNMENT = offsetof(heapframe_align, frame)` (`pcre2_intmodedep.h:1031`).\n- **initial vector** (7516-7541): `heapframes_size = max(frame_size*10, START_FRAMES_SIZE=20480)` (`pcre2_internal.h:225`); if `heapframes_size/1024 > mb->heap_limit` → clamp to `1024*heap_limit`, and **`PCRE2_ERROR_HEAPLIMIT` (-63) at 7521** if `max_size < frame_size`. Reused if `match_data->heapframes_size >= heapframes_size` (7528); else free+malloc, **`PCRE2_ERROR_NOMEMORY` (-48) at 7537** (also zeroes `heapframes_size`). Then `memset(...0xff...)` of frame-0 ovector (7545-7546).\n- **growth path** (`MATCH_RECURSE`, 758-802): triggered when `(char*)N + frame_size >= frames_top` (759). `newsize = heapframes_size*2` (772), with `PCRE2_SIZE_MAX` saturation (765-771, `NOMEMORY` at 768). Heap-limit clamp 774-789: **`HEAPLIMIT` at 778** when `mb->heap_limit <= old_size`; else `newsize = old + 1024*(heap_limit-old_size)` minus partial-KiB (781-785). **`HEAPLIMIT` at 791** if `newsize - usedsize < frame_size`. **`NOMEMORY` at 793** if malloc fails. On success: memcpy `usedsize` (794), re-point `N`/`F` (796-797), free old, update `match_data->heapframes`/`_size`/`frames_top` (799-802) — **`match_data` is mutated across calls**, so heapframes_size is sticky/monotonic.\n- Reach HEAPLIMIT: `heap_limit=1` (KiB) + `/(a+)+b/` on `\"aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\"` → 7521 passes (frame_size ≈128B < 1024) then 778 fires (old_size=1, heap_limit=1). `heap_limit=0` → 7521 fires immediately (`max_size=0 < frame_size`). For 791: a pattern with many captures (large frame_size) + heap_limit just above the current size, e.g. `frame_size > 1024` (≈60+ captures) with `heap_limit = ceil(current/1024)+1`.\n- Reach NOMEMORY: custom `pcre2_general_context` allocator returning NULL on the Nth malloc.\n\n**Recursion loop**: `PCRE2_ERROR_RECURSELOOP` (-52) at **5729**, inside `case OP_RECURSE` (5707). Condition (5720-5731): `Fcurrent_recurse != RECURSE_UNSET` (i.e. already inside a pattern recursion), walk the `Flast_group_offset` chain (5723-5724) for `N->group_frame_type == (GF_RECURSE|number)`, and `Feptr == P->eptr && mb->last_used_ptr == P->recurse_last_used && (mb->moptions & PCRE2_DISABLE_RECURSELOOP_CHECK) == 0`. `F->recurse_last_used = mb->last_used_ptr` at 5739. `RECURSE_UNSET = 0xffffffffu` (67). Test: `/((?2))((?1))/` on `\"abc\"` → -52. With `PCRE2_DISABLE_RECURSELOOP_CHECK` the same input instead terminates via `MATCHLIMIT` (-47) or `HEAPLIMIT`/`NOMEMORY` — the option is not in `PUBLIC_JIT_MATCH_OPTIONS` (77-80) so it also forces interpreter. Note the check also requires *unchanged* `last_used_ptr`, so `/((?2))((?1)(?=x))/`-style patterns that inspect a character escape the check.\n\nOther internal error returns: `PCRE2_ERROR_INTERNAL` at 7477 (bad newline convention), 6957 (bad `Freturn_id`), 6889 (unknown opcode); corrupted-heapframe asserts at 907, 949, 6375.\n\n# (D) ovector / match_data\n\n`pcre2_match_data_create` (`pcre2_match_data.c:53-68`): clamps `oveccount<1 → 1` (**57**), `>UINT16_MAX → UINT16_MAX` (**58**); size `offsetof(pcre2_match_data,ovector) + 2*oveccount*sizeof(PCRE2_SIZE)` (**60**); sets only `oveccount`(63), `flags=0`(64), `heapframes=NULL`(65), `heapframes_size=0`(66). **`rc`, `mark`, `subject`, `startchar`, `ovector[]` are left uninitialised.**\n\n`pcre2_match_data_create_from_pattern` (**80-88**): `code==NULL → NULL` (**84**); `gcontext==NULL → gcontext=(pcre2_general_context*)code` (**85**, i.e. pattern's allocator); `oveccount = re->top_bracket + 1` (**86**). Differential: `pcre2_match_data_create(0,...)` → oveccount 1; `_from_pattern` on `/(a)(b)/` → oveccount 3; on `/abc/` → 1.\n\n`pcre2_match_data_free` **96-109** (frees heapframes 101-103, copied subject 104-106). Accessors: `pcre2_get_mark` **117-121** (`return match_data->mark`), `pcre2_get_ovector_pointer` **129-133**, `pcre2_get_ovector_count` **141-145**, `pcre2_get_startchar` **153-157** (`return match_data->startchar`), `pcre2_get_match_data_size` **165-170**, `pcre2_get_match_data_heapframes_size` **178-182**.\n\nFill semantics (`pcre2_match.c`):\n- `OP_END` success (**1040-1054**): `ovector[0]=Fstart_match-start_subject`, `ovector[1]=Feptr-start_subject` (1045-1046, always safe: oveccount≥1). `i = 2*min(top_bracket+1, oveccount)` (1050-1051); `memcpy(ovector+2, Fovector, (i-2)*sizeof)` (1052); trailing pairs `while (--i >= Foffset_top + 2) ovector[i] = PCRE2_UNSET` (1053). Frame ovector pre-set to `0xff` at 7545. Gaps set UNSET dynamically.\n- `match_data->rc` (**8180-8181**): `((int)mb->end_offset_top >= 2*match_data->oveccount) ? 0 : (int)mb->end_offset_top/2 + 1`. So **rc==0 means \"ovector too small\"** but pairs 0..oveccount-1 *are still filled* (truncation, not failure).\n- Success extras (8179-8202): `subject_length=length`, `start_offset`, `startchar = start_match - subject`, `leftchar = mb->start_used_ptr - subject`, `rightchar = max(last_used_ptr, end_match_ptr) - subject`.\n- Always set (8168-8171): `code`, `mark`, `matchedby = PCRE2_MATCHEDBY_INTERPRETER`, `options = original_options`.\n- **PARTIAL** (**8221-8232**): only `ovector[0] = match_partial - subject`, `ovector[1] = end_subject - subject`; pairs ≥1 are **stale/uninitialised**. `startchar = match_partial-subject`, `leftchar = start_partial-subject`, `rightchar = end_subject-subject`, `rc = PCRE2_ERROR_PARTIAL`. `start_partial/match_partial` captured at 7984-7988 from `mb->start_used_ptr` / `start_match`.\n- **NOMATCH** (**8236-8242**): `rc = PCRE2_ERROR_NOMATCH`; **no ovector write at all**.\n- Errors (**8215**): `if (rc != MATCH_NOMATCH && rc != PCRE2_ERROR_PARTIAL) match_data->rc = rc;` — ovector untouched.\n- `mark`: `match_data->mark = mb->mark` at **8169**, then **overwritten** with `mb->nomatch_mark` at **8211** for every non-`MATCH_MATCH` outcome (including errors). Sources: `Fmark = mb->nomatch_mark = Fecode+2` for `OP_MARK` (6778), `OP_COMMIT_ARG` (6810), `OP_PRUNE_ARG` (6823), `OP_THEN_ARG` (6874); `OP_SKIP_ARG` deliberately does **not** set it (6837-6841); `mb->mark`/`nomatch_mark` init NULL at 7430; `mb->mark = NULL` per bumpalong at 8079.\n- `startchar` is also overwritten by UTF errors (7137 zeroed; 7205, 7333, 7345, 8135 set to the bad-CU offset) → on `PCRE2_ERROR_UTF8_ERR*` it is the absolute error offset.\n\nTest shapes: `/(a)(b)(c)/` on `\"abc\"` with `oveccount` = 1 → rc 0, ovector[0..1]={0,3}; 2 → rc 0, pairs 0,1; 3 → rc 0; 4 → rc 4, all pairs; 10 → rc 4, pairs 4..9 = UNSET. `/(a)(b)?/` on `\"a\"` → rc 2, ovector[4]=ovector[5]=UNSET. `/(?:(a)|(b))c/` on `\"bc\"` → ovector[2..3] UNSET (gap). `\\K`: `/ab\\Kcd/` on `\"abcd\"` → ovector={2,4}, `startchar=2`, `leftchar=0`.\n\n# (E) `pcre2_next_match()` — `pcre2_match_next.c`\n\nSignature **96-98**: `int pcre2_next_match(pcre2_match_data *match_data, PCRE2_SIZE *pstart_offset, uint32_t *poptions)`; returns `TRUE`/`FALSE` (as `int`). Reads only `match_data->rc` (100), `->start_offset` (101), `->ovector` (102), plus `->subject`, `->subject_length`, `->code` inside `do_bumpalong`.\n\nDecision order:\n1. **108-109** `rc < 0` (NOMATCH, PARTIAL, or any error) → `return FALSE`; `*pstart_offset`/`*poptions` untouched.\n2. **116** `PCRE2_ASSERT(ovector[1] >= start_offset)`.\n3. **129-141** `\\K` degenerate case `ovector[0] != start_offset && ovector[1] == start_offset` (non-empty match that makes no progress): if `start_offset >= subject_length` → FALSE; else `*pstart_offset = do_bumpalong(match_data, ovector[1])`, `*poptions = 0`, TRUE.\n4. **147-160** empty match `ovector[0] == ovector[1]`: if `>= subject_length` → FALSE; else `*pstart_offset = ovector[1]`, `*poptions = PCRE2_NOTEMPTY_ATSTART`, TRUE. (**No bumpalong** here.)\n5. **166-168** normal: `*pstart_offset = ovector[1]`, `*poptions = 0`, TRUE.\n\n`do_bumpalong` (**49-88**) distinguishes:\n- **CRLF** (61-71): `subject[offset]==CR && offset+1 < subject_length && subject[offset+1]==LF` **and** `code->newline_convention ∈ {CRLF, ANY, ANYCRLF}` → `offset+2`. (CR/LF/NUL conventions fall through to +1.)\n- **UTF** (75-85): `utf = code->overall_options & PCRE2_UTF`; `FORWARDCHARTEST(next, subject_end)` → next character boundary.\n- else `offset + 1` (87).\n\nCombos to cover: rc<0 vs rc≥0 vs rc==0 (oveccount-too-small still ≥0 → iterates); empty match mid-subject vs at end; non-empty; `\\K` case 3 with `subject_length` boundary; CR at end of subject (no LF follows); CRLF under each of the 5 newline conventions; UTF multi-byte at `ovector[1]`; and the caller loop `PCRE2_NOTEMPTY_ATSTART` retry producing NOMATCH then requiring another `pcre2_next_match` (which returns FALSE because rc<0). Note `do_bumpalong` dereferences `match_data->subject`, which with `PCRE2_COPY_MATCHED_SUBJECT` is the internal copy, and after a `pcre2_match_data_create` with no prior match is uninitialised.\n\n# (F) `_pcre2_study()` — `pcre2_study.c`\n\nSignature **1914-1916**: `int PRIV(study)(pcre2_real_code *re)`. Returns 0 normally; 1 = `SSB_UNKNOWN` from `set_start_bits`; 2 = missing capturing bracket; 3 = unknown opcode in `find_minlength` (all three are `PCRE2_DEBUG_UNREACHABLE`). Called once, `pcre2_compile.c:11249`, only when `PCRE2_OPTIM_START_OPTIMIZE` is on.\n\nBody:\n- `utf`/`ucp` from `re->overall_options` (1919-1920); `code = (uint8_t*)re + re->code_start` (1924).\n- **Bitmap phase, gated at 1930**: `if ((re->flags & (PCRE2_FIRSTSET|PCRE2_STARTLINE)) == 0)` → `depth=0; set_start_bits(re, code, utf, ucp, &depth)` (1932-1933). `SSB_UNKNOWN` → return 1 (1935-1940). If `SSB_DONE` (1950): scan the 256-bit map (1956-2017) — if exactly **one** bit set → `re->first_codeunit = a`, `flags = PCRE2_FIRSTSET` (2035-2037); if **two** bits that are case-partners (`TABLE_GET(fcc)`, or `UCD_OTHERCASE` when utf||ucp; bail if `UCD_CASESET(c)!=0`) → `PCRE2_FIRSTSET|PCRE2_FIRSTCASELESS` (2038); else `goto DONE` with `flags = PCRE2_FIRSTMAPSET` (1965). 8-bit UTF: bits ≥128 abort the conversion (1948-1949 comment / `if (utf && c>127) goto DONE`, 1990-1991). 16/32-bit: bit 0xff excluded (1975-1977). `re->flags |= flags` at 2042. **Special**: if converting to a first CU and `re->last_codeunit` equals `a` or `b`, `PCRE2_LASTSET|PCRE2_LASTCASELESS` are cleared and `last_codeunit=0` (2029-2033) — needed for `/a*a/`.\n- **minlength phase, gated at 2053**: `if ((re->flags & (PCRE2_MATCH_EMPTY|PCRE2_HASACCEPT)) == 0 && re->top_backref <= MAX_CACHE_BACKREF)`. `MAX_CACHE_BACKREF = 128` (**52**). `find_minlength(re, code, code, utf, NULL, &count, backref_cache)` (2059). `-1` → leave `minlength` at 0 (2062-2063); `-2`/`-3` → return 2/3; else `re->minlength = min(min, UINT16_MAX)` (2076). Field is `uint16_t minlength` (`pcre2_intmodedep.h:680`); read by `pcre2_pattern_info.c:218`.\n- Also in the caller: `if ((re->flags & PCRE2_FIRSTMAPSET) != 0 && minminlength == 0) minminlength = 1` (`pcre2_compile.c:11262-11263`) and `if (re->minlength < minminlength) re->minlength = minminlength` (11268).\n\n`SSB_*` enum **60**: `{SSB_FAIL, SSB_DONE, SSB_CONTINUE, SSB_UNKNOWN, SSB_TOODEEP}`.\n\n## `set_start_bits` (**1092-1894**)\n`static int set_start_bits(pcre2_real_code *re, PCRE2_SPTR code, BOOL utf, BOOL ucp, int *depthptr)`. `table_limit = utf ? 16 : 32` (8-bit UTF) at 1100-1104. **Depth limit: `*depthptr += 1; if (*depthptr > 1000) return SSB_TOODEEP;` (1105-1106)** — monotonically increasing counter, so it is a *total node count*, not stack depth. Outer 