h = start_match - subject` (**7959**), `cb.callout_flags |= PCRE2_CALLOUT_STARTMATCH` (**7960**).\n\n`callout_flags` (`pcre2.h:575-578`): `PCRE2_CALLOUT_STARTMATCH 0x1`, `PCRE2_CALLOUT_BACKTRACK 0x2`; struct field is Version-2 (`pcre2.h:600`). `BACKTRACK` is OR'ed in `RETURN_SWITCH` at **6913** (`mb->cb->callout_flags |= PCRE2_CALLOUT_BACKTRACK;`, after the `Frdepth==0` early return at 6912). Both are cleared only by `do_callout` at 328 — so flags **accumulate** across bumpalongs/backtracks that contain no callout, and a single callout can see both bits set.\n\nCall sites:\n- `case OP_CALLOUT: case OP_CALLOUT_STR:` (**5989-5996**): `rrc>0 → RRETURN(MATCH_NOMATCH)`; `rrc<0 → RRETURN(rrc)`; `rrc==0 → Fecode += length`.\n- Inside `OP_COND/OP_SCOND` before an assertion condition (**6026-6039**), same 3-way handling, plus `Fecode += length; Llength -= length`.\n\nReturn-value semantics: `0` = continue; `>0` = fail this match path (backtracks, so the overall match may still succeed at another position/alternative); `<0` = abort and propagate to the caller unchanged. `PCRE2_ERROR_CALLOUT = -37` (`pcre2.h:401`, \"Never used by PCRE2 itself\") — it is purely a convention for the callout to return. **Collision hazard for differential tests**: internal codes `MATCH_ACCEPT=-999`, `MATCH_KETRPOS=-998`, `MATCH_COMMIT=-997`, `MATCH_PRUNE=-996`, `MATCH_SKIP=-995`, `MATCH_SKIP_ARG=-994`, `MATCH_THEN=-993` (`pcre2_match.c:90-99`); a callout returning one of these is misinterpreted as a backtracking verb. A callout returning `-1` surfaces as `PCRE2_ERROR_NOMATCH` via 8215.\n\nCoverage combos: no callout function set (returns 0 at 279); `(?C)` / `(?C1)` / `(?C255)`; `(?C\"str\")` / `(?C'str')` / `(?C{str}` variants → string fields; `PCRE2_AUTO_CALLOUT` (callouts at every item, plus the OP_COND-before-assertion path); callout returning 0 / +1 / -1 / -37 / -999; callout at `pattern_position==0` vs at end (`next_item_length==0`); `capture_top`/`capture_last` after `(a)(b)` partial progres