[2...]` = `active_states` (line 580), `new_states = active_states + wscount_states` (581).\n- **DFA_WSSIZE at run time**: the four state-adding macros, lines 489-525 — `ADD_ACTIVE` (496), `ADD_ACTIVE_DATA` (506), `ADD_NEW` (515), `ADD_NEW_DATA` (525); each returns `PCRE2_ERROR_DFA_WSSIZE` when `active_count++ >= wscount` / `new_count++ >= wscount`.\n- **The caller's workspace is never grown or reallocated.** It is reused verbatim across all bumpalong iterations (passed at line 4034; `workspace[0]` re-zeroed each call at line 694). Growth happens only for the *internal* recursion workspace (RWS) — see (F).\n\n# (B) Option branches\n\nAccepted mask, lines 83-87:\n```c\n#define PUBLIC_DFA_MATCH_OPTIONS \\\n  (PCRE2_ANCHORED|PCRE2_ENDANCHORED|PCRE2_NOTBOL|PCRE2_NOTEOL|PCRE2_NOTEMPTY| \\\n   PCRE2_NOTEMPTY_ATSTART|PCRE2_NO_UTF_CHECK|PCRE2_PARTIAL_HARD| \\\n   PCRE2_PARTIAL_SOFT|PCRE2_DFA_SHORTEST|PCRE2_DFA_RESTART| \\\n   PCRE2_COPY_MATCHED_SUBJECT)\n```\nNumeric mask = 0xE00040FF | 0x4000 = **0xE00040FF + 0x4000 → 0xE00040FF|0x00004000 = 0xE00040FF plus bit14** i.e. `0x80000000|0x40000000|0x20000000|0x4000|0xFF`.\n\n| Option | Lines | Effect |\n|---|---|---|\n| rejection | **3399-3400** `if ((options & ~PUBLIC_DFA_MATCH_OPTIONS) != 0) rc = PCRE2_ERROR_BADOPTION` | Rejects: `PCRE2_NO_JIT` (0x2000), `PCRE2_DISABLE_RECURSELOOP_CHECK` (0x40000), all `PCRE2_SUBSTITUTE_*` (0x100,0x200,0x400,0x800,0x1000,0x8000,0x10000,0x20000), and every other bit. Note DFA accepts NO_JIT-free only — `pcre2_dfa_match(..., PCRE2_NO_JIT, ...)` → BADOPTION. |\n| second BADOPTION | **3413-3415** | `(PARTIAL_HARD|PARTIAL_SOFT)` together with `ENDANCHORED` (from either `re->overall_options` or `options`) → BADOPTION. |\n| PCRE2_DFA_RESTART | 86; **668-674**; **3454-3459**; **3467**; **3709** | 668: at `rlevel==1` skips branch push, sets `new_count = workspace[1]`, and if `!workspace[0]` memcpy's `active_states`→`new_states`. 3456-3458: sanity check → `DFA_BADRESTART`. 3467: **forces `anchored = TRUE`** (hence `firstline=FALSE` at 3474). 3709: **disables all start optimizations**. |\n| PCRE2_DFA_SHORTEST | 86; **891** | At end-of-pattern, `return match_count;` immediately after recording the first (shortest) match — returns 1 (or 0 if oveccount==0). |\n| PCRE2_PARTIAL_HARD | 85; **963-964** (OP_EOD → immediate `PCRE2_ERROR_PARTIAL`), **990-997** (OP_ANY at split CRLF → `partial_newline`), **1015-1016** (OP_EODN → PARTIAL), **1025-1026 / 1038-1042** (OP_DOLL), **1052-1053 / 1063-1067** (OP_DOLLM), **1290, 1321, 1351, 1379, 1408** (TYPEPLUS/TYPEQUERY/TYPESTAR/TYPEEXACT/TYPEUPTO CRLF-split), **2129** (PROP_EXTRA+TYPEEXACT/UPTO \\X), **2308** (OP_EXTUNI), **2341** (OP_ANYNL CR at end), **3278**, **3855**, **3912**, **3924** | Forces `could_continue`/`reset_could_continue`; converts assertions of end-of-subject into PARTIAL; suppresses first_cu/start_bits/minlength/req_cu optimizations. |\n| PCRE2_PARTIAL_SOFT | 86; **1033**, **1058**, **3280-3281**, **3855**, **3912**, **3924** | Same optimization suppression; at 3280 PARTIAL only when `match_count < 0` (never overrides a found match). |\n| PCRE2_NOTBOL | 84; **947** (OP_CIRC), **953** (OP_CIRCM) | Suppresses `^` matching at `start_subject`. |\n| PCRE2_NOTEOL | 84; **1023** (OP_DOLL), **1050** (OP_DOLLM); **1071-1072** | Suppresses `$`; for DOLLM the `else` at 1071 still allows `$` before an interior newline. |\n| PCRE2_NOTEMPTY | 84; **876** | In OP_KET/KETR* end-of-pattern block: no match recorded if `ptr == current_subject`. |\n| PCRE2_NOTEMPTY_ATSTART | 85; **877-878** | Empty match rejected only when `current_subject <= start_subject + mb->start_offset`. |\n| both, via pattern flags | **3445-3449** | `(*NOTEMPTY)` / `(*NOTEMPTY_ATSTART)` bits (`PCRE2_NOTEMPTY_SET`/`PCRE2_NE_ATST_SET`) shifted into `options`. |\n| PCRE2_ANCHORED | 84; **3467-3468** | `anchored = (options & (ANCHORED|DFA_RESTART)) != 0 || (re->overall_options & ANCHORED)`. Used at 3741 (anchored first-cu probe) and 4042 (no bumpalong). |\n| PCRE2_ENDANCHORED | 84; **3305-3308**; 3413-3415 | Post-loop in `internal_dfa_match`: `if (match_count >= 0 && ((mb->moptions|mb->poptions) & ENDANCHORED) && ptr < end_subject) match_count = PCRE2_ERROR_NOMATCH;`. Note this uses the *final* `ptr` of the scan, not each recorded match end. |\n| PCRE2_NO_UTF_CHECK | 85; **3590** | Skips the whole UTF validation + BADUTFOFFSET block (3589-3628). |\n| PCRE2_COPY_MATCHED_SUBJECT | 87; **3679-3684**, **4061-4074** | 3679: frees a previously copied subject (`PCRE2_MD_COPIED_SUBJECT`). 4061: on `rc >= 0` only (not on PARTIAL) mallocs+memcpy `CU2BYTES(length)`; `length==0` → `subject=NULL`; failure → `PCRE2_ERROR_NOMEMORY` (4068). |\n\nAlso: `PCRE2_ERROR_NULL` 3396-3398 (`match_data==NULL`, or `re/subject/workspace == NULL`); `NULL,length 0` → empty string 3392; `PCRE2_ERROR_BADOFFSET` 3408; `PCRE2_ERROR_BADMAGIC` 3425-3426; `PCRE2_ERROR_BADMODE` 3430-3431; `PCRE2_ERROR_BADOFFSETLIMIT` 3503-3506 (offset_limit set without compile-time `PCRE2_USE_OFFSET_LIMIT`).\n\n# (C) Rejected features\n\nTwo DFA_UITEM sites: line **825** (unsupported *argument* of a type-repeat) and line **3258-3259** (`default:` of the main opcode switch).\n\n**PCRE2_ERROR_DFA_UITEM (-42)**\n\nOpcodes with **no case label** in the switch (verified by enumerating the `OP_` enum in `pcre2_internal.h` against the case labels) → all fall to `default:` line 3259:\n\n| Opcode(s) | Minimal trigger pattern |\n|---|---|\n| `OP_ANYBYTE` (14) | `\\C` **only in 8/16-bit UTF mode** (`/\\C/utf`). In 8-bit non-UTF `\\C` compiles to `OP_ALLANY` and *works* — see `pcre2_compile.c:8350-8368` (`if (!utf) meta_arg = OP_ALLANY;`). |\n| `OP_SET_SOM` (3) | `\\K` → `a\\Kb` |\n| `OP_REF`, `OP_REFI`, `OP_DNREF`, `OP_DNREFI` | back references: `(a)\\1`, `(?i)(a)\\1`, `(?<n>a)(?<n>b)\\k<n>` (DNREF/DNREFI need duplicate names) |\n| `OP_VREVERSE` (127) | **variable-length lookbehind**: `(?<=a{1,3})b`. (Fixed-length `OP_REVERSE` is handled in the special lookbehind prologue 592-654. Note 600 reads `GET2(end_code,2+LINK_SIZE)` unconditionally, so for a VREVERSE branch it mis-reads the min value, then 644 sets `revlen=0` and the state lands on the `OP_VREVERSE` byte itself → default → UITEM.) |\n| `OP_ASSERT_NA`, `OP_ASSERTBACK_NA` | non-atomic lookarounds: `(*napla:a)b`, `(*naplb:a)b`, `(?*a)b` |\n| `OP_ASSERT_SCS` | scan-substring: `(*scs:(1)...)` (`pcre2_compile.c:6641`) |\n| `OP_SCRIPT_RUN` | `(*script_run:\\d+)` / `(*sr:\\d+)` (`pcre2_compile.c:6904`) |\n| `OP_MARK`, `OP_PRUNE`, `OP_PRUNE_ARG`, `OP_SKIP`, `OP_SKIP_ARG`, `OP_THEN`, `OP_THEN_ARG`, `OP_COMMIT`, `OP_COMMIT_ARG` | `a(*MARK:m)b`, `a(*PRUNE)b`, `a(*PRUNE:x)b`, `a(*SKIP)b`, `a(*SKIP:x)b`, `a(*THEN)b`, `a(*THEN:x)b`, `a(*COMMIT)b`, `a(*COMMIT:x)b`. **Exception: `(*FAIL)`/`(?!)` → `OP_FAIL`, which IS supported (line 2781-2782).** |\n| `OP_ACCEPT`, `OP_ASSERT_ACCEPT`, `OP_CLOSE` | `a(*ACCEPT)b`, `(a(*ACCEPT))` |\n| `OP_END`, `OP_REVERSE`, `OP_CREF`, `OP_DNCREF`, `OP_RREF`, `OP_DNRREF`, `OP_FALSE`, `OP_TRUE`, `OP_DEFINE` | unreachable as top-level states in practice (CREF/RREF/FALSE/TRUE handled inline inside `OP_COND`, 2850-2881) |\n\nExplicit UITEM returns:\n- **825**: `case OP_ANYBYTE: return PCRE2_ERROR_DFA_UITEM;` inside the `codevalue >= OP_TYPESTAR` argument dispatch → **quantified `\\C` under UTF**: `/\\C*/utf`, `/\\C+/utf`, `/\\C?/utf`, `/\\C{2,4}/utf`.\n- **2943**: `if (code[1 + LINK_SIZE] == OP_CREF) return PCRE2_ERROR_DFA_UITEM;` — comment \"Argument list has not been supported yet.\" → **recursion with a capture-argument list**: `((a))(?1(2))` (syntax parsed at `pcre2_compile.c:5272-5277`, emitted as `OP_RECURSE` + `OP_CREF...` at `pcre2_compile.c:8218-8231`).\n\n**Supported (do NOT trigger UITEM)** — worth pinning for the diff suite: possessive quantifiers (`OP_POSSTAR`/`POSPLUS`/`POSQUERY`/`POSUPTO` 2434-2606, `OP_CRPOS*` 2698-2747, `OP_BRAPOS`/`SBRAPOS`/`CBRAPOS`/`SCBRAPOS`/`BRAPOSZERO` 3030-3034), atomic groups (`OP_ONCE` 3136), `\\X` (`OP_EXTUNI` 2302), `\\R` (`OP_ANYNL` 2320), `\\p`/`\\P` (1164-1165), `OP_XCLASS` **and** `OP_ECLASS` (extended/set-operation classes, 2643-2644, guarded by `#ifdef SUPPORT_WIDE_CHARS`, which *is* defined in 8-bit + SUPPORT_UNICODE per `pcre2_intmodedep.h:230-238`), UCP word boundaries (`OP_UCP_WORD_BOUNDARY`/`OP_NOT_UCP_WORD_BOUNDARY` 1097-1098), fixed-length lookbehinds, `\\G` (`OP_SOM` 975), `(?(R)...)` recursion-any condition.\n\n**PCRE2_ERROR_DFA_UCOND (-40)** — 2 sites:\n- **2855-2857**: `condcode == OP_CREF || OP_DNCREF || OP_DNRREF` → numbered/named capture conditions: `(a)?(?(1)b|c)`, `(?<n>a)?(?(<n>)b|c)`, and duplicate-name recursion condition `(?(R&n)a|b)` where `n` is duplicated (DNRREF).\n- **2874-2877**: `condcode == OP_RREF && value != RREF_ANY` → specific-group recursion condition: `(a(?(R1)b|c))`, `(?(R2)a|b)`. `(?(R)a|b)` (RREF_ANY) is supported.\n\n**PCRE2_ERROR_DFA_UFUNC (-41)** — never produced in this file. Produced when a DFA-produced match_data is passed to capture-extraction APIs (guard is `match_data->matchedby == PCRE2_MATCHEDBY_DFA_INTERPRETER`, set at line 3691):\n- `pcre2_substring_copy_byname` — `pcre2_substring.c:74-75`\n- `pcre2_substring_get_byname` — `pcre2_substring.c:161-163`\n- `pcre2_substring_length_byname` — `pcre2_substring.c:268-270`\n- `pcre2_substitute` — `pcre2_substitute.c:849-850` (only on the `PCRE2_SUBSTITUTE_MATCHED` path)\n- Note `pcre2_substring_length_bynumber` (`pcre2_substring.c:324-335`) has a *permissive* DFA branch (only `oveccount` bound-checks, no `top_bracket`/UNSET checks).\n\n**PCRE2_ERROR_DFA_RECURSE (-39)** — **line 2995**: `if (rc == 0) return PCRE2_ERROR_DFA_RECURSE;` after the `OP_RECURSE` internal call. Trigger: a pattern recursion whose recursed sub-match produces more than `RWS_OVEC_RSIZE/OVEC_UNIT / 2` = **500 distinct match lengths at one point** (local ovector overflow). e.g. `^(a|aa|aaa...)` style recursion, or `^((?:a?){500,})(?1)?` — needs >500 alternative end positions from the recursed group at one start.\n\n**PCRE2_ERROR_DFA_BADRESTART (-38)** — **lines 3454-3459**:\n```c\nif ((workspace[0] & (-2)) != 0 || workspace[1] < 1 ||\n    workspace[1] > (int)((wscount - 2)/INTS_PER_STATEBLOCK))\n```\nTriggers when `PCRE2_DFA_RESTART` is set and: `workspace[0]` is anything other than 0 or 1; or `workspace[1] < 1`; or `workspace[1] > (wscount-2)/3`. **Note the asymmetry**: the check divides by `INTS_PER_STATEBLOCK` (3) but the real per-vector capacity is `(wscount-2)/6` — so a value in `((wscount-2)/6, (wscount-2)/3]` passes validation but exceeds capacity. Easiest triggers: fresh/zeroed workspace + RESTART (workspace[1]==0), or `workspace[0]=2`.\n\n**PCRE2_ERROR_DFA_UINVALID_UTF (-66)** — **lines 3419-3420**: `if ((re->overall_options & PCRE2_MATCH_INVALID_UTF) != 0)`. It is a *pattern* property, checked before the magic-number/mode checks, so any pattern compiled with `PCRE2_MATCH_INVALID_UTF` (0x04000000) is rejected regardless of subject or match options. See (H).\n\nAlso reachable and DFA-specific in flavour: **`PCRE2_ERROR_RECURSELOOP` (-52)** at **2960-2967** (same group_num + same `ptr` + same `mb->last_used_ptr`); DFA has **no** `PCRE2_DISABLE_RECURSELOOP_CHECK` escape hatch (not in the option mask), unlike `pcre2_match`.\n\n# (D) Ovector semantics + RESTART protocol\n\nCore code, lines **861-894** (`OP_KET`/`OP_KETRMIN`/`OP_KETRMAX`/`OP_KETRPOS` with `code == end_code`):\n```c\nif (match_count < 0) match_count = (offsetcount >= 2)? 1 : 0;\n  else if (match_count > 0 && ++match_count * 2 > (int)offsetcount)\n    match_count = 0;\ncount = ((match_count == 0)? (int)offsetcount : match_count * 2) - 2;\nif (count > 0) (void)memmove(offsets + 2, offsets, (size_t)count * sizeof(PCRE2_SIZE));\nif (offsetcount >= 2)\n  { offsets[0] = current_subject - start_subject; offsets[1] = ptr - start_subject; }\n```\n- `offsetcount` = `match_data->oveccount * 2` (line 4033), rounded down to even at **568**.\n- **One start, many ends**: `offsets[2i]` is `current_subject` for *every* pair — the DFA reports a single start offset with N alternative end offsets. No capture-group data at all (`cb.capture_top = 1`, `cb.capture_last = 0`, line 3485-3486).\n- **Longest-first ordering** is a side effect of the insert-at-front `memmove`: because the subject is scanned left to right, each newly completed match is longer than all previous ones and is shifted into slot 0.\n- **oveccount == 0** → `offsetcount == 0` → first match sets `match_count = 0` → function returns **0**, nothing written. `PCRE2_ERROR_PARTIAL` also writes nothing (guarded by `match_data->oveccount > 0` at 4046).\n- **oveccount == 1** → one pair, the longest match only; return 1 while only one match exists, then 0 once a second (longer) one is found.\n- **small oveccount** → once overflowed, `match_count` sticks at 0 and each further match still shifts the whole vector (`count = offsetcount - 2`), so the vector always ends up holding the `oveccount` **longest** matches, and the return value is **0** (\"offsets overflowed; longest matches are present\", per header comment 3333-3336).\n- **large oveccount** → return value = number of distinct match lengths found.\n- `PCRE2_DFA_SHORTEST` (891) returns after the *first* recorded match → return 1, `ovector[0..1]` = shortest match.\n- `PCRE2_ERROR_PARTIAL` contents — **lines 4046-4050**: `ovector[0] = start_match - subject`, `ovector[1] = end_subject - subject` (i.e. the whole inspected tail, *not* the partial-match extent). Additionally 4052-4059 set `match_data->subject_length`, `start_offset`, `leftchar` (= `mb->start_used_ptr`), `rightchar` (= `mb->last_used_ptr`), `startchar` (= `start_match`). `match_data->mark` is always NULL (3690); `matchedby = PCRE2_MATCHEDBY_DFA_INTERPRETER` (3691); `match_data->rc = rc` (4124).\n- Partial decision logic, **3274-3294**: requires `new_count <= 0` AND `could_continue` AND (hard-partial OR (soft-partial AND `match_count < 0`)) AND (`partial_newline` OR (`ptr >= end_subject` AND (`ptr > mb->start_used_ptr` OR `mb->allowemptypartial`))). `mb->allowemptypartial` set at 3531-3532 from `re->max_lookbehind > 0 || (re->flags & PCRE2_MATCH_EMPTY)`.\n\n**RESTART protocol**\n- Caller must pass `PCRE2_DFA_RESTART` plus **the identical `workspace` vector, unmodified, with the same `wscount`**. Nothing else in the workspace is documented/needed — the state is entirely `workspace[0]`, `workspace[1]`, and the two stateblock vectors starting at `workspace + 2`.\n- `workspace[0]`: bit 0 only = which vector is \"current\" (set at 694 `= 0`, toggled at **719** `workspace[0] ^= 1`). `workspace[1]`: `active_count`, written every character at **720**.\n- Restart path, **668-674**: only at `rlevel == 1`; walks the top-level `OP_ALT` chain to find `end_code`; `new_count = workspace[1]`; if `workspace[0] == 0`, copies `new_count` stateblocks from `active_states` (`workspace+2`) into `new_states` (because the main loop swaps at 713-715 before using them).\n- Side effects: `anchored` forced TRUE (3467), therefore no bumpalong and `firstline` FALSE (3474); **all** start optimizations skipped (3709).\n- Also must be preserved by the caller: the pattern, and `start_offset` pointing at the continuation point (used by `OP_SOM`/`\\G` at 976 and NOTEMPTY_ATSTART at 878 via `mb->start_offset` = 3530). `match_data` need not be preserved.\n\n# (E) Start optimisations vs pcre2_match.c\n\nBlock: **3698-4019** (`for(;;)` bumpalong), gate at **3708-3709**. `pcre2_match.c` counterpart: 7632-7950, gate at 7625.\n\nSame machinery, differences:\n1. **Extra gate condition** (3709): `&& (options & PCRE2_DFA_RESTART) == 0`. pcre2_match.c:7625 has no such term.\n2. **Partial test spelled differently**: DFA uses `(mb->moptions & (PCRE2_PARTIAL_HARD|PCRE2_PARTIAL_SOFT)) == 0` (3855, 3912, 3924); pcre2_match uses `mb->partial == 0` (there is no `partial` field in `dfa_match_block`, `pcre2_intmodedep.h:1085-1110`).\n3. **Failure exits differ**: DFA does a bare `break` out of the bumpalong loop and falls into `NOMATCH_EXIT:` (4110-4114); pcre2_match sets `rc = MATCH_NOMATCH; break;`. The minlength test at **3933** uses `goto NOMATCH_EXIT` directly (pcre2_match uses `rc=MATCH_NOMATCH; break`).\n4. **memchr caches** `memchr_found_first_cu`/`memchr_found_first_cu2` are function-locals initialised once at 3361-3362 (8-bit only) — in pcre2_match they are reset at `FRAGMENT_RESTART` (7609-7612) because of invalid-UTF fragment restarts; DFA has no fragment loop.\n5. **No `mb->check_subject`**: DFA has no such field; lookbehind clamping uses a local `check_subject` only for UTF validation (3592) and lookbehinds are bounded by `start_subject` (616, 629, 1102) rather than a check_subject barrier.\n6. **No `true_end_subject`** and no invalid-UTF fragment machinery.\n7. Otherwise identical: `firstline` (3719-3735), anchored first-cu/bitmap probe (3741-3760), unanchored caseless double-memchr with caching (3766-3843), `startline` linebreak advance incl. CR/LF fudge (3863-3891), `start_bits` bitmap scan (3898-3915), `end_subject` restore (3920), `re->minlength` (3933), `req_cu` with `REQ_CU_MAX` / `REQ_CU_MAX*1000` heuristic and `req_cu_ptr` caching (3957-4011).\n8. `optimization_flags`/`PCRE2_NO_START_OPTIMIZE`: identical semantics — `PCRE2_NO_START_OPTIMIZE` clears `PCRE2_OPTIM_START_OPTIMIZE` at compile time (`pcre2_compile.c:10414-10415`); `(*NO_START_OPT)` also (`pcre2_compile.c:749`).\n9. `offset_limit`: 3503-3508 — requires compile-time `PCRE2_USE_OFFSET_LIMIT` else `PCRE2_ERROR_BADOFFSETLIMIT`; `bumpalong_limit` default `end_subject` (3475), tested at **4019** `if (start_match > bumpalong_limit) break;`. pcre2_match sets it unconditionally at 7400-7401 against `true_end_subject`.\n10. Bumpalong advance 4085-4106: `firstline && IS_NEWLINE` break, `ACROSSCHAR` for UTF, `start_match > end_subject` break, CR/LF skip gated on `(re->flags & PCRE2_HASCRORLF) == 0`.\n11. **DFA has no empty-match retry loop** — no re-run with `PCRE2_NOTEMPTY_ATSTART|PCRE2_ANCHORED` as pcre2_match does; empty matches are simply reported.\n\n# (F) Recursion / heap\n\n- **Recursion vehicle**: `internal_dfa_match` (529-540) calls itself for `OP_ASSERT`/`ASSERT_NOT`/`ASSERTBACK`/`ASSERTBACK_NOT` (2808-2818), assertion **conditions** (2907-2917), `OP_RECURSE` (2978-2988), possessive groups `OP_*BRAPOS*` (3067-3077, in a loop), `OP_ONCE` (3154-3164). Top-level call at **4027-4037** with `rlevel = 0`.\n- **`depth_limit` — honoured**, line **567**: `if (rlevel++ > mb->match_limit_depth) return PCRE2_ERROR_DEPTHLIMIT;` — this is the `internal_dfa_match` nesting depth. `depth_limit = 0` permits only the top level.\n- **`match_limit` — honoured but with different meaning**, line **566**: `if (mb->match_call_count++ >= mb->match_limit) return PCRE2_ERROR_MATCHLIMIT;` — counts **total invocations of `internal_dfa_match`**, and `mb->match_call_count` is zeroed only once at **3535**, i.e. *before* the bumpalong loop, so the budget is shared across all bumpalong positions. (`pcre2_match.c:873` uses the same counter name but counts `match()` entries.)\n- **`heap_limit` — honoured**, in `more_workspace` 420-457: `newsize = rws->size * 2` (with `UINT32_MAX` saturation, 437); clamp to `heap_limit - heap_used` in KiB (440-442); if the clamped size `< RWS_RSIZE + ovecsize + RWS_ANCHOR_SIZE` → **`PCRE2_ERROR_HEAPLIMIT` (-63)** (444-445). `mb->heap_used` in KiB, zeroed at 3536; `heap_limit` capped by `re->limit_heap` at 3523-3524.\n- **`PCRE2_ERROR_NOMEMORY` (-48) paths**: exactly two — **line 447** (`mb->memctl.malloc` for a new RWS block fails) and **line 4068** (`PCRE2_COPY_MATCHED_SUBJECT` subject copy fails).\n- **RWS structure**: `RWS_anchor { next; uint32_t size; uint32_t free; }` (332-336), `RWS_ANCHOR_SIZE` (338). Base block is **on the C stack**: `int base_recursion_workspace[RWS_BASE_SIZE]` = `DFA_START_RWS_SIZE/sizeof(int)` = 30720 bytes (3384-3388). Carve sizes: `RWS_RSIZE` = 1000 ints per recursive frame; `RWS_OVEC_OSIZE` = `2*OVEC_UNIT` (1 pair) for assertions/ONCE/BRAPOS; `RWS_OVEC_RSIZE` = `1000*OVEC_UNIT` (500 pairs) for `OP_RECURSE` (326-328, `OVEC_UNIT` at 323).\n- Carve/return pattern at every recursion site: `if (rws->free < RWS_RSIZE + ovec) more_workspace(...)`; `local_offsets = (PCRE2_SIZE *)(RWS + rws->size - rws->free)`; `local_workspace = ((int*)local_offsets) + ovec`; `rws->free -= RWS_RSIZE + ovec;` … `rws->free += RWS_RSIZE + ovec;` (2793-2804/2820, 2892-2903/2919, 2937-2954/2990, 3041-3053/3094, 3141-3152/3166).\n- **Blocks are chained and reused**: 426-429 reuses `rws->next` if present; the chain is freed only at **`EXIT:` 4117-4122**. Note that after `more_workspace` the local `RWS` pointer advances but the *caller's* `RWS` is unchanged, so unwinding naturally returns to the previous block.\n- Each recursive frame's own DFA workspace is `RWS_RSIZE = 1000` ints → `(1000-2)/6 = 166` states per vector; the caller's `wscount` is used **only** at rlevel 1.\n- **`pcre2_set_recursion_memory_management` is irrelevant/dead**: `pcre2_context.c:514-523` is a no-op stub since 10.30 (`(void)mymalloc; (void)myfree; return 0;`). DFA allocation goes through `mb->memctl` (= `mcontext->memctl` or `re->memctl`, 3496/3511) i.e. `pcre2_set_general_context`'s allocator. `pcre2_set_recursion_limit` is an alias for `pcre2_set_depth_limit` (`pcre2_context.c:508-511`).\n\n# (G) Callouts\n\n`do_callout_dfa` at **360-398**; invoked at **3248** (`OP_CALLOUT`/`OP_CALLOUT_STR`, extracode 0) and **2843** (`extracode = 1 + LINK_SIZE`, for the auto-callout inserted between `OP_COND` and an assertion condition).\n\n- `cb->version = 2` (3481). Set once at 3480-3487: `subject`, `subject_length`, `callout_flags = 0`, `capture_top = 1`, `capture_last = 0`, `mark = NULL`.\n- **Fields that differ from pcre2_match**:\n  - `cb->offset_vector = offsets` (376) — points at the **DFA match-length vector**, not a capture vector. Inside recursion it points at `local_offsets` in the RWS. `pcre2_match.c:285-299` sets it to the frame ovector with real capture data.\n  - `cb->capture_top` is **always 1**, `cb->capture_last` always 0 (3485-3486) — pcre2_match computes them (`pcre2_match.c:298-299`).\n  - `cb->mark` is **always NULL** (3487) — no `(*MARK)` support (and `OP_MARK` is a UITEM anyway).\n  - `cb->callout_flags` is **always 0** — DFA never sets `PCRE2_CALLOUT_STARTMATCH` (cf. `pcre2_match.c:7960`) nor `PCRE2_CALLOUT_BACKTRACK` (cf. `pcre2_match.c:6913`).\n  - `cb->start_match = current_subject - mb->start_subject`, `cb->current_position = ptr - mb->start_subject` (377-378); `pattern_position` / `next_item_length` read from the code (379-380); string-callout fields 391-394 (`callout_string = code + 1 + 4*LINK_SIZE + extracode + 1`, `callout_string_length = *lengthptr - (1+4*LINK_SIZE) - 2`).\n  - `if (mb->callout == NULL) return 0;` at **371** — but `*lengthptr` is computed first (367-369), so the opcode is still skipped correctly with no callout installed.\n- **Return-value handling**: at 3250-3252, `rrc < 0` → `return rrc` (abandons the whole match, including a callout returning `PCRE2_ERROR_NOMATCH` which propagates as a hard error/no-match up through the assertion machinery); `rrc == 0` → `ADD_ACTIVE(state_offset + callout_length, 0)`; `rrc > 0` → the state is simply not added, i.e. **only that DFA thread dies**, other threads continue (no \"backtrack\" semantics). In the COND path (2845-2847) `rrc > 0` → `break` (fail this thread).\n- **Auto-callout works** (`PCRE2_AUTO_CALLOUT`): callouts are `OP_CALLOUT` items in the code stream and are handled; the comment at 2835-2837 plus code at 2839-2848 exists specifically to cope with the auto-callout inserted before an assertion condition. Caveat for differential testing: because the DFA runs many threads in parallel and re-runs assertions/recursions via nested `internal_dfa_match`, a given callout can fire **more than once** per (start, subject position) and in an order unrelated to pcre2_match's; and callouts inside assertions see a `local_offsets` vector.\n\n# (H) UTF handling\n\n- `utf = (re->ove