ways the original `plength` (set once at convert_posix:171). Glob: `pattern - pattern_start` at the failure point (:1088); 0 for the UTF/separator pre-check (:871).\n\n## Glob converter `convert_glob` :846-1094\nSetup: `separator = ccontext->glob_separator`, `escape = ccontext->glob_escape` (:854-855); `no_wildsep = options & 0x30`, `no_starstar = options & 0x50` (:857-858); :867-874 `utf && (separator>=128 || escape>=128)` → `PCRE2_ERROR_CONVERT_SYNTAX (-64)`, `*bufflenptr=0` (unreachable via the public setters); :876 `with_escape = separator ∈ pcre2_escaped_literals` → true for `\\` and `.`, false for `/`.\nConstructs:\n1. Always emits leading `(?s)` (:883-887).\n2. `\\A` anchor emitted unless the pattern starts with `*` and (`no_wildsep`, or `**` with `!no_starstar`) (:891-905).\n3. `**` (only if `!no_starstar`) :921-988 — collapses a run of `*`; at end of pattern → `no_slash_z=TRUE`, break (:928-932); optional skip of `escape separator` after a separator (:936-938); at pattern start followed by separator → `(?:\\A|<sep>)` (:944-956), at start not followed by separator → `continue` (emits nothing, :942); otherwise `(*COMMIT)` (:959, helper :813-826) then either `.*?` (:961-968) or `(?:.*?<sep>)??` (:970-987).\n4. single `*` :990-1032 — collapses runs; `no_wildsep` + end → `no_slash_z`, break; `no_wildsep` + is_start → nothing; if not at start: `(?>` opening an atomic group when the previous item was `**` (`after_starstar`, closed at :1077-1078 / :915-919) else `(*COMMIT)`; then `.` (no_wildsep) or `[^<sep>]` via `convert_glob_print_wildcard` :474-485; then quantifier `*?`, or `*+` if at end of pattern (:1027-1031).\n5. `?` :1035-1042 → `.` when `no_wildsep`, else `[^<sep>]`.\n6. `[...]` → `convert_glob_parse_range` :637-804: `!` or `^` as first char → negated class `[^` plus the separator inserted into the negated set unless `no_wildsep` (:657-685); `]` immediately after `[`/`[!` is a literal `\\]` (:692-700); ranges `a-z` (:747-778) with `prev_c > c` → `PCRE2_ERROR_CONVERT_SYNTAX`, and `[:class:]` used as a range endpoint → `PCRE2_ERROR_CONVERT_SYNTAX` (:762-766); escape char inside the class consumes the next char (:757-761, :781-787); `[ ] \\ -` are backslash-escaped on output (:793-795); on `]` closing a *positive* class that can match the separator (and `!no_wildsep`) a `(?<!<sep>)` lookbehind is appended (:711-721); running off the end → `PCRE2_ERROR_MISSING_SQUARE_BRACKET (106)` (:651-655, :662-666, :802-803).\n   POSIX classes: `convert_glob_parse_class` :499-551 recognises exactly the 14 names in `posix_classes` :110-124 (alpha, lower, upper, alnum, ascii, blank, cntrl, digit, graph, print, punct, space, word, xdigit); malformed → returns 0 and the `[` is treated literally. Separator membership is decided by `convert_glob_char_in_class` :563-621 against **`PRIV(default_tables)` cbits**, not the context tables.\n7. escape char (default `\\`) :1052-1060 — consumes and literalises the next char; escape as the final char → `PCRE2_ERROR_CONVERT_SYNTAX`.\n8. Any other char :1062-1065 — backslash-escaped iff in `pcre2_escaped_literals` :94-99 = ``\\ ? * + | . ^ $ { } [ ] ( )``.\n9. Trailing `\\z` unless `no_slash_z` (:1070-1075), close pending atomic group (:1077-1078), NUL (:1080). Non-dummy overflow check :1082-1083 → `PCRE2_ERROR_NOMEMORY`. Success: `*bufflenptr = out.output_size - 1` (:1092).\nNote: a leading `/` (or any separator) is emitted literally (escaped if in escaped_literals, i.e. `.`/`\\` yes, `/` no); `.` in a glob has no special meaning (plain literal, escaped in output). Only errors reachable: -64, -48, 106.\n\n## POSIX converter `convert_posix` :149-384 (`pattype`, `extended = pattype & POSIX_EXTENDED` :163)\n- Always prefixes `(*NUL)` (`STR_STAR_NUL` :64, emitted :172) so the newline convention of the generated pattern is NUL.\n- Character class body handled by the state machine :204-246 with states `POSIX_CLASS_NOT_STARTED/STARTING/STARTED` (:68-69): `[[:alpha:]]` etc. are copied through verbatim (`:]` emitted at :224), a `\\` inside a class is doubled (:241), `]` ends the class (:206-210). Unterminated class → `PCRE2_ERROR_MISSING_SQUARE_BRACKET (106)` (:378-379). `[[:<:]]`/`[[:>:]]` support is `#ifdef NEVER` (:255-277), i.e. absent.\n- `[` outside a class :252-300: emits `[`, then passes a leading `^` and/or leading `]` through verbatim.\n- `\\` :302-315: at end of pattern → `PCRE2_ERROR_END_BACKSLASH (101)`. ERE: `nextisliteral=TRUE` (next char loses meta meaning, `sc=0` at :199). BRE: if next char ∈ `posix_meta_escapes` :103-106 = `( ) { } 1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8 9` then it is *unescaped* into a metacharacter — `\\(`→`(`, `\\)`→`)`, `\\{`→`{`, `\\}`→`}` — except digits, which are re-escaped as backrefs `\\1`..`\\9` (:308); anything else → literal.\n- `)` :317-320: special only in ERE and only when `bracount > 0`, else escaped literal; `(` :322-323 increments bracount (BRE reaches ESCAPE_LITERAL via :331).\n- `? + { } |` :326-331: special in ERE, escaped literal in BRE.\n- `.` and `$` :334-341: always copied as-is (BRE's \"`$` only special at end\" rule is **not** emulated).\n- `*` :343-351: consecutive `*`s collapsed (:351); in BRE a `*` at start of regex/after `(` is an escaped literal (:346-348).\n- `^` :353-361: ERE → always special; BRE → special only at start of regex or right after `(` (sets POSIX_ANCHORED), otherwise falls through to escaped literal.\n- default :363-374: escaped iff in `pcre2_escaped_literals`; multi-unit UTF chars copied by `memcpy` of `clength` units.\n- Buffer overflow anywhere → `PCRE2_ERROR_NOMEMORY` (PUTCHARS macro :73-80 and :242/:309/:339/:370). Success: `*bufflenptr = convlength` (:381), NUL written at :382. In a dummy run `p` is rewound to `use_buffer` each item (:186), so the 100-byte dummy buffer suffices.\n- Never returns `PCRE2_ERROR_CONVERT_SYNTAX`.\n\n`void pcre2_converted_pattern_free(PCRE2_UCHAR *converted)` :1250-1259 — NULL-safe; otherwise reads the hidden `pcre2_memctl` at `converted - sizeof(pcre2_memctl)` and calls its `free`. **Only valid for buffers allocated by the two-call protocol**; calling it on a caller-supplied buffer is UB.\n\n# (C) pcre2_serialize.c\n\nHeader format: `pcre2_serialized_data` (pcre2_internal.h:2169-2174) = `{uint32 magic; uint32 version; uint32 config; int32 number_of_codes;}` = 16 bytes. `SERIALIZED_DATA_MAGIC 0x50523253` (:52); `SERIALIZED_DATA_VERSION = MAJOR | (MINOR<<16)` = `10 | (48<<16)` = **0x0030000A** (:57-58); `SERIALIZED_DATA_CONFIG = sizeof(PCRE2_UCHAR) | (sizeof(void*)<<8) | (sizeof(PCRE2_SIZE)<<16)` = `1 | 8<<8 | 8<<16` = **0x00080801** on LP64 (:60-61).\nStream layout: `[hidden pcre2_memctl (24B, before the returned pointer)] [16B header] [1088B tables] [code0 blocksize bytes] … [codeN-1]`. `*serialized_size = 16 + 1088 + Σ blocksize` (does **not** include the hidden memctl, though the malloc does: :107).\n\n`int32_t pcre2_serialize_encode(const pcre2_code **codes, int32_t number_of_codes, uint8_t **serialized_bytes, PCRE2_SIZE *serialized_size, pcre2_general_context *gcontext)` :69-153\n- memctl = `gcontext->memctl` else `PRIV(default_compile_context).memctl` (:82-83) — a NULL gcontext is fine.\n- :85-86 `codes==NULL || serialized_bytes==NULL || serialized_size==NULL` → `PCRE2_ERROR_NULL (-51)`.\n- :88 `number_of_codes <= 0` (0 and negative) → `PCRE2_ERROR_BADDATA (-29)`.\n- :96 any `codes[i]==NULL` → `PCRE2_ERROR_NULL`; :98 `magic_number != MAGIC_NUMBER` → `PCRE2_ERROR_BADMAGIC (-31)`; :99-102 second and later codes whose `re->tables` **pointer** differs from the first → `PCRE2_ERROR_MIXEDTABLES (-30)`. (Same-content-different-pointer, e.g. one code from `pcre2_code_copy_with_tables` or two separate `pcre2_maketables` calls, still triggers MIXEDTABLES; all default-table codes share `PRIV(default_tables)` so they are fine.)\n- :107-108 malloc fail → `PCRE2_ERROR_NOMEMORY (-48)`.\n- :140-145 zeroes `memctl`, `tables`, `executable_jit` inside each copied code so output is deterministic.\n- Success returns `number_of_codes` (>0). N=1 and N=large behave identically; note there is no upper bound check.\n\n`int32_t pcre2_serialize_decode(pcre2_code **codes, int32_t number_of_codes, const uint8_t *bytes, pcre2_general_context *gcontext)` :160-260\nChecks in order (:176-181): `bytes==NULL || codes==NULL` → `PCRE2_ERROR_NULL`; `number_of_codes <= 0` → `PCRE2_ERROR_BADDATA`; `data->number_of_codes <= 0` → `PCRE2_ERROR_BADSERIALIZEDDATA (-62)`; magic mismatch → `PCRE2_ERROR_BADMAGIC`; version mismatch → `PCRE2_ERROR_BADMODE (-32)`; config mismatch → `PCRE2_ERROR_BADMODE` (this is what catches a 16/32-bit or different-pointer-size stream; there is no per-code width check).\n- :183-184 `number_of_codes > data->number_of_codes` → **clamped** to the serialized count and that (smaller) value is returned. `number_of_codes` smaller than serialized → only that many decoded, that many returned; caller array must have room for exactly `min(number_of_codes, data->number_of_codes)` entries; `codes` must be pre-allocated by the caller (it is never allocated here).\n- :191-196 one shared 1088-byte tables copy is allocated with `TABLES_LENGTH + sizeof(PCRE2_SIZE)`, refcount word set to the number of decoded codes; malloc failure → `PCRE2_ERROR_NOMEMORY`.\n- Per code: :207-213 blocksize read via memcpy (unaligned-safe); `blocksize <= sizeof(pcre2_real_code)` → `PCRE2_ERROR_BADSERIALIZEDDATA`; :217-223 `memctl_malloc(blocksize, gcontext)` failure → `PCRE2_ERROR_NOMEMORY`; :229-235 after copy, `magic_number != MAGIC_NUMBER`, or `name_entry_size > MAX_NAME_SIZE + IMM2_SIZE + 1` (= 128+2+1 = 131), or `name_count > MAX_NAME_COUNT` (10000) → `PCRE2_ERROR_BADSERIALIZEDDATA`.\n- :239-241 sets `tables`, `executable_jit=NULL`, `flags |= PCRE2_DEREF_TABLES` (0x40000) so `pcre2_code_free` refcounts the shared tables.\n- `cleanup:` :250-259 frees the partially-built code, the tables, and all previously stored `codes[j]` (setting them to NULL), then returns the error.\n- Success returns the number of decoded codes (>0).\n\n`int32_t pcre2_serialize_get_number_of_codes(const uint8_t *bytes)` :267-278 — NULL → `PCRE2_ERROR_NULL`; bad magic → `PCRE2_ERROR_BADMAGIC`; bad version/config → `PCRE2_ERROR_BADMODE`. **No `<=0` check**, so a hand-crafted header with 0 or a negative count is returned verbatim (differs from decode, which gives -62).\n\n`void pcre2_serialize_free(uint8_t *bytes)` :285-293 — NULL-safe; otherwise `free`s `bytes - sizeof(pcre2_memctl)` via the hidden memctl. Must only be used on encode output.\n\n# (D) pcre2_config.c\n\n`int pcre2_config(uint32_t what, void *where)` :70-248.\n`where == NULL` path (:73-103): the 14 listed numeric requests return `sizeof(uint32_t)` = **4**; `JITTARGET`, `UNICODE_VERSION`, `VERSION` `break` and fall into the main switch; anything else → `PCRE2_ERROR_BADOPTION (-34)`.\nMain switch (`where != NULL`) writes a `uint32_t` and returns **0**, except the three string requests which return `1 + strlen`.\n\n| request | id | line | value in this build |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `PCRE2_CONFIG_BSR` | 0 | :110-116 | `PCRE2_BSR_UNICODE` = **1** (BSR_ANYCRLF undef) |\n| `PCRE2_CONFIG_JIT` | 1 | :144-150 | **0** |\n| `PCRE2_CONFIG_JITTARGET` | 2 | :152-161 | **`PCRE2_ERROR_BADOPTION (-34)`** for both `where==NULL` and `where!=NULL` (no-JIT branch) |\n| `PCRE2_CONFIG_LINKSIZE` | 3 | :163-165 | `CONFIGURED_LINK_SIZE` = **2** |\n| `PCRE2_CONFIG_MATCHLIMIT` | 4 | :167-169 | **10000000** |\n| `PCRE2_CONFIG_NEWLINE` | 5 | :171-173 | `NEWLINE_DEFAULT` = **2** (LF) |\n| `PCRE2_CONFIG_PARENSLIMIT` | 6 | :183-185 | **250** |\n| `PCRE2_CONFIG_DEPTHLIMIT` (= RECURSIONLIMIT 7) | 7 | :132-134 | **10000000** |\n| `PCRE2_CONFIG_STACKRECURSE` | 8 | :190-192 | **0** (obsolete) |\n| `PCRE2_CONFIG_UNICODE` | 9 | :209-215 | **1** |\n| `PCRE2_CONFIG_UNICODE_VERSION` | 10 | :198-207 | writes `\"17.0.0\"` + NUL, returns **7** (`where==NULL` → 7 too) |\n| `PCRE2_CONFIG_VERSION` | 11 | :236-243 | `XSTRING(Z PCRE2_PRERELEASE)[1] == '-' != 0` → second branch → **`\"10.48-DEV 2025-10-21\"`** (20 chars),