 → emit nothing. Applies only when `special == 0`. |\n| UNKNOWN_UNSET | 1191 (`$+` with top_bracket==0), 1258 (numeric group > top_bracket: skip remaining digits), 1371–1374 (name not in nametable → `group = top_bracket+1`), 1407–1411 (maps `NOSUBSTRING` → `UNSET`) | Converts \"no such group\" into \"unset group\". **Does not by itself suppress the error** — you still get `PCRE2_ERROR_UNSET` unless UNSET_EMPTY is also set. Never affects `PCRE2_ERROR_UNAVAILABLE` (1412). |\n| OVERFLOW_LENGTH | 649 (CHECKMEMCPY), 675 (CHECKCASECPY_BASE), 1748–1755 | Instead of immediate `NOROOM`, sets `overflowed=TRUE`, accumulates `extra_needed`, and finally returns `PCRE2_ERROR_NOMEMORY` with `*blength = buff_length + extra_needed`. Also suppresses the substitute_callout (1652/1686). |\n| LITERAL | 1054–1057 | `CHECKMEMCPY(replacement, rlength)` verbatim; no `$`, no `\\`, no case forcing. Takes precedence over EXTENDED. Callout still fires. |\n| MATCHED | 824, 827, 840–872, 898–917, 979–983 | See protocol below. |\n| REPLACEMENT_ONLY | 825, 965, 1045, 1669, 1735–1739 | Suppresses: prefix copy up to `start_offset`, inter-match text, the trailing subject tail, and (1669) the restore-original-text on callout rejection. |\n\n## Inherited match options\n`pcre2_substitute` does **no** validation of the residue; `pcre2_match` does (`src/pcre2_match.c` 7045–7046 vs `PUBLIC_MATCH_OPTIONS` 71–76).\n\n- **Accepted**: `PCRE2_ANCHORED`, `PCRE2_ENDANCHORED`, `PCRE2_NOTBOL`, `PCRE2_NOTEOL`, `PCRE2_NOTEMPTY`, `PCRE2_NOTEMPTY_ATSTART`, `PCRE2_NO_UTF_CHECK`, `PCRE2_PARTIAL_HARD`, `PCRE2_PARTIAL_SOFT`, `PCRE2_NO_JIT`, `PCRE2_COPY_MATCHED_SUBJECT`, `PCRE2_DISABLE_RECURSELOOP_CHECK`.\n- **REJECTED → `PCRE2_ERROR_BADOPTION` (-34)**: everything else, notably `PCRE2_DFA_RESTART` (0x40) and `PCRE2_DFA_SHORTEST` (0x80), plus any unassigned bit. Error comes from `pcre2_match` at 984 → 996 `goto EXIT`.\n- Extra `BADOPTION` from `pcre2_match` 7111–7113: `PARTIAL_*` together with `ENDANCHORED` (compile or match).\n- `PCRE2_NO_UTF_CHECK` (938–946) also gates the UTF validity check of the *replacement* string (`PRIV(valid_utf)`); on failure `match_data->startchar` is set and the UTF error code (-3..-23) is returned. After the first `pcre2_match`, `NO_UTF_CHECK` is force-set (987–989).\n- `PCRE2_COPY_MATCHED_SUBJECT` is cleared at 921 whenever an internal match_data is used (i.e. `match_data==NULL` or MATCHED), so it is only honoured for a caller-supplied non-MATCHED match_data.\n\n## Partial matching\n- 759: `partial = (options & (PARTIAL_HARD|PARTIAL_SOFT)) != 0` — computed from the *option bits*, not from the match result.\n- 796–797: `partial && !REPLACEMENT_ONLY` → **`PCRE2_ERROR_BADOPTION`**, returned before anything else (`*blength` already `PCRE2_UNSET` from 779).\n- An actual partial match: `pcre2_match` returns `PCRE2_ERROR_PARTIAL` (-2) → 994 (not NOMATCH) → 996 `goto EXIT` → **-2 returned**, `*blength == PCRE2_UNSET`.\n- **`PCRE2_ERROR_PARTIALSUBS` (-76)**: 1153–1157 for `$'` and 1170–1174 for `$_` — triggered purely by the option bit. `` $` `` is *allowed* in partial mode.\n\n## SUBSTITUTE_MATCHED protocol\nPre-existing match_data required; `match_data == NULL` → `PCRE2_ERROR_NULL` (-51) at 827.\nChecks in order (840–872):\n1. 845–846: `match_data->rc < 0 && != PCRE2_ERROR_NOMATCH` → return `match_data->rc` verbatim (so a stored `PCRE2_ERROR_PARTIAL` propagates as -2).\n2. 849–850: `matchedby == PCRE2_MATCHEDBY_DFA_INTERPRETER` → `PCRE2_ERROR_DFA_UFUNC` (-41).\n3. 852–853: `code != match_data->code` (pointer identity) → **`PCRE2_ERROR_DIFFSUBSPATTERN` (-71)**.\n4. 859–864: `length != match_data->subject_length` OR NOT (`original_subject == match_data->subject` OR (`PCRE2_MD_COPIED_SUBJECT` set AND (`length==0` OR `memcmp` equal))) → **`PCRE2_ERROR_DIFFSUBSSUBJECT` (-72)**. `original_subject` (762) is captured *before* the NULL→`null_str` swap, so NULL/0 vs NULL/0 compares equal.\n5. 866–867: `start_offset != match_data->start_offset` → **`PCRE2_ERROR_DIFFSUBSOFFSET` (-73)**.\n6. 869–871: `(options & ~(SUBSTITUTE_OPTIONS|PCRE2_NO_UTF_CHECK)) != (match_data->options & ~PCRE2_NO_UTF_CHECK)` → **`PCRE2_ERROR_DIFFSUBSOPTIONS` (-74)**. `match_data->options` is `original_options` as passed to `pcre2_match` (`pcre2_match.c` 6980, 8171). Note `PCRE2_COPY_MATCHED_SUBJECT`, `NO_JIT`, `ANCHORED`, `ENDANCHORED`, `DISABLE_RECURSELOOP_CHECK` **are** part of the comparison; only `NO_UTF_CHECK` and the substitute bits are exempt. Consequence: any option bit rejected by `pcre2_match` can never be in `match_data->options`, so MATCHED + a bad option yields DIFFSUBSOPTIONS, not BADOPTION.\n\nThen 898–917: an internal match_data of the *same* `oveccount` is created and `memcpy`'d for `offsetof(ovector) + 2*pairs*sizeof(PCRE2_SIZE)` where `pairs = min(top_bracket+1, oveccount)`; `heapframes`/`heapframes_size` zeroed; `PCRE2_MD_COPIED_SUBJECT` cleared. The external block is never modified. `pcre2_match_data_create` failure → `PCRE2_ERROR_NOMEMORY` (909).\nFirst loop iteration (979–983) uses `match_data->rc`; `use_existing_match` cleared. Stored `PCRE2_ERROR_NOMATCH` → 994 break → 0 substitutions, plain copy of subject.\n\n## Other whole-function errors\n| Error | Line | Trigger |\n|---|---|---|\n| `PCRE2_ERROR_NULL` -51 | 804 | `replacement == NULL && rlength != 0` |\n| `PCRE2_ERROR_NULL` -51 | 815 | `subject == NULL && length != 0` |\n| `PCRE2_ERROR_NOMEMORY` -48 | 895 | internal match_data create failed |\n| `PCRE2_ERROR_BADOFFSET` -33 | 956–960 | `start_offset > length` |\n| `PCRE2_ERROR_BADSUBSPATTERN` -60 | 1001–1005 | `ovector[1] < ovector[0]` or `ovector[0] < start_offset` (`\\K` moving the match start back) |\n| `PCRE2_ERROR_INTERNAL_DUPMATCH` -65 | 1015–1023 | LCOV-excluded progress assertion |\n| `PCRE2_ERROR_TOOMANYREPLACE` -61 | 1032–1036 | `subs == INT_MAX` |\n| `PCRE2_ERROR_TOOLARGEREPLACE` -70 | 1779–1781 | `PCRE2_SIZE` overflow in length accumulation (643, 695, 723, 1701, 1752) |\n| `PCRE2_ERROR_REPLACECASE` -69 | 1775–1777 | case callout returned `~(PCRE2_SIZE)0` (708) |\n\nSide effect (1766–1768): when the caller-supplied match_data is used directly (no internal block, i.e. `match_data != NULL && !MATCHED`), `match_data->rc = rc` — the substitute return code overwrites the match rc.\n\n`NULL`/zero-length normalisation: `replacement==NULL,rlength==0` → `null_str` (802–806); `rlength==PCRE2_ZERO_TERMINATED` → `PRIV(strlen)` (808); same for subject (813–819).\n\n---\n\n# (B) Replacement mini-language\n\nThree modes: **LITERAL** (whole string verbatim, 1054), **non-extended** (only `$`), **EXTENDED** (`$` + `\\`).\n`escaped_literal` is declared at **function scope (754)**, not per-iteration ⇒ an unterminated `\\Q` leaks into the next GLOBAL iteration, making the whole replacement literal from then on. Good differential case: pattern `a`, subject `aa`, replacement `\\Q$1`, GLOBAL|EXTENDED.\n\n## `$` forms — parsed in BOTH non-extended and extended mode\n| Syntax | Lines | Behaviour / min. example |\n|---|---|---|\n| `$` at end | 1110 | `BADREPLACEMENT` — `\"$\"` |\n| `$$` | 1111 | one literal `$` — `\"$$\"` |\n| `$&` | 1126–1131 | group 0 — `\"$&\"` |\n| `` $` `` | 1132–1150 | `subject[0 .. ovector[0]]` (pre-match). Allowed in partial mode — `` \"$`\" `` |\n| `$'` | 1132–1161 | `subject[ovector[1] .. length]`; partial → `PARTIALSUBS` — `\"$'\"` |\n| `$_` | 1165–1179 | whole subject; partial → `PARTIALSUBS` — `\"$_\"` |\n| `$+` | 1180–1217 | highest set group. `top_bracket==0`: `NOSUBSTRING` unless UNKNOWN_UNSET (then group 0 → UNSET_EMPTY? `continue` : `UNSET`). `oveccount < top_bracket+1` → `UNAVAILABLE`. All unset → UNSET_EMPTY? skip : `UNSET` — `\"$+\"` |\n| `$+{name}` | 1180–1181 excluded | falls to name reader at `+` → `BADREPLACEMENT` — `\"$+{a}\"` |\n| `$n` | 1242–1270 | decimal run, arbitrary length. `group > top_bracket` → `NOSUBSTRING`, or with UNKNOWN_UNSET skip remaining digits — `\"$1\"`, `\"$0\"` (whole match), `\"$99\"` |\n| `${n}` | 1219–1224, 1316–1323 | `\"${1}\"`; missing `}` → `REPMISSINGBRACE` (`\"${1\"`) |\n| `$name` | 1271–1280 (`read_name_subst`) | unbraced maximal `ctype_word` run — `\"$a\"` |\n| `${name}` | as above | `\"${a}\"`; `\"${}\"` → `BADREPLACEMENT` (empty name, 252); name > `MAX_NAME_SIZE`=128 (`src/config.h` 223) → `BADREPLACEMENT` (248) |\n| `$<name>` | 1225–1233, 1326–1331 | JS syntax; **names only** — digit branch skipped by `!inangle` (1242), so `\"$<1>\"` → nametable lookup → `NOSUBSTRING`. Missing `>` → `BADREPLACEMENT` (`\"$<a\"`). `*` not allowed (`\"$<*MARK>\"` → BADREPLACEMENT) |\n| `$*MARK`, `${*MARK}` | 1235–1240, 1336–1354 | `pcre2_get_mark`; length from `mark[-1]`. `mark==NULL` → emits nothing, no error. Name != `\"MARK\"` (case-sensitive `strcmp_c8`) → `BADREPLACEMENT` (`\"${*mark}\"`) |\n\n## `${name:…}` — EXTENDED only (1288–1324)\nGate: `EXTENDED && !star && ptr < repend - 2 && *ptr == ':'` (1290–1291) — **requires ≥3 code units remaining** from the `:`.\n| Syntax | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `${1:-def}` | group set → group text; unset → `def` **reprocessed** (1426–1447) |\n| `${1:+set:unset}` | set → `set`; unset → `unset`; both reprocessed |\n| `${1:+set}` | unset → `text2 = NULL..NULL` → empty |\n| `${1:x}` | `special` not `+`/`-` → **`BADSUBSTITUTION` (-59)** (1294–1298) |\n| `${1:}` | only 2 units left → else branch → `*ptr==':'` → **`REPMISSINGBRACE` (-58)** |\n| `${1:-x}` w/o EXTENDED | else branch → `REPMISSINGBRACE` |\n| `${1:-\\d}` | `find_text_end` → `check_escape` error → **`BADREPESCAPE` (-57)** (137) |\n| `${1:-x` | `find_text_end` hits end → **`REPMISSINGBRACE`** (175) |\n| `${*MARK:-x}` | `!star` fails → else branch → `REPMISSINGBRACE` |\n| nesting >10 deep | `ptrstackptr >= PTR_STACK_SIZE`(=20, 2 slots/level) → **`BADREPLACEMENT`** (1433) |\n\n`find_text_end` (76–180) tracks `${` nesting (104–111), `\\Q…\\E` literal spans (87–94, 152–153), skips `\\L \\l \\U \\u` (120–128), treats bare `\\E` and `\\g` leniently (149, 156–163), accepts data chars and negative (group-ref) returns, and rejects any other positive `ESC_` → `BADREPESCAPE` (165–171).\n\n## `\\` forms — EXTENDED only (1472–1613)\nRecognised *before* `check_escape` (1478–1520), each requires `ptr < repend - 1`:\n| Syntax | Lines | Result |\n|---|---|---|\n| `\\L` | 1480–1484 | `CASE_LOWER`, single_char FALSE |\n| `\\l` | 1486–1497 | `CASE_LOWER`, single_char TRUE; if immediately followed by `\\U` **and `ptr+2 < repend`** → `CASE_REVERSE_TITLE_FIRST`, single_char FALSE |\n| `\\U` | 1499–1503 | `CASE_UPPER`, single_char FALSE |\n| `\\u` | 1505–1516 | `CASE_TITLE_FIRST`, single_char TRUE; if immediately followed by `\\L` **and `ptr+2 < repend`** → `CASE_TITLE_FIRST`, single_char FALSE |\n| `\\E` | 1549–1550 | `goto SETFORCECASE` with `{NONE,FALSE}` → cancels case forcing |\n\n**Off-by-one worth testing**: the `\\l\\U` / `\\u\\L` fusion needs ≥1 code unit *after* the second escape. `\"\\u\\L\"` alone is *not* fused (benign), but `\"${1:+\\u\\L}rest\"` behaves differently from the fused form because `repend` is the fragment end.\n\nThen `PRIV(check_escape)(&ptr, repend, &ch, &errorcode, code->overall_options, code->extra_options, code->top_bracket, FALSE, NULL)` (1543–1544). `cb == NULL` filter (`pcre2_compile.c` ~1610–1618): among table-zero characters only digits, `c`, `o`, `x`, `g` are permitted; all others → `ERR3` → **`BADREPESCAPE`**. `alt_bsux` is forced FALSE.\n\n| Syntax | Result | Min. string |\n|---|---|---|\n| `\\n \\r \\t \\f \\a \\e` | 0x0A 0x0D 0x09 0x0C 0x07 0x1B (escapes table, `pcre2_compile.c` 404–414) | `\"\\\\n\"` |\n| `\\b` `\\v` | remapped: backspace 0x08, VT 0x0B (1557–1561) | `\"\\\\b\"` |\n| `\\0` | octal, 1–3 digits → embedded NUL in output | `\"\\\\0\"` |\n| `\\12` | Perl disambiguation (`pcre2_compile.c` ~1893–1928): backref if `s<10 \\|\\| c>='8' \\|\\| s<=top_bracket`, else octal ⇒ `\\12` is octal 0x0A when <12 capture groups | `\"\\\\12\"` |\n| `\\x41`, `\\x{41}` | data char; UTF-encoded by `ord2utf` if UTF (1564) | `\"\\\\x41\"` |\n| `\\x` alone / `\\xg` | `ERR78` → `BADREPESCAPE` | `\"\\\\x\"` |\n| `\\x{}` | `ERR78` → `BADREPESCAPE` | `\"\\\\x{}\"` |\n| `\\x{41` | `ERR67` → `BADREPESCAPE` | `\"\\\\x{41\"` |\n| `\\x{110000}` (UTF) / `\\x{100}` (non-UTF 8-bit) | `ERR34` → `BADREPESCAPE` | `\"\\\\x{110000}\"` |\n| `\\x{d800}` (UTF) | `ERR73` → `BADREPESCAPE` | `\"\\\\x{d800}\"` |\n| `\\o{101}` | octal data char | `\"\\\\o{101}\"` |\n| `\\o` (no brace) | `ERR55` → `BADREPESCAPE` | `\"\\\\o\"` |\n| `\\o{}` | `ERR78`; `\\o{8}` → `ERR64` | `\"\\\\o{}\"` |\n| `\\o{400}` non-UTF 8-bit | `ERR34` → `BADREPESCAPE` | `\"\\\\o{400}\"` |\n| `\\cA` | 0x01; `\\c` at end → `ERR2`; `\\c` + non-printable-ASCII → `ERR68` | `\"\\\\c\"` |\n| `\\$` `\\\\` `\\{` etc. | literal (outside `['0'..'z']` or positive self-mapping table entry) | `\"\\\\$\"` |\n| `\\Q…\\E` | 1552–1554 + 1088–1097; `\\Q` sets `escaped_literal`, `\\E` clears it (consumes 2 units) | `\"\\\\Qa$1\\\\E\"` |\n| `\\1` … | negative return → `group = -rc - 1` → GROUP_SUBSTITUTE (1604–1610) | `\"\\\\1\"` |\n| `\\g<name>` | ESC_g → 1578–1602: requires `<`, `read_name_subst`, `>`; any failure → `BADREPESCAPE` | `\"\\\\g<a>\"` |\n| `\\g<0>` | `-(0+1)` from check_escape → group 0 (only place `\\g<0>` is legal) | `\"\\\\g<0>\"` |\n| `\\g` (no `<`) | `ERR57` → `BADREPESCAPE` | `\"\\\\g\"` |\n| `\\g<1` | `ERR119` → `BADREPESCAPE` | `\"\\\\g<1\"` |\n| `\\d \\s \\w \\A \\Z \\K \\k \\R \\X \\h \\H \\V \\W \\D \\S \\B \\C \\N \\p \\P \\z \\G` | positive `ESC_` → `default:` 1604/1611 → `BADREPESCAPE` | `\"\\\\d\"` |\n| `\\F \\I \\J \\M \\O \\T \\Y \\i \\j \\m \\q \\y` | `ERR3` → `BADREPESCAPE` | `\"\\\\q\"` |\n| `\\N{U+41}` | `cb==NULL` → `ERR37` → `BADREPESCAPE` | `\"\\\\N{U+41}\"` |\n| `\\` at end | `ptr >= ptrend` → `ERR1` → `BADREPESCAPE` | `\"\\\\\"` |\n| `\\d` non-extended | literal `\\` then literal `d` (1617–1631) | `\"\\\\d\"` |\n| `\\$1` non-extended | literal `\\` then `$1` substitution | `\"\\\\$1\"` |\n\n## Group-substitution error branches (GROUP_SUBSTITUTE, 1361–1463)\n- name lookup via `pcre2_substring_nametable_scan` (1370): `NOSUBSTRING` → UNKNOWN_UNSET? `group = top_bracket+1` : propagate `NOSUBSTRING`. `NOUNIQUESUBSTRING` cannot occur here (`firstptr != NULL`). Duplicate names: first entry with `ng < ovector_count` that is set; else first in-ovector; else `GET2(first,0)` (1379–1396).\n- `pcre2_substring_length_bynumber` (1404): `NOSUBSTRING` (+UNKNOWN_UNSET → `UNSET`), `UNAVAILABLE` (**never** converted, 1412 → returned as-is), `UNSET`, `PCRE2_ERROR_PARTIAL`.\n- Plain substitution + `UNSET`: UNSET_EMPTY ? `continue` : `PCRE2_ERROR_UNSET` (-55) (1413–1417).\n- `NOMEMORY`/`TOOMANYREPLACE`/`TOOLARGEREPLACE`/`REPLACECASE` per (A)/(C).\n\nAll replacement-parse errors exit via `PTREXIT` (1790–1792) which sets **`*blength = ptr - replacement`** (a byte offset into the replacement string, generally pointing just past the offending construct).\n\n---\n\n# (C) Buffer-length semantics\n\n- 777–779: `buff_offset = 0; lengthleft = buff_length = *blength; *blength = PCRE2_UNSET;` — `*blength` is an in/out parameter and is clobbered to `PCRE2_UNSET` immediately, before the `partial`/`NULL` checks.\n- The terminating zero is **always** written and always counted: 1741–1742 `temp[0]=0; CHECKMEMCPY(temp,1);`.\n- **Success** (1760–1764): `rc = subs; *blength = buff_offset - 1` — length **excluding** the terminating zero. The zero *is* in the buffer at `buffer[*blength]`.\n- **`PCRE2_ERROR_NOMEMORY` without OVERFLOW_LENGTH** (`NOROOM`, 1771–1773): `*blength` stays `PCRE2_UNSET`.\n- **`PCRE2_ERROR_NOMEMORY` with OVERFLOW_LENGTH** (1748–1755): `*blength = buff_length + extra_needed` = total code units required **including** the terminating zero. Exact, because at the overflow point `buff_offset + lengthleft == buff_length` and `extra_needed = chunk - lengthleft` (651), with all later chunks added in full.\n- **Two-call idiom therefore**: call 1 returns `N` = size including NUL; call 2 with `*blength = N` succeeds and reports `N-1`.\n- Off-by-one cases:\n  - `*blength == required` (incl. NUL) → success, `*blength` set to `required-1`.\n  - `*blength == required - 1` (one short) → the final `CHECKMEMCPY(temp,1)` fails → `NOMEMORY`; `*blength` = `PCRE2_UNSET`, or `required` with OVERFLOW_LENGTH (`extra_needed == 1`).\n  - `*blength == 0` → **always** `NOMEMORY` (even for empty output, since the NUL needs 1 unit). With OVERFLOW_LENGTH, `*blength = extra_needed` = exact required size.\n  - `buffer == NULL` is **never checked**. It is safe only if no `memcpy` executes, i.e. `*blength == 0` with OVERFLOW_LENGTH (also note 932 stores it into `scb.output`, and the substitute_callout is skipped while `overflowed`). `buffer==NULL` with `*blength > 0` is UB.\n- Pessimism caveats on the OVERFLOW_LENGTH figure:\n  - With a `substitute_case_callout`, `DELAYEDFORCECASE` (714–737) uses `pessimistic_case_inflation(len) = (len>>3)+10` (289–293) — an estimate, documented (283–287) as possibly requiring more than two calls.\n  - With a `substitute_callout`, the callout cannot be run while overflowed (1686–1709), so `max(oldlength, newlength)` is charged per match — the figure can be larger than actually needed.\n- Errors that leave `*blength == PCRE2_UNSET`: BADOPTION(797), NULL(804/815/827), NOMEMORY(895/909), UTF errors(944), BADOFFSET(959), BADSUBSPATTERN(1003), INTERNAL_DUPMATCH(1021), TOOMANYREPLACE(1034), NOROOM(1772), REPLACECASE(1776), TOOLARGEREPLACE(1780), DIFFSUBS*(853–871), DFA_UFUNC(850), and pass-through match errors (996).\n- Errors that set `*blength` to a replacement-string offset: all `PTREXIT` reachers (see B).\n\n---\n\n# (D) Case transformation\n\n## Callout protocol\nSetter (`src/pcre2_context.c` 465–474, no validation, always returns 0):\n```c\nint pcre2_set_substitute_case_callout(pcre2_match_context *mcontext,\n  PCRE2_SIZE (*cb)(PCRE2_SPTR input, PCRE2_SIZE input_len,\n                   PCRE2_UCHAR *output, PCRE2_SIZE output_cap,\n                   int to_case, void *data),\n  void *data);\n```\nStored in `pcre2_real_match_context` (`src/pcre2_intmodedep.h` 628–630); read in `pcre2_substitute` at 781–785.\n\n- `to_case` is only ever `PCRE2_SUBSTITUTE_CASE_LOWER` (1), `_UPPER` (2), `_TITLE_FIRST` (3) (`include/pcre2.h` 517–519). The internal `_NONE` (0, line 268) and `_REVERSE_TITLE_FIRST` (4, line 270) are **never** passed out — `do_case_copy` (443–605) decomposes them:\n  - `single_char` + LOWER/TITLE_FIRST (`\\l`, `\\u`) → one callout on the leading character with that `to_case`, then `memmove` of the remainder (496–497, 563–573).\n  - `REVERSE_TITLE_FIRST` (`\\l\\U`) → LOWER on the leading char + UPPER on the rest (500–503, 578–581).\n  - Plain LOWER/UPPER/TITLE_FIRST with `single_char==FALSE` → single callout on the whole fragment (485–494); TITLE_FIRST then degrades to LOWER for subsequent fragments (490–491).\n- **Return value** = number of code units the transformation requires. If `> output_cap` the callout must not write; the wrapper handles it. `~(PCRE2_SIZE)0` (== `PCRE2_UNSET`) means failure → **`PCRE2_ERROR_REPLACECASE` (-69)** (541, 582, 708, 1775–1777).\n- The callout may be called **repeatedly with identical input** while the wrapper grows `ch1_cap` from `ch1_len` up to `output_cap - rest_len` (529–561), `memmove`-ing the remainder rightwards each time. It must be deterministic-ish but the code tolerates non-determinism.\n- **Buffers may be the same / overlap** (in-place, `input_output` at 445, 451–452). The wrapper copies the first character to a local `ch1[6]` first (509–518) so the callout may scramble `output`.\n- Transformation is **deferred**: characters are first copied verbatim into `buffer`, then `DELAYEDFORCECASE()` (714–737) rewinds `buff_offset` to `casestart_offset` and re-runs in place. Triggered at a case-mode change (1532–1534) and after the whole replacement (1641–1643).\n- `default_substitute_case_callout` (297–434) additionally **asserts non-overlap** (320–321) — so the no-callout path only ever gets disjoint source (subject / `temp[]` / mark) and destination.\n\n## Internal default handling (no callout)\n`CHECKCASECPY_DEFAULT` (687–700) → `default_substitute_case_callout`:\n- `input_len == 0` → return 0 (328).\n- State machine (330–358): LOWER/UPPER set `next_to_upper = rest_to_upper`; TITLE_FIRST → first upper, rest lower, state becomes LOWER; REVERSE_TITLE_FIRST → first lower, rest upper, state becomes UPPER; `single_char` → state becomes NONE after the first character (356–358), remainder `memcpy`'d verbatim (416–430).\n- **Unicode path** (367–380): only when `(utf || ucp) && ch >= 128` — uses `UCD_CHARTYPE`/`PRIV(ucp_gentype)`/`UCD_OTHERCASE`, i.e. **simple 1:1 case folding only**. Explicit TODO at 375–379: SpecialCasing.txt is **not** supported (ß stays ß, ﬁ ligature unchanged, final sigma not handled), and \"not even correct for all the ordinary case mappings\".\n- **Non-Unicode / ASCII path** (383–389): `ch <= 255` uses `code->tables + cbits_offset + (cbit_upper|cbit_lower)` bit test then `code->tables + fcc_offset` (flip-case table). Note: in UTF mode, code points 0–127 also take this path, so locale tables govern ASCII.\n- Output re-encoding (391–397): `PRIV(ord2utf)` when `utf`, else a single code unit. In non-UTF 8-bit with UCP, `UCD_OTHERCASE` can return a value > 255 which is then truncated by `temp[0] = ch` — a real divergence trap.\n- Overflow accounting (399–412): once `overflow` is set it keeps counting; integer overflow → `~(PCRE2_SIZE)0`.\n- **Turkish casing is NOT implemented.** `PCRE2_EXTRA_TURKISH_CASING` (`include/pcre2.h` line ~163) is never read in `pcre2_substitute.c` (grep: zero hits); the TODO at 379 says so explicitly. So `\\U` on `i` yields `I` (not `İ`) even for a Turkish-casing pattern.\n\n## Where case forcing applies\n1346–1350 (`${*MARK}`), 1459–1463 (group / `$&` / `` $` `` / `$'` / `$_`), 1571–1575 (escape-produced data char), 1626–1630 (literal code unit). **Not** under `PCRE2_SUBSTITUTE_LITERAL` (1054–1057). `forcecase` is reset to `{NONE,FALSE}` at the top of **each global iteration** (975).\n\n---\n\n# (E) `pcre2_set_substitute_callout` protocol\n\nSetter (`src/pcre2_context.c` 455–462, no validation, returns 0): `int pcre2_set_substitute_callout(pcre2_match_context *, int (*)(pcre2_substitute_callout_block *, void *), void *)`.\n\n`pcre2_substitute_callout_block` (`include/pcre2.h` 616–626):\n| Field | Set at | Value |\n|---|---|---|\n| `uint32_t version` | 930 | 0 |\n| `PCRE2_SPTR input` | 931 | `subject` (post-`null_str` substitution) |\n| `PCRE2_SPTR output` | 932 | `(PCRE2_SPTR)buffer` — the original buffer pointer, captured **before** any writes |\n| `PCRE2_SIZE output_offsets[2]` | 1046 / 1655 | `[0]` = `buff_offset` before this replacement was expanded (i.e. after the pre-match text was copied); `[1]` = `buff_offset` after expansion + deferred case forcing |\n| `PCRE2_SIZE *ovector` | 933 | `pcre2_get_ovector_pointer(match_data)` — **live** pointer, holds the current match |\n| `uint32_t oveccount` | 1047 | `rc` from `pcre2_match` (pairs set), or `ovector_count` when `rc == 0` (ovector too small) — see 1043 |\n| `uint32_t subscount` | 1654 | `subs`, 1-based |\n\nTiming (1648–1675): after the entire replacement for this match is in the buffer **and** after the trailing `DELAYEDFORCECASE()` (1641–1643), before the GLOBAL advance. So `buffer[output_offsets[0] .. output_offsets[1])` is the expanded replacement text (case transformations already applied), and everything before `output_offsets[0]` is the accumulated output so far. There is **no** terminating NUL yet.\n\nReturn value:\n- **0** → keep the substitution.\n- **> 0** (any non-zero, 1662): rewind `buff_offset -= newlength; lengthleft += newlength` and, unless REPLACEMENT_ONLY, `CHECKMEMCPY(subject + ovector[0], ovector[1] - ovector[0])` — the original matched text is restored. With REPLACEMENT_ONLY nothing is emitted at all. `subs` is **not** decremented, so the function's return value counts rejected substitutions.\n- **< 0** (1671–1673): the same rewind/restore, **plus** `suboptions &= ~PCRE2_SUBSTITUTE_GLOBAL`, so the global loop ends after this iteration (1715).\n- The callout is **skipped entirely when `overflowed`** (1652, `else` 1686–1709): the length estimate charges `max(oldlength, newlength)` where `newlength = (buff_offset - output_offsets[0]) + (extra_needed - sub_start_extra_needed)`. Comment 1677–1684 documents that this is deliberate so that the 2-call OVERFLOW_LENGTH idiom cannot be defeated by a callout that changes its answer.\n\n---\n\n# (F) `pcre2_substring.c` — complete inventory\n\n**File:** `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-GdDnk6/translated_rust/c_src/src/pcre2_substring.c` (553 lines)\n\n### `pcre2_substring_copy_byname` — 68–91\n```c\nint pcre2_substring_copy_byname(pcre2_match_data *, PCRE2_SPTR stringname,\n                                PCRE2_UCHAR *buffer, PCRE2_SIZE *sizeptr);\n```\nBranches: 74–75 `matchedby == DFA` → `DFA_UFUNC` (-41). 76–78 `nametable_scan` < 0 → propagate (`NOSUBSTRING` -49; `NOUNIQUESUBSTRING` impossible, `firstptr != NULL`). 79 `failrc = UNAVAILABLE` (-54). 80–89 loop over duplicate entries stepping `entrysize`: first entry with `n < oveccount` **and** `ovector[n*2] != PCRE2_UNSET` → delegate to `copy_bynumber`; any in-range-but-unset sets `failrc = UNSET` (-55). 90 return `failrc`.\nInput shapes: name not in pattern → `NOSUBSTRING`; DUPNAMES with all copies ≥ `oveccount` → `UNAVAILABLE`; DUPNAMES with at least one in range but all unset → `UNSET`; DUPNAMES with several set → **first in nametable (i.e. lowest-numbered) set** one wins.\n\n### `pcre2_substring_copy_bynumber` — 116–130\n```c\nint pcre2_substring_copy_bynumber(pcre2_match_data *, uint32_t stringnumber,\n                                  PCRE2_UCHAR *buffer, PCRE2_SIZE *sizeptr);\n```\n122–123 `length_bynumber` first — its errors take precedence over the buffer check. 124 **`if (size + 1 > *sizeptr) return PCRE2_ERROR_NOMEMORY;`** → `*sizeptr` must be ≥ `size + 1`. 125–126 `memcpy` skipped