without consulting `match_data->rc`**, so on a partial match a stale non-`PCRE2_UNSET` slot can cause delegation to `length_bynumber`, which then returns `PCRE2_ERROR_PARTIAL` (-2) for `n > 0`.\n\n### `pcre2_substring_length_bynumber` — 311–352\n```c\nint pcre2_substring_length_bynumber(pcre2_match_data *, uint32_t stringnumber,\n                                    PCRE2_SIZE *sizeptr);\n```\nExact branch order:\n1. 316–321 `count = match_data->rc`; if `count == PCRE2_ERROR_PARTIAL`: `stringnumber > 0` → **`PCRE2_ERROR_PARTIAL` (-2)**; else `count = 0`.\n2. 322 else `count < 0` → return `count` (e.g. `PCRE2_ERROR_NOMATCH` -1).\n3. 324–332 non-DFA: `stringnumber > code->top_bracket` → **`NOSUBSTRING` (-49)**; `stringnumber >= oveccount` → **`UNAVAILABLE` (-54)**; `ovector[n*2] == PCRE2_UNSET` → **`UNSET` (-55)`**. **`NOSUBSTRING` is tested before `UNAVAILABLE`.**\n4. 333–337 DFA: `stringnumber >= oveccount` → `UNAVAILABLE`; `count != 0 && stringnumber >= count` → `UNSET`. (No `top_bracket` test ⇒ no `NOSUBSTRING` for DFA.)\n5. 341–349 `left > subject_length || right > subject_length` → `PCRE2_ERROR_INVALIDOFFSET` (-67), marked LCOV-unreachable.\n6. 350 `if (sizeptr != NULL) *sizeptr = (left > right) ? 0 : right - left;` — `sizeptr == NULL` is legal (existence probe); a `\\K`-inverted group yields length **0**, not an error.\n\nGroup 0 on a partial match: `count` becomes 0 and (non-DFA) `top_bracket >= 0`, `0 < oveccount`, `ovector[0] != PCRE2_UNSET` → returns the partial-match extent `ovector[1]-ovector[0]`.\n\n### `pcre2_substring_list_get` — 377–437\n```c\nint pcre2_substring_list_get(pcre2_match_data *, PCRE2_UCHAR ***listptr,\n                             PCRE2_SIZE **lengthsptr);\n```\n389 `rc < 0` → return `rc` (includes `PCRE2_ERROR_PARTIAL` -2 and `NOMATCH` -1). 390 `count == 0` (ovector too small) → `count = oveccount`. 392–401 size computation: header + `(count+1)` pointers + optional `count` lengths + per-group `(len + 1)` code units. 403–404 malloc failure → `NOMEMORY` (-48). 406–418 layout: `memctl | PCRE2_UCHAR*[count+1] | PCRE2_SIZE[count] (only if lengthsptr != NULL) | string data`. 420–433 per group: `size = (ovector[i+1] > ovector[i]) ? ovector[i+1]-ovector[i] : 0`, `memcpy` skipped when 0 (comment 424–426: avoids `subject + PCRE2_UNSET` overflow), always NUL-terminated. 435 final NULL pointer. No `matchedby` check ⇒ works for DFA. **Unset groups appear as empty strings with length 0**, indistinguishable from genuinely empty captures — the only way to tell them apart is the ovector. `lengthsptr == NULL` → no lengths array allocated and `*lengthsptr` untouched.\n\n### `pcre2_substring_list_free` — 450–458\n`void pcre2_substring_list_free(PCRE2_UCHAR **list);` NULL-safe (453); recovers `pcre2_memctl` at `list - sizeof(pcre2_memctl)`.\n\n### `pcre2_substring_nametable_scan` — 485–526\n```c\nint pcre2_substring_nametable_scan(const pcre2_code *code, PCRE2_SPTR stringname,\n                                   PCRE2_SPTR *firstptr, PCRE2_SPTR *lastptr);\n```\n489–492 binary chop over `code->name_count` entries of `code->name_entry_size`, table at `(const char *)code + sizeof(pcre2_real_code)`; each entry is `IMM2_SIZE` big-endian group number followed by the NUL-terminated name. 494–523 `PRIV(strcmp)` (zero-terminated, so a `stringname` containing an embedded NUL truncates). On hit, 506–515 expand `first`/`last` linearly to span all equal-named entries. 516–517 **`firstptr == NULL`** → `(first == last) ? (int)GET2(entry,0) : PCRE2_ERROR_NOUNIQUESUBSTRING` (-50). 518–520 else set `*firstptr`/`*lastptr`, return **`entrysize`** (= `name_entry_size`, a positive value used as the loop stride by the `_byname` functions). 525 not found → `PCRE2_ERROR_NOSUBSTRING` (-49).\nInput shapes: `name_count == 0` → `NOSUBSTRING` immediately (`top == bot == 0`). Duplicate name without `PCRE2_DUPNAMES` cannot be compiled, so `NOUNIQUESUBSTRING` requires `(?J)`/`PCRE2_DUPNAMES` **and** `firstptr == NULL`.\n\n### `pcre2_substring_number_from_name` — 546–551\n`int pcre2_substring_number_from_name(const pcre2_code *code, PCRE2_SPTR stringname);` → `nametable_scan(code, stringname, NULL, NULL)`. Returns the group number, `NOSUBSTRING` (-49), or `NOUNIQUESUBSTRING` (-50). Doc note (533–535) about undefined choice among duplicates is stale: the code returns `NOUNIQUESUBSTRING`, never an arbitrary number.\n\n### Cross-module notes\n- **No** function in `pcre2_substring.c` checks `match_data == NULL`, `code == NULL`, `stringname == NULL`, `buffer == NULL`, `listptr == NULL`, or `stringptr == NULL`. Only `length_bynumber`'s `sizeptr` may legally be NULL.\n- `pcre2_substitute` depends on two of these: `pcre2_substring_length_bynumber` (lines 1137 and 1404) and `pcre2_substring_nametable_scan` (line 1370) — so `NOSUBSTRING` / `UNAVAILABLE` / `UNSET` / `PARTIAL` / `NOUNIQUESUBSTRING` semantics are shared between the two files and must be kept consistent in any port."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":368,"cache_read_input_tokens":103898,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":368,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_017supyu2PYf7f22uKJcQtRE","session_id":"aeab5d90-512d-4436-80fd-a67670a151c9","uuid":"477737a6-4a00-4353-af1a-17ce49211c4f","timestamp":"2026-08-14T21:04:36.865Z","subagent_type":"Explore","task_description":"Analyze substitute and substring"}
