{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_boha3i3nqnz33flobsgeqquab6bxqb2cs2ejitserchwlro427ca","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# PCRE2 10.48 / 8-bit / SUPPORT_UNICODE / no-JIT — small-module analysis\n\nBase: `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-GdDnk6/translated_rust/c_src/src/`\nAll names use `PRIV(x)` = `_pcre2_x_8` in the built 8-bit library. `PCRE2_UCHAR`=`uint8_t`, `PCRE2_SPTR`=`const uint8_t *`, `PCRE2_SIZE`=`size_t`, `BOOL`=`int`, `LINK_SIZE`=2 (default), `IMM2_SIZE`=2.\nRelevant config: `config.h:66` → `/* #undef HAVE_BUILTIN_MUL_OVERFLOW */`; `pcre2_internal.h:182` → `INT64_OR_DOUBLE = int64_t`.\n\n---\n\n## 1. `_pcre2_is_newline` — pcre2_newline.c:74-141\n\n**Signature (verbatim, pcre2_newline.c:74-77; decl pcre2_internal.h:2329-2330):**\n```c\nBOOL\nPRIV(is_newline)(PCRE2_SPTR ptr, uint32_t type, PCRE2_SPTR endptr,\n  uint32_t *lenptr, BOOL utf)\n```\n`extern BOOL _pcre2_is_newline(PCRE2_SPTR, uint32_t, PCRE2_SPTR, uint32_t *, BOOL);`\n\n**State needed:** none. Pure. Preconditions from the `IS_NEWLINE` macro (`pcre2_internal.h:473-483`): `ptr < endptr`, and it is only called when `nltype != NLTYPE_FIXED`. `lenptr` must be writable.\n\n**`type` domain:** `NLTYPE_FIXED`=0, `NLTYPE_ANY`=1, `NLTYPE_ANYCRLF`=2 (`pcre2_internal.h:467-469`). Line 87 tests **only** `== NLTYPE_ANYCRLF`; every other value (including 0 and garbage) falls into the NLTYPE_ANY branch (line 103). PCRE2_NEWLINE_CR/LF/CRLF/NUL → NLTYPE_FIXED (handled inline, never reaches here); PCRE2_NEWLINE_ANY→1, PCRE2_NEWLINE_ANYCRLF→2 (`pcre2_compile.c:10681,10706,10710`; `pcre2_dfa_match.c:3541,3566,3570`).\n\n**Decode branch (line 80-85):** `utf=TRUE` → `GETCHAR(c,ptr)` (full UTF-8 decode, no advance) ; `utf=FALSE` → `c = *ptr` (one byte, so c ≤ 0xff).\n\n**Equivalence classes (8-bit, non-EBCDIC):**\n\n| # | type | utf | bytes at ptr | endptr | result | `*lenptr` | line |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n|1|2|any|`0x0A`|any|TRUE|1|89-91|\n|2|2|any|`0x0D 0x0A`|`ptr+2`|TRUE|2|93-95|\n|3|2|any|`0x0D 0x0A`|`ptr+1` (CR is last unit; LF not in subject)|TRUE|**1**|94|\n|4|2|any|`0x0D 0x41`|`ptr+2`|TRUE|1|94|\n|5|2|any|`0x0D`|`ptr+1` (CR at end)|TRUE|1|94|\n|6|2|any|`0x0B`/`0x0C`/`0x85`/`0x41`|any|FALSE|untouched|97-98|\n|7|1|any|`0x0A`, `0x0B` (VT), `0x0C` (FF)|any|TRUE|1|108-112|\n|8|1|any|`0x0D 0x0A`, `ptr<endptr-1`|—|TRUE|2|114-116|\n|9|1|any|`0x0D` at end / `0x0D`+non-LF|—|TRUE|1|115|\n|10|1|**FALSE**|raw byte `0x85`|—|TRUE|**1**|120-122|\n|11|1|**TRUE**|`0xC2 0x85` (NEL)|—|TRUE|**2**|120-122|\n|12|1|**TRUE**|`0xE2 0x80 0xA8` (U+2028 LS)|—|TRUE|**3**|124-127|\n|13|1|**TRUE**|`0xE2 0x80 0xA9` (U+2029 PS)|—|TRUE|**3**|126|\n|14|1|FALSE|any other byte, e.g. `0x41`, `0xE2`|—|FALSE|untouched|138-139|\n|15|1|TRUE|any other char, e.g. `a`, U+2027|—|FALSE|untouched|138-139|\n\nNote class 12/13 are **unreachable when `utf=FALSE`** (c is a single byte). `CHAR_NEL` = `(unsigned char)'\\x85'` (`pcre2_internal.h:679`).\nCRLF-split boundary is `ptr < endptr - 1` (strict): a CR whose LF lies at/after `endptr` yields length 1.\n\n**Black-box reach:** direct call (exported symbol). Indirect: `pcre2_compile()` with `PCRE2_NEWLINE_ANY|ANYCRLF` in the compile context and `(?x)`/`#`-comment scanning (`pcre2_compile.c:3463` `IS_NEWLINE(ptr)`), or `pcre2_match()`/`pcre2_dfa_match()` with `.` (OP_ANY, `pcre2_match.c:1062`), `$`/`\\Z` multiline, `firstline`. e.g. compile `\"a.b\"` with `PCRE2_NEWLINE_ANY` + `PCRE2_UTF`, subject `\"a\\xC2\\x85b\"` → no match (NEL is a newline, len 2).\n\n---\n\n## 2. `_pcre2_was_newline` — pcre2_newline.c:164-237\n\n**Signature (verbatim, 164-166; decl pcre2_internal.h:2346-2347):**\n```c\nBOOL\nPRIV(was_newline)(PCRE2_SPTR ptr, uint32_t type, PCRE2_SPTR startptr,\n  uint32_t *lenptr, BOOL utf)\n```\n`extern BOOL _pcre2_was_newline(PCRE2_SPTR, uint32_t, PCRE2_SPTR, uint32_t *, BOOL);`\n\n**State needed:** none. Precondition from `WAS_NEWLINE` (`pcre2_internal.h:487-497`): `ptr > startptr`. Line 169 does `ptr--` first; if `utf` then `BACKCHAR(ptr)` (walk back over 0x80-0xBF continuation bytes) then `GETCHAR` (lines 171-177).\n\n**Equivalence classes (positions relative to the *decremented/back-adjusted* `ptr`):**\n\n| # | type | utf | preceding bytes | result | `*lenptr` | line |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n|1|2|any|`...0x0D 0x0A` and `ptr > startptr`|TRUE|2 (CRLF)|186|\n|2|2|any|`0x0A` at `startptr` (no room for CR)|TRUE|**1**|186|\n|3|2|any|`0x41 0x0A`|TRUE|1|186|\n|4|2|any|`0x0D`|TRUE|1|189-191|\n|5|2|any|`0x0B`,`0x0C`,`0x85`,`0x41`|FALSE|untouched|193-194|\n|6|1|any|`0x0A` preceded by `0x0D`, `ptr>startptr`|TRUE|2|202|\n|7|1|any|`0x0A` at startptr or after non-CR|TRUE|1|202|\n|8|1|any|`0x0B` (VT), `0x0C` (FF), `0x0D` (CR)|TRUE|1|208-212|\n|9|1|FALSE|raw `0x85`|TRUE|**1**|216-218|\n|10|1|TRUE|`0xC2 0x85`|TRUE|**2**|216-218|\n|11|1|TRUE|`0xE2 0x80 0xA8` / `0xA9`|TRUE|**3**|220-223|\n|12|1|any|anything else|FALSE|untouched|234-235|\n\nCR-LF backwards check uses raw `ptr[-1] == CHAR_CR` (byte compare, not UTF-aware — safe because CR is ASCII and cannot be a UTF-8 continuation byte).\n\n**Black-box reach:** direct; or `pcre2_match()`/`pcre2_dfa_match()` with `^` in `PCRE2_MULTILINE` (`WAS_NEWLINE`) and `PCRE2_NEWLINE_ANY|ANYCRLF`, plus the \"advance to after next newline\" loops (`pcre2_dfa_match.c:3870,3878`). e.g. compile `\"^b\"` with `PCRE2_MULTILINE|PCRE2_NEWLINE_ANY|PCRE2_UTF`, subject `\"a\\xE2\\x80\\xA8b\"` → match at offset 4.\n\n---\n\n## 3. `_pcre2_valid_utf` — pcre2_valid_utf.c:92-315 (UTF-8 arm 100-315)\n\n**Signature (verbatim, 92-94; decl pcre2_internal.h:2345):**\n```c\nint\nPRIV(valid_utf)(PCRE2_SPTR string, PCRE2_SIZE length, PCRE2_SIZE *erroroffset)\n```\n`extern int _pcre2_valid_utf(PCRE2_SPTR, PCRE2_SIZE, PCRE2_SIZE *);`\n\n**State needed:** none. Pure. `erroroffset` must be writable; **it is NOT written on success** (line 315 returns 0 without touching it). `length` is a unit count, not NUL-terminated.\n\n`ab = PRIV(utf8_table4)[c & 0x3f]` (line 154; table `pcre2_tables.c:128-132`): lead `0xC0-0xDF`→ab=1, `0xE0-0xEF`→2, `0xF0-0xF7`→3, `0xF8-0xFB`→4, `0xFC-0xFD`→5.\n\n**Every error class (offset is always relative to `string`; error codes `include/pcre2.h:355-375`):**\n\n| err | val | trigger byte sequence (concrete) | length | offset returned | line |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n|ERR20|-22|`\"\\x80\"` (or any isolated `0x80`-`0xBF`), e.g. `\"a\\xBF\"`|1 / 2|index of the stray byte (0 / 1)|142-146|\n|ERR21|-23|`\"\\xFE\"` or `\"\\xFF\"`|1|index of byte|148-152|\n|ERR1|-3|`ab-length==1`: `\"\\xC2\"`; `\"\\xE0\\xA0\"`; `\"\\xF0\\x90\\x80\"`; `\"\\xF8\\x80\\x80\\x80\"`|1/2/3/4|index of lead byte|158-160|\n|ERR2|-4|`ab-length==2`: `\"\\xE0\"`; `\"\\xF0\\x90\"`; `\"\\xF8\\x80\\x80\"`; `\"\\xFC\\x80\\x80\\x80\"`|1/2/3/4|lead|161|\n|ERR3|-5|`ab-length==3`: `\"\\xF0\"`; `\"\\xF8\\x80\"`; `\"\\xFC\\x80\\x80\"`|1/2/3|lead|162|\n|ERR4|-6|`ab-length==4`: `\"\\xF8\"`; `\"\\xFC\\x80\"`|1/2|lead|163|\n|ERR5|-7|`ab-length==5`: `\"\\xFC\"`|1|lead|164|\n|ERR6|-8|2nd byte not `10xxxxxx`: `\"\\xC2\\x41\"`, `\"\\xE0\\x20\\xA0\"`, `\"\\xF0\\xC0\\x80\\x80\"`|≥2|lead (`p-string-1`)|171-175|\n|ERR7|-9|3rd byte bad; ab=2: `\"\\xE0\\xA0\\x41\"`; ab=3: `\"\\xF0\\x90\\x41\\x80\"`; ab=4: `\"\\xF8\\x88\\x41\\x80\\x80\"`; ab=5: `\"\\xFC\\x84\\x41\\x80\\x80\\x80\"`|—|lead (`-2`)|198-202 / 220-224 / 251-255 / 277-281|\n|ERR8|-10|4th byte bad; ab=3: `\"\\xF0\\x90\\x80\\x41\"`; ab=4: `\"\\xF8\\x88\\x80\\x41\\x80\"`; ab=5: `\"\\xFC\\x84\\x80\\x41\\x80\\x80\"`|—|lead (`-3`)|225-229 / 256-260 / 282-286|\n|ERR9|-11|5th byte bad; ab=4: `\"\\xF8\\x88\\x80\\x80\\x41\"`; ab=5: `\"\\xFC\\x84\\x80\\x80\\x41\\x80\"`|—|lead (`-4`)|261-265 / 287-291|\n|ERR10|-12|6th byte bad; ab=5: `\"\\xFC\\x84\\x80\\x80\\x80\\x41\"`|6|lead (`-5`)|292-296|\n|ERR11|-13|structurally valid 5-byte: `\"\\xF8\\x88\\x80\\x80\\x80\"` (ab==4)|5|lead (`p-string-ab`)|309-312|\n|ERR12|-14|structurally valid 6-byte: `\"\\xFC\\x84\\x80\\x80\\x80\\x80\"` (ab==5)|6|lead|309-312|\n|ERR13|-15|4-byte > U+10FFFF: `c>0xF4` → `\"\\xF5\\x80\\x80\\x80\"`; or `c==0xF4 && d>0x8F` → `\"\\xF4\\x90\\x80\\x80\"` (U+110000)|4|lead (`-3`)|235-239|\n|ERR14|-16|3-byte surrogate: `c==0xED && d>=0xA0` → `\"\\xED\\xA0\\x80\"` (U+D800), `\"\\xED\\xBF\\xBF\"` (U+DFFF)|3|lead (`-2`)|208-212|\n|ERR15|-17|overlong 2-byte: `(c&0x3E)==0` → `\"\\xC0\\x80\"`, `\"\\xC1\\xBF\"`|2|lead (`-1`)|186-190|\n|ERR16|-18|overlong 3-byte: `c==0xE0 && (d&0x20)==0` → `\"\\xE0\\x80\\x80\"`, `\"\\xE0\\x9F\\xBF\"`|3|lead (`-2`)|203-207|\n|ERR17|-19|overlong 4-byte: `c==0xF0 && (d&0x30)==0` → `\"\\xF0\\x80\\x80\\x80\"`, `\"\\xF0\\x8F\\xBF\\xBF\"`|4|lead (`-3`)|230-234|\n|ERR18|-20|overlong 5-byte: `c==0xF8 && (d&0x38)==0` → `\"\\xF8\\x80\\x80\\x80\\x80\"` (**reachable** despite the \"won't ever occur\" comment — checked before the `ab>3` test)|5|lead (`-4`)|266-270|\n|ERR19|-21|overlong 6-byte: `c==0xFC && (d&0x3C)==0` → `\"\\xFC\\x80\\x80\\x80\\x80\\x80\"`|6|lead (`-5`)|297-301|\n|**0**|0|`length==0` (any pointer, incl. non-NULL garbage); `\"abc\"`; `\"\\x7F\"`; `\"\\xC2\\x80\"` (U+80); `\"\\xDF\\xBF\"` (U+7FF); `\"\\xE0\\xA0\\x80\"` (U+800); `\"\\xEF\\xBF\\xBF\"` (U+FFFF); `\"\\xF0\\x90\\x80\\x80\"` (U+10000); `\"\\xF4\\x8F\\xBF\\xBF\"` (U+10FFFF)|—|**erroroffset untouched**|315|\n\nOrdering matters for tests: continuation-byte checks (ERR7/8/9/10) precede the overlong/range checks (ERR16/17/13/18/19) inside each `case`; the missing-byte checks (ERR1-5) precede ERR6; ERR11/ERR12 are only reached when the whole 5/6-byte form is structurally valid.\n\n**Black-box reach:** direct; or via `pcre2_compile()` with `PCRE2_UTF` and no `PCRE2_NO_UTF_CHECK` (`pcre2_compile.c:10628` → returns `PCRE2_ERROR_UTF8_ERRn` with `*erroroffset` set); `pcre2_match()` (`pcre2_match.c:7200,7347,8138`), `pcre2_dfa_match()` (`:3620`), `pcre2_substitute()` on the replacement (`pcre2_substitute.c:940`), `pcre2_pattern_convert()` (`pcre2_convert.c:1162`).\n\n---\n\n## 4. `_pcre2_ord2utf` — pcre2_ord2utf.c:77-95 (8-bit arm 82-94)\n\n**Signature (verbatim, 77-79; decl pcre2_internal.h:2336):**\n```c\nunsigned int\nPRIV(ord2utf)(uint32_t cvalue, PCRE2_UCHAR *buffer)\n```\n`extern unsigned int _pcre2_ord2utf(uint32_t, PCRE2_UCHAR *);`\n\n**State needed:** none (reads only the static `utf8_table1`/`utf8_table1_size`/`utf8_table2`). Caller must supply ≥6 bytes of buffer for arbitrary input; returns units written. **No validation whatsoever** (surrogates and >U+10FFFF are happily encoded).\n\n**Branch selector:** `for (i=0; i<utf8_table1_size(=6); i++) if ((int)cvalue <= utf8_table1[i]) break;` with `utf8_table1 = {0x7f,0x7ff,0xffff,0x1fffff,0x3ffffff,0x7fffffff}` (`pcre2_tables.c:114-117`). Note the **signed cast**.\n\n| cvalue | i | units | first byte mask (`utf8_table2[i]`) | return | example output |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n|`0x00`|0|1|0x00|1|`00`|\n|`0x41`|0|1|—|1|`41`|\n|**`0x7f`**|0|1|—|1|`7F`|\n|**`0x80`**|1|2|0xC0|2|`C2 80`|\n|**`0x7ff`**|1|2|0xC0|2|`DF BF`|\n|**`0x800`**|2|3|0xE0|3|`E0 A0 80`|\n|`0xD800` (surrogate)|2|3|0xE0|3|`ED A0 80` ← *emitted, not rejected*|\n|`0xDFFF`|2|3|—|3|`ED BF BF`|\n|**`0xffff`**|2|3|—|3|`EF BF BF`|\n|**`0x10000`**|3|4|0xF0|4|`F0 90 80 80`|\n|**`0x10ffff`**|3|4|0xF0|4|`F4 8F BF BF`|\n|`0x110000`..`0x1fffff`|3|4|0xF0|4|`F4 90 80 80` (invalid UTF-8, caller's fault)|\n|`0x200000`..`0x3ffffff`|4|5|0xF8|5|`F8 88 80 80 80`|\n|`0x4000000`..`0x7fffffff`|5|6|0xFC|6|`FC 84 80 80 80 80`|\n|`>= 0x80000000`|**0**|1|—|1|garbage single byte (signed compare makes `(int)cvalue` negative → i=0 on first iteration) — degenerate/UB-ish class|\n\n**Black-box reach:** direct; or `pcre2_compile()` with `PCRE2_UTF` on any literal/class range >0x7F (`pcre2_compile.c:6549,8459`; `pcre2_compile_class.c:1632-1654`), `pcre2_substitute()` case-transform output (`pcre2_substitute.c:392,1564`), `pcre2_match()` caseless othercase build (`pcre2_match.c:1410`), `pcre2_study`'s starting-byte computation (`pcre2_study.c:832,886,1000-1041,1232`). Concrete: compile `\"\\\\x{10ffff}\"` with `PCRE2_UTF` and check the compiled length / `pcre2_pattern_info(PCRE2_INFO_FIRSTBYTES)`.\n\n---\n\n## 5. String utilities — pcre2_string_utils.c\n\nAll are pure; no `cb`, no `pcre2_code`. Comparison result is always exactly `0`, `+1`, or `-1` via `((c1 > c2) << 1) - 1`.\n\n### `_pcre2_strcmp` — 63-74\n```c\nint\nPRIV(strcmp)(PCRE2_SPTR str1, PCRE2_SPTR str2)\n```\n`extern int _pcre2_strcmp(PCRE2_SPTR, PCRE2_SPTR);`\nLoop condition `*str1 != '\\0' || *str2 != '\\0'` (line 67).\nClasses: equal (`\"abc\"`,`\"abc\"`)→0; both empty (`\"\"`,`\"\"`)→0 (loop never entered); prefix (`\"ab\"`,`\"abc\"`)→**-1** (c1=0 vs 'c'); (`\"abc\"`,`\"ab\"`)→**+1**; differ at 0 (`\"b\"`,`\"a\"`)→+1; (`\"a\"`,`\"b\"`)→-1; empty vs non-empty (`\"\"`,`\"a\"`)→-1; high byte (`\"\\xFF\"`,`\"\\x01\"`)→+1 (unsigned compare, `PCRE2_UCHAR`=uint8_t); embedded NUL: the NUL is a terminator, `\"a\\0b\"` vs `\"a\\0c\"` → 0.\nReached publicly by `pcre2_substring_number_from_name()` / `pcre2_substring_get_byname()` / `..._copy_byname()` / `..._length_byname()` name lookup (`pcre2_substring.c:498,508,513`) and `(*SKIP:name)` handling at match time (`pcre2_match.c:6789`).\n\n### `_pcre2_strcmp_c8` — 91-102\n```c\nint\nPRIV(strcmp_c8)(PCRE2_SPTR str1, const char *str2)\n```\n`extern int _pcre2_strcmp_c8(PCRE2_SPTR, const char *);`\nIdentical logic; `str2` is `const char *` (a C literal). Note `c2 = *str2++` assigns a possibly-signed `char` into `PCRE2_UCHAR` (uint8_t) → literal bytes ≥0x80 compare as unsigned 0x80-0xFF. Same class list as `strcmp`.\nReached publicly by `\\p{...}` name lookup: `get_ucp()` at `pcre2_compile.c:2378-2393` (`bidiclass`/`bc`/`script`/`sc`/`scriptextensions`/`scx` prefixes) and the binary chop over `_pcre2_utt` at `:2417`; also `(*MARK)` name compare in `pcre2_substitute.c:1338`. Concrete: `pcre2_compile(\"\\\\p{Greek}\")`, `pcre2_compile(\"\\\\p{sc:Greek}\")`, `pcre2_compile(\"\\\\p{zzzz}\")` (→ ERR47).\n\n### `_pcre2_strncmp` — 118-129\n```c\nint\nPRIV(strncmp)(PCRE2_SPTR str1, PCRE2_SPTR str2, size_t len)\n```\n`extern int _pcre2_strncmp(PCRE2_SPTR, PCRE2_SPTR, size_t);`\n`for (; len > 0; len--)`.\nClasses: `len==0` → **0 immediately, no dereference at all** (safe with NULL/dangling pointers); equal over len; differ at first unit; differ at last unit; **NUL is NOT a terminator** — `(\"a\\0b\",\"a\\0c\",3)` → -1; comparing past a shorter string's NUL is defined here to read the bytes (caller must guarantee readability).\nReached publicly by duplicate-name / named-group lookup during `pcre2_compile()`: `pcre2_compile_cgroup.c:96,223,255`, `pcre2_compile.c:5731`. Concrete: `(?<ab>x)(?<ab>y)` (dup name error), `(?<n>a)\\k<n>`.\n\n### `_pcre2_strncmp_c8` — 147-158\n```c\nint\nPRIV(strncmp_c8)(PCRE2_SPTR str1, const char *str2, size_t len)\n```\n`extern int _pcre2_strncmp_c8(PCRE2_SPTR, const char *, size_t);`\nSame class list as `strncmp` (`len==0`→0 with no deref).\nReached publicly by POSIX class name lookup (`pcre2_compile.c:2554`), `\\b{start-of-word}`-style checks (`:3899-3900`), `\\Q...\\E` scan (`:4196`), verb-name lookup (`:4777,4898`), `(?(VERSION=` (`:5469`), `(?(DEFINE)` (`:5563`), and start-of-pattern `(*...)` options (`:10508`). Concrete: `[[:alpha:]]`, `(*UTF)a`, `(?(VERSION>=10.0)a|b)`, `(?(DEFINE)(?<x>a))`.\n\n### `_pcre2_strlen` — 170-176\n```c\nPCRE2_SIZE\nPRIV(strlen)(PCRE2_SPTR str)\n```\n`extern PCRE2_SIZE _pcre2_strlen(PCRE2_SPTR);`\nClasses: `\"\"`→0; `\"abc\"`→3; `\"a\\0b\"`→1 (stops at embedded NUL); high bytes counted as units not characters (`\"\\xC2\\x85\"`→2, i.e. code units, not UTF chars).\nReached publicly by passing `PCRE2_ZERO_TERMINATED` for a length: `pcre2_compile(pat, PCRE2_ZERO_TERMINATED, ...)` (`pcre2_compile.c:10396`), `pcre2_match`/`pcre2_dfa_match` subject (`pcre2_match.c:7052`, `pcre2_dfa_match.c:3404`), `pcre2_substitute` subject & replacement (`:808,819`), `pcre2_pattern_convert` (`pcre2_convert.c:1146`).\n\n### `_pcre2_strcpy_c8` — 190-197\n```c\nPCRE2_SIZE\nPRIV(strcpy_c8)(PCRE2_UCHAR *str1, const char *str2)\n```\n`extern PCRE2_SIZE _pcre2_strcpy_c8(PCRE2_UCHAR *, const char *);`\nCopies until NUL, always writes the terminating 0, returns count **excluding** it.\nClasses: `\"\"` → writes one `0`, returns 0; `\"abc\"` → writes `61 62 63 00`, returns 3; source with high bytes `\"\\x85\"` → 1 byte copied (truncating char→uint8_t); no bounds check on `str1`.\nReached publicly by `pcre2_config()` string queries in 8-bit mode: `PCRE2_CONFIG_JITTARGET` (`pcre2_config.c:157`), `PCRE2_CONFIG_UNICODE_VERSION` (`:206`), `PCRE2_CONFIG_VERSION` (`:242`). Concrete: `pcre2_config(PCRE2_CONFIG_UNICODE_VERSION, buf)` → writes `\"17.0.0\"`, returns 6.\n\n---\n\n## 6. `_pcre2_ckd_smul` — pcre2_chkdint.c:65-92\n\n**Signature (verbatim, 65-66; decl pcre2_internal.h:2325):**\n```c\nBOOL\nPRIV(ckd_smul)(PCRE2_SIZE *r, int a, int b)\n```\n`extern BOOL _pcre2_ckd_smul(PCRE2_SIZE *, int, int);`\n\n**Semantics:** modelled on C23 `ckd_mul`. Returns `TRUE` **if the operation overflows** (and `*r` is then *not* stored), `FALSE` on success with `*r = a*b`. Note the inverted-looking polarity: TRUE = failure.\n\n**Which body compiles here:** `HAVE_BUILTIN_MUL_OVERFLOW` is **undefined** in `config.h:66`, so lines 75-87 are active: `INT64_OR_DOUBLE m = (int64_t)a * (int64_t)b;` guarded by `PCRE2_ASSERT(a >= 0 && b >= 0)` (line 77) and then\n`if (sizeof(m) > sizeof(*r) && m > (INT64_OR_DOUBLE)PCRE2_SIZE_MAX) return TRUE;` (line 82).\n\n**Equivalence classes:**\n| # | (a,b) | on LP64 (`sizeof(size_t)==8`) | on ILP32 (`sizeof(size_t)==4`) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n|1 zero|(0,0), (0,7), (7,0)|FALSE, `*r=0`|FALSE, `*r=0`|\n|2 identity/small|(1,1), (3,5)|FALSE, `*r=15`|FALSE|\n|3 large no-overflow|(65535,65535)=4294836225|FALSE|FALSE (< SIZE_MAX=4294967295)|\n|4 \"overflow positive\"|(INT_MAX,INT_MAX)=4611686014132420609|**FALSE** — `sizeof(m)>sizeof(*r)` is false, so the guard short-circuits and the value is stored verbatim (no overflow is ever reported in the 64-bit build)|**TRUE**|\n|5 just over 2^32|(65536,65536)=4294967296|FALSE|**TRUE**|\n|6 negative operand|(-1,5), (-2,-3)|**assertion `a>=0 && b>=0` fires** in a `PCRE2_DEBUG`/assert build; with `NDEBUG` it computes `m=-5` and stores `(PCRE2_SIZE)(-5)` = SIZE_MAX-4 and returns FALSE (no overflow reported)|same|\n\nIf built with `HAVE_BUILTIN_MUL_OVERFLOW` (lines 68-73) semantics differ: `__builtin_mul_overflow(a,b,&m)` with unsigned `PCRE2_SIZE m` reports TRUE for any negative product and for any product exceeding SIZE_MAX. **This is the key portability/behaviour fork a Rust port must decide.**\n\n**Black-box reach:** direct; or `pcre2_compile()` with large bounded quantifiers on a group — `pcre2_compile.c:7477` (`replicate * length_prevgroup`), `:7647` (`(repeat_min-1) * ...`), `:7697` (`repeat_max * ...`). Concrete: `\"(?:abc){65535}\"`, `\"(?:(?:a{1000}){1000}){1000}\"` → `PCRE2_ERROR_PATTERNTOOLARGE` (ERR20/ERR75 path) when TRUE is returned.\n\n---\n\n## 7. `_pcre2_extuni` — pcre2_extuni.c:92-155\n\n**Signature (verbatim, 92-94; decl pcre2_internal.h:2326-2327):**\n```c\nPCRE2_SPTR\nPRIV(extuni)(uint32_t c, PCRE2_SPTR eptr, PCRE2_SPTR start_subject,\n  PCRE2_SPTR end_subject, BOOL utf, int *xcount)\n```\n`extern PCRE2_SPTR _pcre2_extuni(uint32_t, PCRE2_SPTR, PCRE2_SPTR, PCRE2_SPTR, BOOL, int *);`\n\n**State needed:** **no `cb`, no `pcre2_code`.** It needs: `c` = the already-consumed first character; `eptr` = pointer to the *next* character; **`start_subject`** (only used for the Regional-Indicator backwards walk, line 124) and **`end_subject`** (the loop bound, line 99 — yes, an `end` is required); `utf`; `xcount` may be NULL. Reads `PRIV(ucp_gbtable)` (`pcre2_tables.c:203-223`) and UCD via `UCD_GRAPHBREAK` → `_pcre2_ucd_records/stage1/stage2`.\n\n**Return:** pointer just past the grapheme cluster; `*xcount` incremented once per *additional* character consumed (line 151).\n\n**Equivalence classes (gb property values, `pcre2_ucp.h:204-218`):**\n1. `eptr == end_subject` → immediate return of `eptr`, no UCD lookup of a second char (e.g. `\\X` at end of subject).\n2. **Table denies join** (line 105) → break, cluster is 1 char. e.g. `c='a'` (gbOther=12, `gbtable[12]=ESZ`), next `'b'` (gbOther) → bit not set → return `eptr` unchanged.\n3. **CR+LF** (`gbtable[0] == 1<<gbLF`): `c=0x0D`, next `0x0A` → joins (len 2). `c=0x0D`, next `'a'` → breaks.\n4. **LF/Control left**: `gbtable[1]=0`, `gbtable[2]=0` → always break. `c=0x0A`, next anything → 1 char.\n5. **ESZ joins** (Extend|SpacingMark|ZWJ) after Other/Extend/SpacingMark/L/V/T/LV/LVT/ZWJ/EP: `\"a\"+U+0301` (Mn, gbExtend) → joins; `\"\\u0915\"+U+093E` (SpacingMark) → joins.\n6. **Hangul** (`gbtable[6..10]`): L+L, L+V, L+LV, L+LVT join; V+V, V+T join; LV+V, LV+T join; T+T, LVT+T join; **T+V breaks**, V+L breaks. e.g. `U+1100 U+1161 U+11A8` is one cluster.\n7. **Prepend left** (`gbtable[4]`): joins L,V,T,LV,LVT,Other,RI plus ESZ. e.g. `U+0600` + `'1'` → joins.\n8. **ZWJ + Extended_Pictographic with `was_ep_ZWJ` gate** (lines 110-111, 143): table allows it (`gbtable[13]` has the EP bit) but the code breaks unless the ZWJ itself was preceded by EP. Reach both sides: `U+1F468 U+200D U+1F469` (EP,ZWJ,EP) → all three join; `\"a\" U+200D U+1F469` → 'a'+ZWJ join, then break before the pictograph.\n9. **EP + Extend* + ZWJ** (line 148 keeps `lgb` at EP across `Extend`): `U+1F468 U+FE0F U+200D U+1F469` → all four join. This is the only place `lgb` is *not* updated to `rgb`.\n10. **Regional indicators, even count** (lines 116-138): `U+1F1FA U+1F1F8` (2 RIs) → joins. Backwards walk starts at `eptr-1` + `BACKCHAR` when `utf`.\n11. **Regional indicators, odd preceding count** → break: `U+1F1FA U+1F1F8 U+1F1FA` → the 3rd RI starts a new cluster (`ricount & 1`).\n12. **RI walk clipped by `start_subject`** (`while (bptr > start_subject)`): calling with `start_subject == eptr-4` truncates the count — distinct branch worth testing.\n13. `utf=FALSE` (line 103 `c = *eptr`, `len=1`): only single-byte chars; e.g. `c=0x0D`, next byte `0x0A` still joins. Also `utf=FALSE` skips `BACKCHAR` in the RI walk (line 120,127).\n14. `xcount == NULL` vs non-NULL (line 151).\n\n**Black-box reach:** direct; or `\\X` in a pattern — `pcre2_match.c:2898` (plain `\\X`), `:3249,4074,4663` (`\\X*`, `\\X{2,}`, backtracking), `pcre2_dfa_match.c:1574,1845,2127,2306`. Concrete: `pcre2_match` of pattern `\"\\\\X\"` with `PCRE2_UTF` against `\"e\\xCC\\x81\"` → match length 3; `\"\\\\X\"` against `\"\\xF0\\x9F\\x87\\xBA\\xF0\\x9F\\x87\\xB8\\xF0\\x9F\\x87\\xBA\"` → first match length 8 (two RIs), second match length 4.\n\n---\n\n## 8. `_pcre2_script_run` — pcre2_script_run.c:83-341\n\n**Signature (verbatim, 83-85; decl pcre2_internal.h:2337):**\n```c\nBOOL\nPRIV(script_run)(PCRE2_SPTR ptr, PCRE2_SPTR endptr, BOOL utf)\n```\n`extern BOOL _pcre2_script_run(PCRE2_SPTR, PCRE2_SPTR, BOOL);`\n(The header comment at line 63 calls the first argument `pgr`; the actual parameter is `ptr`.)\n\n**State needed:** none besides the UCD tables (`_pcre2_ucd_records/stage1/stage2` via `GET_UCD`, `_pcre2_ucd_script_sets` line 148, `_pcre2_ucd_digit_sets` lines 306-319). Local maps sized `FULL_MAPSIZE = ucp_Script_Count/32+1` and `UCD_MAPSIZE = ucp_Unknown/32+1` (lines 80-81). Character stepping uses `GETCHARINCTEST` → honours `utf` (in 8-bit non-UTF each byte is a character).\n\n**Equivalence classes:**\n1. `ptr >= endptr` (empty) → **TRUE** (line 99).\n2. Exactly one character → **TRUE** (line 101) — even if it is Unknown script.\n3. `script == ucp_Unknown` in a ≥2-char string → **FALSE** (line 132). e.g. U+0378 twice.\n4. **Common/Inherited with no Script Extensions** → skipped entirely for the script check (line 138, `UCD_SCRIPTX_PROP(ucd)==0 && (Inherited||Common)`), still subject to the digit check. e.g. `\"a-b\"`: `-` is Common → accepted with Latin.\n5. **Common/Inherited that DOES have extensions** → goes through full map processing (same line 138). e.g. U+3006, U+0640.\n6. `SCRIPT_UNSET` dispatch (lines 159-183): Han→`SCRIPT_HANPENDING`; Hiragana or Katakana→`SCRIPT_HANHIRAKATA`; Bopomofo→`SCRIPT_HANBOPOMOFO`; Hangul→`SCRIPT_HANHANGUL`; anything else→copy map, `SCRIPT_MAP`.\n7. `SCRIPT_HANPENDING` + another Han → no change (line 204).\n8. `SCRIPT_HANPENDING` + char with **none** of Bopomofo/Hiragana/Katakana/Hangul → **FALSE** (line 213). e.g. Han followed by Latin `\"漢a\"`.\n9. `SCRIPT_HANPENDING` + Bopomofo-only → `HANBOPOMOFO` (215-216); + exactly Hiragana|Katakana → `HANHIRAKATA` (217-218); + all four → stays pending (comment 220-221).\n10. `SCRIPT_HANHIRAKATA` (229-230) / `HANBOPOMOFO` (233-234) / `HANHANGUL` (237-238): FALSE if the char's map lacks the allowed set. e.g. Hiragana then Cyrillic → FALSE; Han+Hiragana `\"漢か\"` → TRUE; Han+Hangul `\"漢한\"` → TRUE; Hiragana then Hangul → FALSE.\n11. `SCRIPT_MAP` with empty intersection → **FALSE** (lines 247-256). e.g. `\"aα\"` (Latin + Greek).\n12. `SCRIPT_MAP` non-empty → narrows `require_map` by intersection (line 284), or transitions into one of the Han states (261-278).\n13. **Digit sets** (302-327): `chartype == ucp_Nd`. Fast path `c <= ucd_digit_sets[1]` (=0x39) → digitset 1; otherwise binary chop over `_pcre2_ucd_digit_sets`. First digit fixes `require_digitset`; a digit from a different set → **FALSE** (line 326). Concrete: `\"0\\u0662\"` (ASCII `0` + Arabic-Indic `٢`) → FALSE; `\"\\u0661\\u0662\"` (both Arabic-Indic) → TRUE; `\"12\"` → TRUE.\n14. `utf=FALSE` (8-bit): each byte is a code point; e.g. bytes `0x41 0x42` → TRUE, `0x41 0xE9` → depends on Latin-1 scripts (both Latin) → TRUE.\n\n**Black-box reach:** direct; or `pcre2_match()` on `(*script_run:...)` / `(*sr:...)` / `(*atomic_script_run:...)` / `(*asr:...)` — verb table `pcre2_compile.c:581-605`, opcode `OP_SCRIPT_RUN` (`:6903-6904`), interpreter call `pcre2_match.c:6481`. Concrete: `pcre2_match(compile(\"(*sr:\\\\w+)\", PCRE2_UTF|PCRE2_UCP), \"漢a\", ...)` → no match; `\"漢か\"` → match.\n\n---\n\n## 9. `_pcre2_xclass` — pcre2_xclass.c:66-441\n\n**Signature (verbatim, 66-68; decl pcre2_internal.h:2348):**\n```c\nBOOL\nPRIV(xclass)(uint32_t c, PCRE2_SPTR data, const uint8_t *char_lists_end, BOOL utf)\n```\n`extern BOOL _pcre2_xclass(uint32_t, PCRE2_SPTR, const uint8_t *, BOOL);`\n\n**There is no `caseless` parameter in 10.48.** Caselessness is fully expanded at compile time (`utf_caseless_extend()`, `pcre2_compile_class.c:153-205`), so a caseless XCLASS is just a bigger class. A Rust port must not invent a caseless flag.\n\n**State needed:** a **valid compiled XCLASS data pointer** — i.e. it points at the flag code unit, which is `code + 1 + LINK_SIZE` for an `OP_XCLASS` (see `pcre2_match.c:2296`: `Lxclass_data = Fecode + 1 + LINK_SIZE`). `char_lists_end` must be the **base for character-list offsets**; all real callers pass `(const uint8_t *)mb->start_code` / `cb->start_code` (`pcre2_match.c:2342`, `pcre2_dfa_match.c:2660`, `pcre2_auto_possess.c:1118`), i.e. the start of the compiled code block. No `cb` and no `pcre2_code` struct otherwise. In 8-bit mode line 77 forcibly sets `utf = TRUE`, so the `utf` argument is **ignored in the 8-bit library** (it still matters for 16-bit).\n\n**Data layout / flags** (`pcre2_internal.h:1481-1565`): `XCL_NOT=0x01`, `XCL_MAP=0x02`, `XCL_HASPROP=0x04`; item tags `XCL_END=0`, `XCL_SINGLE=1`, `XCL_RANGE=2`, `XCL_PROP=3`, `XCL_NOTPROP=4`, `XCL_LIST=0x10` (8-bit). Emission sites: `pcre2_compile_class.c:1229,1457` (props), `1648-1669` (`XCL_RANGE`/`XCL_SINGLE`), `1710` (`XCL_END`), `1713` (`XCL_NOT`), `1714` (`XCL_HASPROP`), `1729` (`XCL_MAP`).\n\n**Equivalence classes:**\n1. `not_negated = (*data & XCL_NOT) == 0` (line 71) — every \"matched\"/\"not matched\" return is XORed by this.\n2. **`XCL_MAP` set and `c < 256`** (82-85) → returns the raw bitmap bit **without applying XCL_NOT** (the map is pre-inverted at compile time). Critical asymmetry. e.g. `[\\x{100}a]` matching `'a'`.\n3. `XCL_MAP` set and `c >= 256` → skip 32 bytes (line 87) and continue.\n4. `XCL_MAP` clear → no bitmap at all; codes <256 go through the property/range machinery.\n5. **Property loop** (93-263), entered iff `*data` is `XCL_PROP` or `XCL_NOTPROP`; `isprop = (*data++)==XCL_PROP` (101); each iteration consumes 2 more units (`data += 2`, line 260) and loops while another PROP/NOTPROP follows (262). One class per `PT_*` case: `PT_LAMP` (106), `PT_GC` (112), `PT_PC` (117), `PT_SC` (121), `PT_SCX` (125, reads `_pcre2_ucd_script_sets`), `PT_ALNUM` (131), `PT_SPACE`/`PT_PXSPACE` (142-143, with the `HSPACE_CASES`/`VSPACE_CASES` sub-branch at 146-147 vs the `ucp_Z` default at 152), `PT_WORD` (158), `PT_UCNC` (166, sub-branch `c<0xa0` vs surrogate range at 175), `PT_BIDICL` (180), `PT_BOOL` (185, reads `_pcre2_ucd_boolprop_sets`), `PT_PXGRAPH` (203, with the Cf exceptions U+061C, U+180E, U+2066-2069), `PT_PXPRINT` (216, Cf exceptions U+061C, U+2066-2069 — **note U+180E differs from PXGRAPH**), `PT_PXPUNCT` (231, plus ASCII `S` for Perl compat), `PT_PXXDIGIT` (240, incl. fullwidth U+FF10-FF19/FF21-FF26/FF41-FF46). `default:` (254) is `PCRE2_DEBUG_UNREACHABLE()` + `return FALSE`.\n6. **Single/range list** taken when `*data < XCL_LIST` (269): loop until `XCL_END` (271). `XCL_SINGLE`: `c <= x` → `return (c==x) ? not_negated : !not_negated` (288) — *early exit exploiting sortedness*; `c > x` → `continue`. `XCL_RANGE`: `c <= y` → `return (c>=x)…` (304). Falling out of the loop at `XCL_END` → `return !not_negated` (307).\n7. **Character-list form** taken when `*data >= XCL_LIST` (310-441). 8-bit reads a 2-byte big-endian type word `(data[0]<<8)|data[1]` (311) then `next_char = char_lists_end - (GET(data,0) << 1)` (319). Sub-branches: `c >= XCL_CHAR_LIST_HIGH_16_START (0x8000)` → skip the Low16 list, shift type (325-337); `c < XCL_CHAR_LIST_LOW_32_START (0x10000)` → 16-bit search (339-375); else the 32-bit path (377-440). Within each: `max_index == XCL_ITEM_COUNT_MASK (3)` → inline count prefix (345-350 / 379-384 / 412-416); `max_index == 0 || c < first` → `return ((type & XCL_BEGIN_WITH_RANGE) != 0) == not_negated` (352-353 / 418-419); `c >= last` → (357-358 / 423-424); otherwise the binary search loop (363-374 / 429-440). Match test is `value == c || (value & XCL_CHAR_END) == 0`.\n\n**How patterns produce one:**\n- `[\\p{L}]` → `OP_XCLASS` with `XCL_HASPROP` + `XCL_PROP PT_GC ucp_L` (+ `XCL_MAP` bitmap for the <256 part, filled by `_pcre2_update_classbits`).\n- `[^\\x{100}]` → `XCL_NOT` set (`pcre2_compile_class.c:1713`) with `XCL_SINGLE 0x100`; whether a bitmap accompanies it depends on `XCLASS_HAS_8BIT_CHARS` (`:1729`).\n- `[\\x{100}-\\x{200}]` → `XCL_RANGE`.\n- A class with many ranges (e.g. `[\\x{100}-\\x{200}\\x{300}-\\x{400}\\x{500}\\x{600}…]`) crosses into the `XCL_LIST` character-list encoding — the only way to reach classes 7.\n- `[\\P{Greek}]` → `XCL_NOTPROP PT_SC ucp_Greek`.\n\n**Black-box reach:** `pcre2_match`/`pcre2_dfa_match` on such a class (`pcre2_match.c:2341,2366,2391`; `pcre2_dfa_match.c:2660`), and indirectly at *compile* time from `_pcre2_auto_possessify` (`pcre2_auto_possess.c:1117`).\n\n---\n\n## 10. `_pcre2_eclass` — pcre2_xclass.c:461-545\n\n**Signature (verbatim, 461-463; decl pcre2_internal.h:2349-2350):**\n```c\nBOOL\nPRIV(eclass)(uint32_t c, PCRE2_SPTR data_start, PCRE2_SPTR data_end,\n  const uint8_t *char_lists_end, BOOL utf)\n```\n`extern BOOL _pcre2_eclass(uint32_t, PCRE2_SPTR, PCRE2_SPTR, const uint8_t *, BOOL);`\n\n**State needed:** `data_start = code + 1 + LINK_SIZE` of an `OP_ECLASS`, `data_end = data_start + len` where `len` is derived from the opcode's link (`pcre2_match.c:2438-2440`); `char_lists_end` = `mb->start_code` (same as xclass); asserts `data_start < data_end` (470). Internal stack is a single `uint32_t` → max 32 operands deep, `stack_depth` only checked under asserts.\n\n**Opcode stream walked** (`pcre2_internal.h:1570-1582`): flags byte with `ECL_MAP=0x01`, then an RPN sequence of `ECL_AND=1`, `ECL_OR=2`, `ECL_XOR=3`, `ECL_NOT=4`, `ECL_XCLASS=5`. (`ECL_ANY=6`/`ECL_NONE=7` are compile-time only and would hit the `default: return FALSE` at 533-535.)\n\n**Equivalence classes:**\n1. `ECL_MAP` set and `c < 256` → bitmap-only answer, immediate return (478-482).\n2. `ECL_MAP` set and `c >= 256` → skip 32 bytes and walk the RPN (484).\n3. `ECL_MAP` clear → all code points walk the RPN.\n4. `ECL_XCLASS` (519-527): recurses into `PRIV(xclass)(c, ptr+1+LINK_SIZE, char_lists_end, utf)`, advances `ptr += GET(ptr,1)`, pushes the bit.\n5. `ECL_AND` (492): `stack = (stack>>1) & (stack | ~1u)`.\n6. `ECL_OR` (499): `stack = (stack>>1) | (stack & 1u)`.\n7. `ECL_XOR` (506): `stack = (stack>>1) ^ (stack & 1u)`.\n8. `ECL_NOT` (513): `stack ^= 1u` (unary, no depth change).\n9. Loop exit `ptr == data_end` → result is `(stack & 1u) != 0` (544); assert `stack_depth == 1`.\n10. Unknown tag → `default:` `PCRE2_DEBUG_UNREACHABLE(); return FALSE` (533-535).\n\n**How patterns produce one:** the `(?[ ... ])` extended class syntax, or `[ ... ]` with set operators when `PCRE2_ALT_EXTENDED_CLASS (0x08000000)` is set (`include/pcre2.h:143`; `pcre2_compile.c:3944,3962`). Operators map at `pcre2_compile_class.c:2493-2506` (note the De Morgan inversion: `META_ECLASS_OR` becomes `ECL_AND` in the negated arm). Emission: `:1895` (`ECL_NOT`), `:1982/2038/2101` (AND/OR/XOR), `:2261` (`ECL_XCLASS`), `:2755` (`ECL_MAP`).\nConcrete patterns: `(?[\\p{L} && \\p{Ll}])`, `(?[\\p{L} -- [aeiou]])`, `(?[\\p{L} ~~ \\p{Greek}])`, `(?[!\\p{L}])`, and `[\\p{L}&&\\p{Ll}]` compiled with `PCRE2_ALT_EXTENDED_CLASS`.\n\n**Black-box reach:** `pcre2_match` (`pcre2_match.c:2484,2509,2534`), `pcre2_dfa_match` (`:2671`), and at compile time via auto-possessification (`pcre2_auto_possess.c:1123`).\n\n---\n\n## 11. `_pcre2_update_classbits` — pcre2_compile_class.c:751-866\n\n**Signature (verbatim, 751-752; decl pcre2_compile.h:303-304, name macro `pcre2_compile.h:270`):**\n```c\nvoid PRIV(update_classbits)(uint32_t ptype, uint32_t pdata, BOOL negated,\n  uint8_t *classbits)\n```\n`void PRIV(update_classbits)(uint32_t ptype, uint32_t pdata, BOOL negated, uint8_t *classbits);`\n\n**State needed:** a writable **32-byte** bitmap; UCD tables. Bits are **OR-ed in** (line 863) — the caller owns initialisation. `classbits` is advanced every 8 code points (line 864), so a 32-byte buffer is mandatory.\n\n**Equivalence classes:**\n1. `ptype == PT_ANY` **and `!negated`** → `memset(classbits, 0xff, 32)`, return (760-763).\n2. `ptype == PT_ANY` **and `negated`** → returns leaving the map untouched (762 guard) — no-op class.\n3. Otherwise loops `c = 0..255` (766) with one branch per `ptype`: `PT_LAMP` (774), `PT_GC` (779), `PT_PC` (783), `PT_SC` (787), `PT_SCX` (791, `_pcre2_ucd_script_sets`), `PT_ALNUM` (796), `PT_SPACE`/`PT_PXSPACE` (801-802, with the `HSPACE_BYTE_CASES`/`VSPACE_BYTE_CASES` sub-branch — **byte cases only**, unlike `_pcre2_xclass` which uses the multibyte `HSPACE_CASES`), `PT_WORD` (816), `PT_UCNC` (823, includes `c >= 0xa0`), `PT_BIDICL` (828), `PT_BOOL` (832, `_pcre2_ucd_boolprop_sets`), `PT_PXGRAPH` (837), `PT_PXPRINT` (843), `PT_PXPUNCT` (849), and `default:` = `PT_PXXDIGIT` (854-858, asserted).\n4. `negated` inverts every bit before setting (862) — so `\\P{L}` sets all non-letter bits <256.\n5. Note lines 837-846: the <256 `PXGRAPH`/`PXPRINT` logic is *simpler* than the corresponding `_pcre2_xclass` cases (no U+061C/U+180E/U+2066-2069 carve-outs, since those are all >255) — a deliberate divergence to preserve.\n\n**Black-box reach:** compile-time only. `pcre2_compile_class.c:1221` (POSIX `[:graph:]`/`[:print:]`/`[:punct:]` in UCP mode) and `:1449` (`\\p`/`\\P` inside a class, `negated = (escape == ESC_P)`). Concrete patterns: `[[:graph:]]` with `PCRE2_UCP`, `[\\p{L}]`, `[\\P{Nd}]`, `[\\p{Any}]` (class 1), `[\\P{Any}]` (class 2). Observable via `pcre2_match` on single-byte subjects, or by dumping via pcre2test `-d`.\n\n---\n\n## 12. `_pcre2_find_bracket` — pcre2_find_bracket.c:66-215\n\n**Signature (verbatim, 66-68; decl pcre2_internal.h:2328):**\n```c\nPCRE2_SPTR\nPRIV(find_bracket)(PCRE2_SPTR code, BOOL utf, int number)\n```\n`extern PCRE2_SPTR _pcre2_find_bracket(PCRE2_SPTR, BOOL, int);`\n\n**State needed:** a **valid compiled-code pointer** into a `pcre2_code`'s code block (typically `codestart`), terminated by `OP_END`. No `cb`. Reads `PRIV(OP_lengths)`. `utf` must match how the pattern was compiled or the scan desynchronises (the `MAYBE_UTF_MULTI` block at 148-209).\n\n**Equivalence classes:**\n1. `OP_END` reached → **NULL** (line 73).\n2. `number >= 0` — find capture group N: matches `OP_CBRA`, `OP_SCBRA`, `OP_CBRAPOS`, `OP_SCBRAPOS` with `GET2(code, 1+LINK_SIZE) == number` (94-98). Sub-classes: found at the very first opcode; found after skipping other groups; number larger than any group → NULL. Note `number == 0` never matches a real CBRA (group numbering starts at 1) → scans to NULL.\n3. `number < 0` — **\"find any lookbehind\" mode**: returns the first `OP_REVERSE` or `OP_VREVERSE` (86-88). **No caller in the 10.48 tree passes a negative number** (only `pcre2_study.c:499,504,559,563` and `pcre2_compile.c:11048`, all with a group number) — so this branch is only reachable by a direct call to the exported symbol. Worth an explicit unit test since a port could silently drop it.\n4. Skips with a **length stored in the code**: `OP_XCLASS`/`OP_ECLASS` → `code += GET(code,1)` (81); `OP_CALLOUT_STR` → `code += GET(code, 1 + 2*LINK_SIZE)` (82).\n5. `OP_REVERSE`/`OP_VREVERSE` with `number >= 0` → skipped via `OP_lengths` (89).\n6. `OP_TYPESTAR/TYPEMINSTAR/TYPEPLUS/TYPEMINPLUS/TYPEQUERY/TYPEMINQUERY/TYPEPOSSTAR/TYPEPOSPLUS/TYPEPOSQUERY` with `code[1] == OP_PROP || OP_NOTPROP` → `code += 2` extra (111-121). e.g. `\\p{L}+`.\n7. `OP_TYPEUPTO/TYPEMINUPTO/TYPEEXACT/TYPEPOSUPTO` with `code[1+IMM2_SIZE] == OP_PROP/OP_NOTPROP` → `code += 2` (123-129). e.g. `\\p{L}{2,5}`.\n8. `OP_MARK`/`OP_COMMIT_ARG`/`OP_PRUNE_ARG`/`OP_SKIP_ARG`/`OP_THEN_ARG` → `code += code[1]` (131-137). e.g. `(*MARK:abc)`.\n9. Everything else → fixed `PRIV(OP_lengths)[c]` (142).\n10. `utf == TRUE` char-with-repeat extension (148-209): the ~56 opcodes `OP_CHAR..OP_NOTPOSQUERYI` get `code += GET_EXTRALEN(code[-1])` when `HAS_EXTRALEN(code[-1])`. Reach with a multi-byte literal + quantifier, e.g. `\\x{100}{2,5}` / `\\x{100}+`. With `utf == FALSE` this is skipped (`(void)utf` at 211 is the non-`MAYBE_UTF_MULTI` variant; in 8-bit UTF builds `MAYBE_UTF_MULTI` *is* defined).\n\n**Black-box reach:** `pcre2_compile()` of any pattern containing a subroutine call/recursion → the group-resolution pass (`pcre2_compile.c:11048`, uses an `RSCAN_CACHE_SIZE` cache so only a cache miss reaches the function) and `_pcre2_study`'s minimum-length computation for backrefs/recursion (`pcre2_study.c:499,559`, gated on `backref_cache`). Concrete patterns: `\"(a)(?1)\"`, `\"(a)(b)(c)(?3)\"`, `\"(?<n>a)\\\\k<n>\"`, `\"(a)(?1)(?1)\"` (cache hit vs miss), `\"(\\\\x{100}+)(?1)\"` with `PCRE2_UTF` (exercises class 10), `\"(*MARK:x)(a)(?1)\"` (class 8), `\"([\\\\x{100}\\\\p{L}])(?1)\"` (class 4).\n\n---\n\n## 13. `_pcre2_auto_possessify` — pcre2_auto_possess.c:1171-1414\n\n**Signature (verbatim, 1171-1172; decl pcre2_internal.h:2321-2322):**\n```c\nint\nPRIV(auto_possessify)(PCRE2_UCHAR *code, const compile_block *cb)\n```\n`extern int _pcre2_auto_possessify(PCRE2_UCHAR *, const compile_block *);`\nReturns 0 on success, `-1` if an opcode `>= OP_TABLE_LENGTH` is seen (1187-1191, `PCRE2_DEBUG_UNREACHABLE`). **It mutates the compiled code in place.**\n\n**State needed:** a **writable** compiled-code block (`codestart`) *and* a fully populated `compile_block *cb`. Fields actually read: `cb->external_options` (`PCRE2_UTF`→`utf`, `PCRE2_UCP`→`ucp`; lines 1179-1180), `cb->fcc` (case-flip table, 1198/1262 → `get_chr_property_list` line 426/432), `cb->cbits` (`cbit_digit/space/word`, lines 811/818/825), `cb->ctypes` (`ctype_digit/space/word`, lines 1019-1039), `cb->had_recurse` (641), `cb->start_code` (1118/1126, passed as `char_lists_end` to xclass/eclass). So a black-box test cannot call this meaningfully without a real compile — **drive it through `pcre2_compile()`**.\n\n**Internal tables (all `static`, not exported):** `autoposstab[APTROWS][APTCOLS]` 75-94 (rows `\\D \\d \\S \\s \\W \\w . .+ \\C \\P \\p \\R \\H \\h \\V \\v \\X`, cols additionally `\\Z \\z $ $M`; bounds `FIRST_AUTOTAB_OP = OP_NOT_DIGIT`, `LAST_AUTOTAB_LEFT_OP = OP_EXTUNI`, `LAST_AUTOTAB_RIGHT_OP = OP_DOLLM`, `pcre2_internal.h:1634-1636`); `propposstab[PT_TABSIZE][PT_TABSIZE]` 127-143 (values 0-17); `catposstab[7][30]` 152-161; `posspropstab[3][4]` 174-178.\n\n**Enable/disable (the compile options that matter):**\n- Enabled by default. Guard at `pcre2_compile.c:11085-11087`: `if (errorcode == 0 && (optim_flags & PCRE2_OPTIM_AUTO_POSSESS) != 0)`; flag value `PCRE2_OPTIM_AUTO_POSSESS 0x00000001u` (`pcre2_internal.h:602`).\n- Disabled by `PCRE2_NO_AUTO_POSSESS` in the compile options (`pcre2_compile.c:10410-10411`).\n- Disabled by `pcre2_set_optimize(ccontext, PCRE2_AUTO_POSSESS_OFF)` (=65) or `PCRE2_OPTIMIZATION_NONE` (=0) — `include/pcre2.h:499-507`, `pcre2_context.c:428`.\n- Disabled by the in-pattern start option `(*NO_AUTO_POSSESS)` (`pcre2_compile.c:746`, `PSO_OPTMZ`).\n\n**Equivalence classes — outer driver (1182-1413):**\n1. Opcode in `OP_STAR..OP_TYPEPOSUPTO` (1194): normalises via `get_repeat_base` (296-305) → `OP_STAR`/`OP_STARI`/`OP_NOTSTAR`/`OP_NOTSTARI`/`OP_TYPESTAR` families. Only `c <= OP_MINUPTO` gets a property list (1197) — i.e. already-possessive forms are skipped. `list[1]` = greedy flag (1199). On success rewrites the opcode: STAR→POSSTAR, MINSTAR→POSSTAR, PLUS→POSPLUS, MINPLUS→POSPLUS, QUERY→POSQUERY, MINQUERY→POSQUERY, UPTO→POSUPTO, MINUPTO→POSUPTO (1204-1237).\n2. Class opcodes `OP_CLASS`/`OP_NCLASS`/`OP_XCLASS`/`OP_ECLASS` (1241) whose trailing repeat is `OP_CRSTAR..OP_CRMINRANGE` (1255) → rewrites to `OP_CRPOSSTAR`/`CRPOSPLUS`/`CRPOSQUERY`/`CRPOSRANGE` (1268-1289). `list[1] = (c & 1) == 0` (1263) distinguishes greedy from minimal.\n3. Advance logic mirrors `find_bracket`: `TYPE*` + `OP_PROP/NOTPROP` → +2 (1300-1318); `OP_CALLOUT_STR` (1320); `OP_XCLASS`/`OP_ECLASS` (1325-1328); `MARK`/`*_ARG` (1331-1337); UTF extra-len for ~56 char opcodes (1348-1409).\n4. `rec_limit = 1000` (1178) → deeply nested groups abort the analysis and leave the rest unpossessified (566).\n\n**Equivalence classes — `compare_opcodes` (547-1148) / what pairs succeed:**\n5. `OP_END` right-hand side (612): possessify iff greedy (`base_list[1] != 0`). `a+` → `a++`. `a*?` → unchanged.\n6. Callouts skipped (584-594): `a+(?C1)b` still possessifies.\n7. `OP_ALT` → jump to end of group (598-602): `(?:a+|x)b`.\n8. `OP_KET`/`OP_KETRPOS` (623): non-greedy → FALSE; `OP_CBRA`/`SCBRA`/`CBRAPOS`/`SCBRAPOS` + `cb->had_recurse` → FALSE (e.g. `(a+)(?1)` not possessified, but `(a+)b` is); `OP_SCRIPT_RUN` → only if base is `OP_CHAR`/`OP_CHARI` (648-650, e.g. `(*sr:a+)` OK, `(*sr:\\d+)` not); `OP_ASSERT`/`OP_ASSERT_NOT`/`OP_ONCE` → `!entered_a_group` (657-660, e.g. `(?=a+)` yes, `(?=(?:a+))`-style re-entry no); `OP_ASSERTBACK`/`OP_ASSERTBACK_NOT` → walk all branches, `OP_VREVERSE` in any branch → FALSE (667-675, e.g. `(?<=a+)` yes vs `(?<=ab?a+)` no); `OP_ASSERT_NA`/`OP_ASSERTBACK_NA` → FALSE (680-682, i.e. `(?*a+)`).\n9. `OP_ONCE`/`OP_BRA`/`OP_CBRA` ahead (692-710): recurse per branch, set `entered_a_group`.\n10. `OP_BRAZERO`/`OP_BRAMINZERO` (712-729): only followed by BRA/CBRA/ONCE, else FALSE.\n11. Unsupported opcode → `get_chr_property_list` returns NULL → FALSE (741-742). Also `OP_KETRMAX`/`OP_KETRMIN` fall here by design (comment 615-621).\n12. **char-vs-char** (747-756 sets `chr_ptr`/`list_ptr`, then 987-1137): `a+b` → possessify; `a+a` → no; `a+A` → possessify, but `(?i)a+A` → no (the `OP_CHARI` case at 418-441 loads both cases into `list[2]`/`list[3]` via `cb->fcc` or `UCD_OTHERCASE`).\n13. **char-vs-type** (1018-1093): `\\d`, `\\D`, `\\s`, `\\S`, `\\w`, `\\W` use `cb->ctypes`; `\\h`/`\\H`/`\\v`/`\\V`/`\\R` use `HSPACE_CASES`/`VSPACE_CASES`; `OP_DOLL`/`OP_EODN` treat CR/LF/VT/FF/NEL/U+2028/U+2029 as blocking; `OP_EOD` always possessifiable (1092). e.g. `a+\\d` → yes; `1+\\d` → no; `a+$` → yes; `\\n+$` → no.\n14. **class-bitmap vs bitmap/type** (760-856): `[ab]+c` → yes (`OP_CLASS` bitmap ∩ `{c}` empty), `[ab]+b` → no; `[ab]+[cd]` → yes; `[a-z]+\\d` → yes (bitmap ∩ `cb->cbits+cbit_digit`); `[a-z]+\\D` → no (`invert_bits` path 807-809/836-843). In 8-bit **non-UTF** mode `OP_NCLASS` is treated as `OP_CLASS` (762-768) — a distinct 8-bit-only branch.\n15. **XCLASS on the right of a bitmap** (792-804): `XCL_HASPROP` set → FALSE immediately (795); `XCL_MAP` clear → return `(*xclass_flags & XCL_NOT) == 0` when `list[1]==0` (799), else `continue`. e.g. `[a-z]+[\\x{100}]` vs `[a-z]+[^\\x{100}]` vs `[a-z]+[\\p{L}]`.\n16. **char vs XCLASS/ECLASS** (1116-1128): calls `PRIV(xclass)`/`PRIV(eclass)` with `cb->start_code`. e.g. `a+[\\x{100}]` → yes; `a+[\\x{61}\\x{100}]` → no; `a+(?[\\p{L}])` → no.\n17. **PROP vs PROP** (870-968) — reachable only when both sides are `OP_PROP`/`OP_NOTPROP`, i.e. with `\\p`/`\\P` or with `PCRE2_UCP` (which rewrites `\\d`→`PT_PC ucp_Nd`, `pcre2_compile.c:675,2942`). All 18 `propposstab` values are distinct classes:\n   - 0 → never: `\\p{Greek}+\\p{bidiclass:L}` (`PT_SC`×`PT_BIDICL`).\n   - 1 (both must be PROP): `\\p{L&}+\\p{Xps}` (`PT_LAMP`×`PT_SPACE`).\n   - 2 (same group): `\\p{L}+\\p{N}` → yes; `\\p{L}+\\p{L}` → no; `\\P{L}+\\p{L}` → yes (`same==FALSE`).\n   - 3 (differ): `\\p{L&}+\\P{L&}` → yes.\n   - 4 (left GC, right PC): **`\\p{L}+\\d` with `PCRE2_UCP`** → `catposstab[ucp_L][ucp_Nd] == 1 == same` → yes. `\\p{L}+\\p{Ll}` → `catposstab[L][Ll] == 0` → no.\n   - 5 (right GC, left PC): `\\p{Ll}+\\p{N}` → yes; `\\p{Ll}+\\p{L}` → no.\n   - 6/7/8 (left ALNUM/SPACE/WORD vs right GC): `\\p{Xan}+\\p{Z}`, `\\p{Xps}+\\p{L}`, `\\p{Xwd}+\\p{Z}`.\n   - 9/10/11 (right ALNUM/SPACE/WORD vs left GC): `\\p{Z}+\\p{Xan}`, `\\p{L}+\\p{Xps}`, `\\p{Z}+\\p{Xwd}`.\n   - 12/13/14 (left special vs right PC): `\\p{Xan}+\\p{Zs}`, `\\p{Xps}+\\p{Ll}`, `\\p{Xwd}+\\p{Zs}`.\n   - 15/16/17 (right special vs left PC): `\\p{Zs}+\\p{Xan}`, `\\p{Ll}+\\p{Xps}`, `\\p{Zs}+\\p{Xwd}`.\n   - `rightop == OP_EOD` special-case (872-873): `\\p{L}+\\z` → always yes.\n   - `PT_CLIST` is *never* seen here: `get_chr_property_list` (446-478) converts a `PT_CLIST` property into an `OP_CHAR` character list from `_pcre2_ucd_caseless_sets` (so `(?i)\\x{1c4}+…` becomes a char-list comparison; `check_char_prop` `PT_CLIST` at 258-264 handles the mirror case).\n   - `PT_BIDICL`/`PT_BOOL` always FALSE in `check_char_prop` (272-276) → `\\p{bidiclass:L}`, `\\p{Bidi_Control}` never possessify against a char.\n18. **`autoposstab` fallback** (973-975) for non-PROP type pairs. Row/col pairs worth testing: `\\d+\\D`→1 (yes), `\\d+\\d`→0, `\\D+\\d`→1, `\\s+\\S`→1, `\\w+\\W`→1, `\\d+\\s`→1, `\\d+\\R`→1, `\\d+\\h`→1, `\\d+\\v`→1, `\\d+\\Z`→1, `\\d+$`→1, `.+\\R`→1, `\\h+\\H`→1, `\\H+\\h`→1, `\\v+\\V`→1, `\\R+.`→1, `\\X+\\z`→1, `\\C+\\z`→1, and every `\\P`/`\\p` row/col which is uniformly 0 (86-87).\n19. `list[1] != 0` (possibly-empty repeat, e.g. `a*`, `a{0,3}`, `[ab]*`) → keeps scanning further opcodes instead of returning TRUE (853-855, 979-981, 1141). So `a*bc` must check both `b` and `c`.\n\n**Black-box reach:** compile any of the above patterns twice — once plain, once with `PCRE2_NO_AUTO_POSSESS` — and compare (a) `pcre2_pattern_info(PCRE2_INFO_SIZE)`/opcode dump, or (b) observable backtracking behaviour, e.g. `\"a+b\"` vs `\"a++b\"` against `\"aaa\"` (no match either way but different match-limit consumption — use `pcre2_set_match_limit()`/`PCRE2_INFO_...` or a callout counter to observe), or (c) `[ab]+c` vs subject `\"abab\"`.\n\n---\n\n## 14. pcre2_tables.c — exported tables\n\n| Table | Declared type & size | Definition | Extern decl | Public-API read path (concrete) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n|`_pcre2_OP_lengths`|`const uint8_t []` — `OP_LENGTHS` macro, **173 entries** (`OP_TABLE_LENGTH`=173, `pcre2_internal.h:1908`, last opcode `OP_UCP_WORD_BOUNDARY`=172)|`pcre2_tables.c:67`|`pcre2_internal.h:2242`|Every compile & match walks it: `_pcre2_find_bracket` (find_bracket.c:89,99,142), `_pcre2_auto_possessify` (auto_possess.c:586,687,696,728,1342), `_pcre2_study`, `pcre2_match`, `pcre2_dfa_match`. Any `pcre2_compile(\"(a)(?1)\")`.|\n|`_pcre2_hspace_list`|`const uint32_t []` = `HSPACE_LIST`, 8-bit UTF build (`pcre2_internal.h:377-381`): `{0x09,0x20,0xA0,0x1680,0x180E,0x2000..0x200A,0x202F,0x205F,0x3000, NOTACHAR}` = **20 entries incl. terminator**|`pcre2_tables.c:72`|`pcre2_internal.h:2249`|`pcre2_compile` of `[\\h]` / `[\\H]` — `pcre2_compile_class.c:1388,1400`; and `(?[\\h])` via `append_char_list`/`append_negated_char_list` `:384,390`.|\n|`_pcre2_vspace_list`|`const uint32_t []` = `VSPACE_LIST` (`:410-411`): `{0x0A,0x0B,0x0C,0x0D,0x85,0x2028,0x2029, NOTACHAR}` = **8 entries**|`pcre2_tables.c:73`|`pcre2_internal.h:2250`|`[\\v]` / `[\\V]` — `pcre2_compile_class.c:1412,1424`; `(?[\\v])` `:396,402`.|\n|`_pcre2_callout_start_delims`|`const uint32_t []`, **9 entries** (8 + 0 terminator): `` ` ' \" ^ % # $ { `` , 0|`pcre2_tables.c:84-87`|`pcre2_internal.h:2244`|`pcre2_compile` of a string callout: `pcre2_compile.c:5332-5334`. Pattern: ``\"(?C`abc`)x\"``, `\"(?C{abc})x\"`, `\"(?C\\\"abc\\\")x\"`.|\n|`_pcre2_callout_end_delims`|`const uint32_t []`, **9 entries**; identical except `}` replaces `{`|`pcre2_tables.c:89-92`|`pcre2_internal.h:2243`|Same site, `pcre2_compile.c:5336` picks the matching closer. Pattern `\"(?C{abc})\"` → delimiter `}`.|\n|`_pcre2_utf8_table1`|`const int []`, **6 entries**: `{0x7f,0x7ff,0xffff,0x1fffff,0x3ffffff,0x7fffffff}`|`pcre2_tables.c:114-115`|`pcre2_internal.h:2203`|`_pcre2_ord2utf` (ord2utf.c:85-86). Any `pcre2_compile(\"\\\\x{100}\", PCRE2_UTF)`.|\n|`_pcre2_utf8_table1_size`|`const unsigned` = `ARR_SIZE(utf8_table1)` = **6**|`pcre2_tables.c:117`|`pcre2_internal.h:2204`|Same (loop bound, ord2utf.c:85).|\n|`_pcre2_utf8_table2`|`const int []`, **6 entrie