` (one byte, so c ≤ 0xff).\n\n**Equivalence classes (8-bit, non-EBCDIC):**\n\n| # | type | utf | bytes at ptr | endptr | result | `*lenptr` | line |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n|1|2|any|`0x0A`|any|TRUE|1|89-91|\n|2|2|any|`0x0D 0x0A`|`ptr+2`|TRUE|2|93-95|\n|3|2|any|`0x0D 0x0A`|`ptr+1` (CR is last unit; LF not in subject)|TRUE|**1**|94|\n|4|2|any|`0x0D 0x41`|`ptr+2`|TRUE|1|94|\n|5|2|any|`0x0D`|`ptr+1` (CR at end)|TRUE|1|94|\n|6|2|any|`0x0B`/`0x0C`/`0x85`/`0x41`|any|FALSE|untouched|97-98|\n|7|1|any|`0x0A`, `0x0B` (VT), `0x0C` (FF)|any|TRUE|1|108-112|\n|8|1|any|`0x0D 0x0A`, `ptr<endptr-1`|—|TRUE|2|114-116|\n|9|1|any|`0x0D` at end / `0x0D`+non-LF|—|TRUE|1|115|\n|10|1|**FALSE**|raw byte `0x85`|—|TRUE|**1**|120-122|\n|11|1|**TRUE**|`0xC2 0x85` (NEL)|—|TRUE|**2**|120-122|\n|12|1|**TRUE**|`0xE2 0x80 0xA8` (U+2028 LS)|—|TRUE|**3**|124-127|\n|13|1|**TRUE**|`0xE2 0x80 0xA9` (U+2029 PS)|—|TRUE|**3**|126|\n|14|1|FALSE|any other byte, e.g. `0x41`, `0xE2`|—|FALSE|untouched|138-139|\n|15|1|TRUE|any other char, e.g. `a`, U+2027|—|FALSE|untouched|138-139|\n\nNote class 12/13 are **unreachable when `utf=FALSE`** (c is a single byte). `CHAR_NEL` = `(unsigned char)'\\x85'` (`pcre2_internal.h:679`).\nCRLF-split boundary is `ptr < endptr - 1` (strict): a CR whose LF lies at/after `endptr` yields length 1.\n\n**Black-box reach:** direct call (exported symbol). Indirect: `pcre2_compile()` with `PCRE2_NEWLINE_ANY|ANYCRLF` in the compile context and `(?x)`/`#`-comment scanning (`pcre2_compile.c:3463` `IS_NEWLINE(ptr)`), or `pcre2_match()`/`pcre2_dfa_match()` with `.` (OP_ANY, `pcre2_match.c:1062`), `$`/`\\Z` multiline, `firstline`. e.g. compile `\"a.b\"` with `PCRE2_NEWLINE_ANY` + `PCRE2_UTF`, subject `\"a\\xC2\\x85b\"` → no match (NEL is a newline, len 2).\n\n---\n\n## 2. `_pcre2_was_newline` — pcre2_newline.c:164-237\n\n**Signature (verbatim, 164-166; decl pcre2_internal.h:2346-2347):**\n```c\nBOOL\nPRIV(was_newline)(PCRE2_SPTR ptr, uint32_t type, PCRE2_SPTR startptr,\n  uint32_t *lenptr, BOOL utf)\n```\n`extern BOOL _pcre2_was_newline(PCRE2_SPTR, uint32_t, PCRE2_SPTR, uint32_t *, BOOL);`\n\n**State needed:** none. Precondition from `WAS_NEWLINE` (`pcre2_internal.h:487-497`): `ptr > startptr`. Line 169 does `ptr--` first; if `utf` then `BACKCHAR(ptr)` (walk back over 0x80-0xBF continuation bytes) then `GETCHAR` (lines 171-177).\n\n**Equivalence classes (positions relative to the *decremented/back-adjusted* `ptr`):**\n\n| # | type | utf | preceding bytes | result | `*lenptr` | line |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n|1|2|any|`...0x0D 0x0A` and `ptr > startptr`|TRUE|2 (CRLF)|186|\n|2|2|any|`0x0A` at `startptr` (no room for CR)|TRUE|**1**|186|\n|3|2|any|`0x41 0x0A`|TRUE|1|186|\n|4|2|any|`0x0D`|TRUE|1|189-191|\n|5|2|any|`0x0B`,`0x0C`,`0x85`,`0x41`|FALSE|untouched|193-194|\n|6|1|any|`0x0A` preceded by `0x0D`, `ptr>startptr`|TRUE|2|202|\n|7|1|any|`0x0A` at startptr or after non-CR|TRUE|1|202|\n|8|1|any|`0x0B` (VT), `0x0C` (FF), `0x0D` (CR)|TRUE|1|208-212|\n|9|1|FALSE|raw `0x85`|TRUE|**1**|216-218|\n|10|1|TRUE|`0xC2 0x85`|TRUE|**2**|216-218|\n|11|1|TRUE|`0xE2 0x80 0xA8` / `0xA9`|TRUE|**3**|220-223|\n|12|1|any|anything else|FALSE|untouched|234-235|\n\nCR-LF backwards check uses raw `ptr[-1] == CHAR_CR` (byte compare, not UTF-aware — safe because CR is ASCII and cannot be a UTF-8 continuation byte).\n\n**Black-box reach:** direct; or `pcre2_match()`/`pcre2_dfa_match()` with `^` in `PCRE2_MULTILINE` (`WAS_NEWLINE`) and `PCRE2_NEWLINE_ANY|ANYCRLF`, plus the \"advance to after next newline\" loops (`pcre2_dfa_match.c:3870,3878`). e.g. compile `\"^b\"` with `PCRE2_MULTILINE|PCRE2_NEWLINE_ANY|PCRE2_UTF`, subject `\"a\\xE2\\x80\\xA8b\"` → match at offset 4.\n\n---\n\n## 3. `_pcre2_valid_utf` — pcre2_valid_utf.c:92-315 (UTF-8 arm 100-315)\n\n**Signature (verbatim, 92-94; decl pcre2_internal.h:2345):**\n```c\nint\nPRIV(valid_utf)(PCRE2_SPTR string, PCRE2_SIZE length, PCRE2_SIZE *erroroffset)\n```\n`extern int _pcre2_valid_utf(PCRE2_SPTR, PCRE2_SIZE, PCRE2_SIZE *