{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"a263cebc0f2a387ef","tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01BHNM5ngJDLSJoX1QjtvTti","status":"completed","output_file":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-GdDnk6/tmp/claude-31072124/-local-home-scheschb--harvest-work-harvest-work-GdDnk6-translated-rust/aeab5d90-512d-4436-80fd-a67670a151c9/tasks/a263cebc0f2a387ef.output","summary":"Fixed. Only `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-GdDnk6/translated_rust/src/pcre2_compile.rs` was modified (the `CHAR_BACKSLASH` arm of `parse_regex`'s main loop, ~lines 4414-4590).\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe escape body is now wrapped in a labeled block `'escape_body:` guarded by `let mut escape_failed = errorcode != 0;`, and the real `ESCAPE_FAILED` label body (BAD_ESCAPE_IS_LITERAL check → `ptr = tempptr` → re-read one char / `CHAR_BACKSLASH` at end → fall through to `PARSED_LITERAL`) now lives in a single `if escape_failed { ... }` block after the labeled block (line 4576), reachable from every former `goto ESCAPE_FAILED` site. Each site sets `escape_failed = true; break 'escape_body;` *after* the state changes the C makes before its goto (`errorcode = ...`, `ptr = p`), so both the error code and the error offset match C on the failing path.\n\n## C `goto ESCAPE_FAILED` sites → Rust\n\n| C line (`c_src/src/pcre2_compile.c`) | site | Rust line |\n|---|---|---|\n| 3662 | `ESC_C`, `errorcode = ERR85` under `#ifdef NEVER_BACKSLASH_C` | not compiled (`config.h:233` `#undef NEVER_BACKSLASH_C`) — correctly absent from Rust |\n| 3667 | `ESC_C` + `PCRE2_NEVER_BACKSLASH_C` → ERR83 | 4452 |\n| 3687 | `ESC_X`, ERR45 under `#ifndef SUPPORT_UNICODE` | not compiled (`CMakeLists.txt:17` defines `SUPPORT_UNICODE`) — correctly absent |\n| 3725 | `\\p`/`\\P`: `get_ucp()` failed | 4492 |\n| 3733 | `\\p`/`\\P` ERR45 in the `#else` (no Unicode) | not compiled — correctly absent |\n| 3749 | `\\g`/`\\k` missing `{`/`<`/`'` → ERR57/ERR69 | 4509 |\n| 3768 | `\\g<num` missing terminator → `ptr = p; errorcode = ERR119` | 4527 |\n| 3773 | after `read_number` returned FALSE with `errorcode != 0` | 4544 |\n| 3780 | `read_name()` failed | 4551 |\n\nSix live sites, matching the six previously-mistranslated `do_fail!(); // ESCAPE_FAILED` calls.\n\n## Notes / deliberate deviation from the sketch\n\nI did **not** add `errorcode = 0;` in the ESCAPE_FAILED body. The C does *not* clear `errorcode` there (it just falls through), and `check_escape` resets `*errorcodeptr` on the next escape, so clearing it would have been a new divergence. The Rust now leaves `errorcode` exactly as C does. I also dropped the now-dead `escape = 0;` store (documented by a comment) since the literal write is done inline, avoiding an `unused_assignments` warning; `escape` is not read again in that iteration.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `cargo build --release 2>&1 | grep -E \"^error\"` → no output. Only pre-existing warnings (17, none in the edited region).\n- Ad-hoc differential harness (`/tmp/diffchk.c`, dlopens `c_src/build/libpcre2.so` vs `target/release/libpcre2.so`) over 59 cases — all six sites with and without `PCRE2_EXTRA_BAD_ESCAPE_IS_LITERAL`, UTF variants of the re-read char, valid `\\k<n>`/`\\g<n>`/`\\g'1'`/`\\1` controls, and stale-`errorcode` follow-on constructs (`\\ka{x}`, `\\ka(?<n>b)\\g<n>`, `\\C\\g'zz'`, `\\p{Xyz}x{2}`, …) — compile result, error code, error offset and match ovector are byte-identical. In particular `\\Z\\C` with `NEVER_BACKSLASH_C`: `x=0` → `FAIL err=183 off=4`, `x=2` → compiles, in both libraries. I did not run `cargo test`.","usage":{"total_tokens":65248,"tool_uses":28,"duration_ms":393041},"uuid":"528bac65-dbd4-493b-8840-34e530753ea3","session_id":"aeab5d90-512d-4436-80fd-a67670a151c9"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01BHNM5ngJDLSJoX1QjtvTti","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Fixed. Only `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-GdDnk6/translated_rust/src/pcre2_compile.rs` was modified (the `CHAR_BACKSLASH` arm of `parse_regex`'s main loop, ~lines 4414-4590).\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe escape body is now wrapped in a labeled block `'escape_body:` guarded by `let mut escape_failed = errorcode != 0;`, and the real `ESCAPE_FAILED` label body (BAD_ESCAPE_IS_LITERAL check → `ptr = tempptr` → re-read one char / `CHAR_BACKSLASH` at end → fall through to `PARSED_LITERAL`) now lives in a single `if escape_failed { ... }` block after the labeled block (line 4576), reachable from every former `goto ESCAPE_FAILED` site. Each site sets `escape_failed = true; break 'escape_body;` *after* the state changes the C makes before its goto (`errorcode = ...`, `ptr = p`), so both the error code and the error offset match C on the failing path.\n\n## C `goto ESCAPE_FAILED` sites → Rust\n\n| C line (`c_src/src/pcre2_compile.c`) | site | Rust line |\n|---|---|---|\n| 3662 | `ESC_C`, `errorcode = ERR85` under `#ifdef NEVER_BACKSLASH_C` | not compiled (`config.h:233` `#undef NEVER_BACKSLASH_C`) — correctly absent from Rust |\n| 3667 | `ESC_C` + `PCRE2_NEVER_BACKSLASH_C` → ERR83 | 4452 |\n| 3687 | `ESC_X`, ERR45 under `#ifndef SUPPORT_UNICODE` | not compiled (`CMakeLists.txt:17` defines `SUPPORT_UNICODE`) — correctly absent |\n| 3725 | `\\p`/`\\P`: `get_ucp()` failed | 4492 |\n| 3733 | `\\p`/`\\P` ERR45 in the `#else` (no Unicode) | not compiled — correctly absent |\n| 3749 | `\\g`/`\\k` missing `{`/`<`/`'` → ERR57/ERR69 | 4509 |\n| 3768 | `\\g<num` missing terminator → `ptr = p; errorcode = ERR119` | 4527 |\n| 3773 | after `read_number` returned FALSE with `errorcode != 0` | 4544 |\n| 3780 | `read_name()` failed | 4551 |\n\nSix live sites, matching the six previously-mistranslated `do_fail!(); // ESCAPE_FAILED` calls.\n\n## Notes / deliberate deviation from the sketch\n\nI did **not** add `errorcode = 0;` in the ESCAPE_FAILED body. The C does *not* clear `errorcode` there (it just falls through), and `check_escape` resets `*errorcodeptr` on the next escape, so clearing it would have been a new divergence. The Rust now leaves `errorcode` exactly as C does. I also dropped the now-dead `escape = 0;` store (documented by a comment) since the literal write is done inline, avoiding an `unused_assignments` warning; `escape` is not read again in that iteration.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `cargo build --release 2>&1 | grep -E \"^error\"` → no output. Only pre-existing warnings (17, none in the edited region).\n- Ad-hoc differential harness (`/tmp/diffchk.c`, dlopens `c_src/build/libpcre2.so` vs `target/release/libpcre2.so`) over 59 cases — all six sites with and without `PCRE2_EXTRA_BAD_ESCAPE_IS_LITERAL`, UTF variants of the re-read char, valid `\\k<n>`/`\\g<n>`/`\\g'1'`/`\\1` controls, and stale-`errorcode` follow-on constructs (`\\ka{x}`, `\\ka(?<n>b)\\g<n>`, `\\C\\g'zz'`, `\\p{Xyz}x{2}`, …) — compile result, error code, error offset and match ovector are byte-identical. In particular `\\Z\\C` with `NEVER_BACKSLASH_C`: `x=0` → `FAIL err=183 off=4`, `x=2` → compiles, in both libraries. I did not run `cargo test`."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a263cebc0f2a387ef (use SendMessage with to: 'a263cebc0f2a387ef', summary: '<5-10 word recap>' to continue this agent)\n<usage>subagent_tokens: 66484\ntool_uses: 28\nduration_ms: 393042</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"aeab5d90-512d-4436-80fd-a67670a151c9","uuid":"43bfd6d8-de88-4f36-a04a-94ff0a52a23c","timestamp":"2026-08-14T21:47:01.620Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Fix a translation bug in the Rust port of PCRE2 at\n`/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-GdDnk6/translated_rust`.\nNEVER modify anything under `c_src/` (the C is ground truth). Only edit `src/*.rs`.\n\n## The divergence (found by a differential test)\n\nPattern `\\Z\\C` compiled with `options = PCRE2_NEVER_BACKSLASH_C (0x00100000)` and\n`ccontext` extra options `PCRE2_EXTRA_BAD_ESCAPE_IS_LITERAL (0x2)`:\n\n* C   : compiles successfully (`pcre2_compile` returns non-NULL)\n* Rust: fails with errorcode 183 (= ERR83 + COMPILE_ERROR_BASE 100), erroroffset 4\n\n## Root cause\n\nIn `c_src/src/pcre2_compile.c`, inside `parse_regex()`'s main loop, the\n`case CHAR_BACKSLASH:` arm (READ C LINES 3585–3800) contains the label\n`ESCAPE_FAILED:` **inside** the `if (errorcode != 0) { ... }` block:\n\n```c\n    case CHAR_BACKSLASH:\n    tempptr = ptr;\n    escape = PRIV(check_escape)(&ptr, ptrend, &c, &errorcode, options,\n      xoptions, cb->bracount, FALSE, cb);\n    if (errorcode != 0)\n      {\n      ESCAPE_FAILED:\n      if ((xoptions & PCRE2_EXTRA_BAD_ESCAPE_IS_LITERAL) == 0)\n        goto FAILED;\n      ptr = tempptr;\n      if (ptr >= ptrend) c = CHAR_BACKSLASH; else\n        {\n        GETCHARINCTEST(c, ptr);   /* Get character value, increment pointer */\n        }\n      escape = 0;                 /* Treat as literal character */\n      }\n\n    if (escape == 0)          /* <-- control FALLS THROUGH to here */\n      {\n      PARSED_LITERAL(c, parsed_pattern);\n      }\n    else if (escape < 0) { ...backref... }\n    else switch (escape) { ... 8 × `goto ESCAPE_FAILED;` ... }\n```\n\nSo EVERY `goto ESCAPE_FAILED;` inside that `else switch (escape)` means:\n\"if PCRE2_EXTRA_BAD_ESCAPE_IS_LITERAL is NOT set → the normal compile failure\n(`goto FAILED`, keeping the errorcode); otherwise → rewind `ptr` to `tempptr`,\nre-read one character (or use `CHAR_BACKSLASH` if at the end), set `escape = 0`,\n**clear the pending failure**, and continue the main parse loop as if the item had\nbeen that literal character (i.e. execute `PARSED_LITERAL(c, parsed_pattern)`).\"\n\nRun this to see the exact set of C sites (there are 9 `goto ESCAPE_FAILED;`, one of\nwhich is inside `#ifdef NEVER_BACKSLASH_C` and is NOT compiled here):\n\n    grep -n \"goto ESCAPE_FAILED;\" c_src/src/pcre2_compile.c\n\nThe Rust translation in `src/pcre2_compile.rs` implemented the label-entry\nfixup correctly for the `errorcode != 0` case right after `check_escape`\n(look near line 4413: `if errorcode != 0 { // ESCAPE_FAILED ... }`), but every\n`goto ESCAPE_FAILED` inside the `escape > 0` match was translated as a plain\n`do_fail!();` (grep for `// ESCAPE_FAILED` in src/pcre2_compile.rs, around lines\n4455, 4494, 4510, 4527, 4543, 4549 — but VERIFY the full list yourself; some sites\nmay be unmarked, and the ERR85 one is `#ifdef`-disabled in C so it must NOT exist\nin the Rust at all).\n\n## What to implement\n\nRestructure the Rust `CHAR_BACKSLASH` arm so that all of those sites get the real\n`ESCAPE_FAILED` semantics, e.g. by wrapping the escape handling in a labeled block:\n\n```rust\nCHAR_BACKSLASH => {\n    tempptr = ptr;\n    escape = _pcre2_check_escape_8(...);\n    let mut escape_failed = errorcode != 0;\n    if !escape_failed {\n        'escape_body: {\n            // the existing `if escape == 0 {...} else if escape < 0 {...} else { match escape {...} }`\n            // body goes here; each former `do_fail!(); // ESCAPE_FAILED` becomes\n            //     { escape_failed = true; break 'escape_body; }\n            // (leaving `errorcode` set exactly as the C does)\n        }\n    }\n    if escape_failed {\n        if (xoptions & PCRE2_EXTRA_BAD_ESCAPE_IS_LITERAL) == 0 {\n            do_fail!();                 // keeps errorcode → same error as C\n        }\n        ptr = tempptr;\n        if ptr >= ptrend { c = CHAR_BACKSLASH; } else { c = getcharinctest(&mut ptr, utf); }\n        escape = 0;\n        errorcode = 0;                  // C clears the failure implicitly by falling through\n        // now do exactly what the `escape == 0` branch does (PARSED_LITERAL):\n        ...\n    }\n}\n```\n\nAdapt this sketch to the actual code — do NOT blindly paste it. Requirements:\n\n1. Behaviour must match the C EXACTLY for both settings of\n   PCRE2_EXTRA_BAD_ESCAPE_IS_LITERAL, for every one of the live\n   `goto ESCAPE_FAILED` sites (`\\C` with NEVER_BACKSLASH_C, the `\\p{...}` /\n   `\\P{...}` sites, `\\k`/`\\g` name sites, etc.). Check each C site to see exactly\n   what state (parsed_pattern writes, okquantifier, ptr) has already been changed\n   before the goto, and reproduce that.\n2. `errorcode` must remain set when the failure is real (BAD_ESCAPE_IS_LITERAL\n   not set) so the same error code and error offset are reported.\n3. Do not change any other behaviour, do not reformat unrelated code, and do not\n   introduce `unimplemented!()`/stubs.\n4. `cargo build --release 2>&1 | grep -E \"^error\"` must be clean when you are done.\n   (Do NOT run `cargo test`; I will run the differential tests.)\n\nReport: the list of C `goto ESCAPE_FAILED` sites and, for each, the Rust line you\nchanged; plus confirmation that the release build is clean.","agentId":"a263cebc0f2a387ef","agentType":"general-purpose","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Fixed. Only `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-GdDnk6/translated_rust/src/pcre2_compile.rs` was modified (the `CHAR_BACKSLASH` arm of `parse_regex`'s main loop, ~lines 4414-4590).\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe escape body is now wrapped in a labeled block `'escape_body:` guarded by `let mut escape_failed = errorcode != 0;`, and the real `ESCAPE_FAILED` label body (BAD_ESCAPE_IS_LITERAL check → `ptr = tempptr` → re-read one char / `CHAR_BACKSLASH` at end → fall through to `PARSED_LITERAL`) now lives in a single `if escape_failed { ... }` block after the labeled block (line 4576), reachable from every former `goto ESCAPE_FAILED` site. Each site sets `escape_failed = true; break 'escape_body;` *after* the state changes the C makes before its goto (`errorcode = ...`, `ptr = p`), so both the error code and the error offset match C on the failing path.\n\n## C `goto ESCAPE_FAILED` sites → Rust\n\n| C line (`c_src/src/pcre2_compile.c`) | site | Rust line |\n|---|---|---|\n| 3662 | `ESC_C`, `errorcode = ERR85` under `#ifdef NEVER_BACKSLASH_C` | not compiled (`config.h:233` `#undef NEVER_BACKSLASH_C`) — correctly absent from Rust |\n| 3667 | `ESC_C` + `PCRE2_NEVER_BACKSLASH_C` → ERR83 | 4452 |\n| 3687 | `ESC_X`, ERR45 under `#ifndef SUPPORT_UNICODE` | not compiled (`CMakeLists.txt:17` defines `SUPPORT_UNICODE`) — correctly absent |\n| 3725 | `\\p`/`\\P`: `get_ucp()` failed | 4492 |\n| 3733 | `\\p`/`\\P` ERR45 in the `#else` (no Unicode) | not compiled — correctly absent |\n| 3749 | `\\g`/`\\k` missing `{`/`<`/`'` → ERR57/ERR69 | 4509 |\n| 3768 | `\\g<num` missing terminator → `ptr = p; errorcode = ERR119` | 4527 |\n| 3773 | after `read_number` returned FALSE with `errorcode != 0` | 4544 |\n| 3780 | `read_name()` failed | 4551 |\n\nSix live sites, matching the six previously-mistranslated `do_fail!(); // ESCAPE_FAILED` calls.\n\n## Notes / deliberate deviation from the sketch\n\nI did **not** add `errorcode = 0;` in the ESCAPE_FAILED body. The C does *not* clear `errorcode` there (it just falls through), and `check_escape` resets `*errorcodeptr` on the next escape, so clearing it would have been a new divergence. The Rust now leaves `errorcode` exactly as C does. I also dropped the now-dead `escape = 0;` store (documented by a comment) since the literal write is done inline, avoiding an `unused_assignments` warning; `escape` is not read again in that iteration.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `cargo build --release 2>&1 | grep -E \"^error\"` → no output. Only pre-existing warnings (17, none in the edited region).\n- Ad-hoc differential harness (`/tmp/diffchk.c`, dlopens `c_src/build/libpcre2.so` vs `target/release/libpcre2.so`) over 59 cases — all six sites with and without `PCRE2_EXTRA_BAD_ESCAPE_IS_LITERAL`, UTF variants of the re-read char, valid `\\k<n>`/`\\g<n>`/`\\g'1'`/`\\1` controls, and stale-`errorcode` follow-on constructs (`\\ka{x}`, `\\ka(?<n>b)\\g<n>`, `\\C\\g'