{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01AvfMMUX33JxZwpwguhA9Nw","type":"tool_result","content":"CMakeLists.txt\nbuild\ninclude\nsrc\ncmake_minimum_required(VERSION 3.10)\nproject(pcre2 C)\nset(CMAKE_C_STANDARD 99)\n\nfile(GLOB PCRE2_SOURCES \"src/*.c\")\n\nadd_library(pcre2 SHARED ${PCRE2_SOURCES})\n\ntarget_include_directories(pcre2\n    PUBLIC include\n    PRIVATE src\n)\n\ntarget_compile_definitions(pcre2 PRIVATE\n    HAVE_CONFIG_H\n    PCRE2_CODE_UNIT_WIDTH=8\n    SUPPORT_UNICODE\n)\n\ntarget_compile_options(pcre2 PRIVATE -w)\n\n# Output the shared library to the build directory root (expected by the runner)\nset_target_properties(pcre2 PROPERTIES\n    LIBRARY_OUTPUT_DIRECTORY \"${CMAKE_BINARY_DIR}\"\n    PREFIX \"lib\"\n)\n=== config.h ===\n19:macros that are not defined on the command line.\n22:defined (conventionally to 1) for TRUE, and not defined at all for FALSE. All\n24:as MATCH_LIMIT, whose actual value is relevant, have defaults defined, but are\n28:   character or sequence of characters. If BSR_ANYCRLF is defined (to any\n39:   character codes, define this macro to any value. When EBCDIC is set, PCRE2\n40:   assumes that all input strings are in EBCDIC. If you do not define this\n46:/* To force an EBCDIC environment, define this macro to make the core PCRE2\n51:/* In an EBCDIC environment, define this macro to any value to arrange for the\n169:#define HEAP_LIMIT 20000000\n178:#define LINK_SIZE 2\n184:#define LT_OBJDIR \".libs/\"\n195:#define MATCH_LIMIT 10000000\n209:#define MATCH_LIMIT_DEPTH MATCH_LIMIT\n216:#define MAX_NAME_COUNT 10000\n223:#define MAX_NAME_SIZE 128\n229:#define MAX_VARLOOKBEHIND 255\n240:#define NEWLINE_DEFAULT 2\n244:#define PACKAGE \"pcre2\"\n247:#define PACKAGE_BUGREPORT \"\"\n250:#define PACKAGE_NAME \"PCRE2\"\n253:#define PACKAGE_STRING \"PCRE2 10.48-DEV\"\n256:#define PACKAGE_TARNAME \"pcre2\"\n259:#define PACKAGE_URL \"\"\n262:#define PACKAGE_VERSION \"10.48-DEV\"\n268:#define PARENS_NE