e EXACT error constant (e.g. `PCRE2_ERROR_BADDATA`, `PCRE2_ERROR_NULL`,\n  `PCRE2_ERROR_NOMEMORY`, `PCRE2_ERROR_UTF8_ERR5`, `NULL` return, `-1`), not just\n  \"both < 0\".\n* Where a row's trigger also produces output (e.g. `*erroroffset`, `*blength`,\n  `pcre2_get_error_message` text), compare those too.\n* Cover in addition, even where ERRORS.md has no row, the generic boundaries:\n  - NULL pointers for every pointer parameter of every public function that checks\n    them (read the C to see which are checked; do NOT pass NULL where the C would\n    dereference it unconditionally — that is undefined behaviour and would crash both\n    libraries identically for no information).\n  - zero and oversized lengths (`PCRE2_ZERO_TERMINATED`, huge `PCRE2_SIZE` values\n    that the C rejects, ovector count 0, buffer length 0/1).\n  - values one step past every documented range.\n  - **out-of-range enum values across the FFI boundary**: `pcre2_config` with\n    `what` = 0..40 and 0xffffffff; `pcre2_pattern_info` with `what` = 0..40 and\n    0xffffffff; `pcre2_set_newline` 0..10; `pcre2_set_bsr` 0..5;\n    `pcre2_set_optimize` 0..80 and 0xffffffff; `pcre2_set_glob_escape` /\n    `pcre2_set_glob_separator` with every byte 0..=255 plus large values;\n    `pcre2_get_error_message` with codes -100..300 (compare the full message text,\n    the return value, and behaviour with buffer sizes 0, 1, exact length, and\n    length-1 — read `pcre2_error.c` for the truncation rule);\n    every `pcre2_compile` option bit that is NOT in `PUBLIC_COMPILE_OPTIONS`\n    (one test per undefined bit, expecting `PCRE2_ERROR_BADOPTION`), same for\n    extra options, match options, DFA match options, substitute options, convert\n    options, and `pcre2_jit_compile` options.\n* For `pcre2_substitute` error rows you need a compiled code + match data; build them\n  in each library independently (never pass a C-created object to the Rust library).\n* For rows marked \"(hard to reach from FFI)\" in ERRORS